window.__labSearchIndex={"built":"2026-11-25","fields":["feature","page","kind","heading","url","text"],"e":[["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Visual page","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","mcp/calculator.html","mcp · visual page Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent Enter an AED order and a rate. See the amount the customer pays, rounded up. Then refund it in parts and see how PGW converts each refund, why partial refunds round down, and how the final refund closes the gap. Illustrative Reflects solution requirements v3.0 and PGW stories v0.1 (25-Nov-2026) Read the requirement → Stories: S4 section 2 → S6 → HPP simulator End-to-end view Back to MCP Terms. Order currency : what the merchant priced in (AED). Transaction currency : what the customer pays in and what the scheme clears in. Minor unit : the smallest amount of a currency (GBP 0.01). Rate : AED → transaction currency, 7 decimals, from the Visa section of Planet's file, markup included. Rates on this page are dummy. Field names are from the PGW stories. Try AED 100 → GBP AED 99.99, rounded up AED 0.01 INR Refund 60 + 40 Refund in thirds Full refund Refund below AED 0.10 Refund too much Newer rate file Why round down 1"],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Visual page","Order and rate","mcp/calculator.html#order-and-rate","S4 section 2 Order amount (AED) Transaction currency GBP EUR INR USD SAR JPY MVP currencies have 2 decimals. JPY is Phase 2. Rate: 1 AED = … (7 decimals) Filled from the dummy Visa rate when you pick a currency. Change it to test other rates. 4"],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Visual page","Minimum refund (existing rule)","mcp/calculator.html#minimum-refund-existing-rule","S6 check 1.2 MCP adds no minimum of its own. The existing minimum refund amount (AED 0.10) applies, as for any refund. It is enough for MCP: AED 0.10 converts to at least one minor unit in every MVP currency, because each has a rate of 0.1 or more per AED. Existing minimum refund: AED 0.10 AED 0.10 × 0.2137000 = 0.02137 → down = 0.02 GBP at least one minor unit Currency Dummy rate AED 0.10 converts to GBP 0.2137000 0.02 EUR 0.2489000 0.02 INR 23.1200000 2.31 USD 0.2759000 0.02 SAR 1.0345000 0.10 Decided 25-Nov-2026. A refund below AED 0.10 gets the existing refund message. 2"],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Visual page","The quote the customer pays","mcp/calculator.html#the-quote-the-customer-pays","S4 section 2 · S5 section 3 Order (mcpBaseAmount) 100.00 AED What the merchant priced and sees. AED × rate, exact 21.37 GBP 100.00 × 0.2137000 Quote (amount) 21.37 GBP Exact. Nothing to round. HPP shows: GBP 21.37 Order amount AED 100.00 Exchange rate 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP Stored: mcpRate 0.2137000 Rule. Order amount × rate, rounded up to the currency's decimals (decided 24-Nov). The quote is fixed for the HPP session: a newer rate file does not change it. 3"],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Visual page","Refunds in AED, sent in the transaction currency","mcp/calculator.html#refunds-in-aed-sent-in-the-transaction-currency","S6 section 1 · section 2 Refund amount (AED) Refund Refund the rest Clear refunds # Refund AED (mcpBaseAmount) Checks Conversion Sent GBP (amount) Refunded so far P 100.00 purchase 100.00 × 0.2137000 = 21.37 → up 21.37 — No refunds yet. Enter an AED amount, or use a Try preset. AED: what the merchant refunds AED 100.00 left 100.00 GBP: what goes back to the card GBP 21.37 left 21.37 open Left to refund: AED 100.00 · GBP 21.37. The next refund of AED 100.00 is the final one. A newer rate file has loaded since the purchase (GBP 0.2141000 for the same pair) Compare: what if partial refunds were rounded to the nearest minor unit instead of down? Rule. Non-final refund: refund AED × purchase mcpRate , rounded down . Final refund (AED refunded reaches AED paid): purchase amount − all earlier refunds, in the transaction currency (last-cent rule). Never a new rate."],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: AED 100 → GBP","mcp/calculator.html#try=gb",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: AED 99.99, rounded up","mcp/calculator.html#try=round-up",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: AED 0.01","mcp/calculator.html#try=tiny",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: INR","mcp/calculator.html#try=inr",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Refund 60 + 40","mcp/calculator.html#try=refund-60-40",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Refund in thirds","mcp/calculator.html#try=thirds",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Full refund","mcp/calculator.html#try=full",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Refund below AED 0.10","mcp/calculator.html#try=min",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Refund too much","mcp/calculator.html#try=over",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Newer rate file","mcp/calculator.html#try=newer-rate",""],["MCP","Calculator: the quote, refunds and the last cent","Scenario","Try it: Why round down","mcp/calculator.html#try=nearest-fails",""],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","1. Objective","mcp/docs/requirements.html","v3.0 25-Nov-2026 Source: MCP - Solution Requirements v3.0 (25-Nov-2026).docx Version 3.0 · 25-Nov-2026 · Prepared by Ghulam Rabbani (Product) 1. Objective A customer on Geidea’s hosted payment page (HPP) is offered the price in the currency of the country they are in, and can pay in that currency. The merchant keeps pricing, reporting and settlement in its own order currency (AED). Geidea earns an FX markup on every converted payment. Planet Payment provides the rates and holds the markup, as it does for POS DCC today. This document sets out what each Geidea system and team must deliver. It is organized by system. The PGW dev stories (MCP – PGW Dev Stories) give the PGW requirements at build level."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","2. How the merchant experiences this","mcp/docs/requirements.html#how-the-merchant-experiences-this","Nothing changes for the merchant. It creates orders in AED, sees AED in every API response, webhook, report and portal screen, and is settled in its settlement currency as today. The merchant is not told that the customer paid in another currency. This is the design boundary that every requirement below respects."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","3. How the customer experiences this","mcp/docs/requirements.html#how-the-customer-experiences-this","HPP simulator The customer opens the payment page from the merchant’s site, an SDK that shows Geidea HPP, or a Pay-by-Link. PGW finds the customer’s country from the IP address. If the merchant offers that country’s currency, the HPP shows the total in that currency, the order amount in AED and the exchange rate. The customer can keep the proposed currency, choose another currency the merchant offers, or go back to AED. Card, Apple Pay, Google Pay and Samsung Pay are paid in the chosen currency. Tabby and Tamara are available in AED only. The confirmation shows the amount paid and the AED order amount. When PGW does not propose a currency (location not found, the country’s currency is not offered, or the customer is in the UAE), the HPP shows AED only, with no currency selector, as today."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","4. The three currencies","mcp/docs/requirements.html#the-three-currencies","End-to-end view Currency What it is Who sees it Order currency AED. What the merchant priced the order in. Merchant, Merchant Portal, merchant reports. APEX main amount and currency fields. Transaction currency The currency the customer pays in. The scheme authorizes and clears in it. APEX calls it the cardholder currency. Customer, PGW, MPGS/CyberSource, Postilion, scheme, Planet. APEX cardholder fields (internal). Never the merchant. Settlement currency What the merchant is paid out in. Not changed by MCP. Merchant (as today). Worked example used throughout: order AED 100.00. The customer is in the UK and pays GBP 21.37 at Planet’s rate AED → GBP 0.2137000 (markup included). The merchant is settled in SAR."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","5. Scope","mcp/docs/requirements.html#scope",""],["MCP","1. Objective › 5. Scope","Document","5.1 In scope","mcp/docs/requirements.html#in-scope","Any AED order paid on Geidea HPP: orders created by API (Create Session), by an SDK that shows Geidea HPP, or by Pay-by-Link. Includes saved-card payments that the customer starts on HPP. Card payments, including Apple Pay, Google Pay and Samsung Pay. Sale ( paymentOperation = Pay ). Full refund and partial refunds, including several partial refunds on one transaction. UAE merchants on Geidea’s ecommerce gateway, on MPGS and CyberSource. Order currency AED at launch. The solution supports other order currencies through configuration, with no code change."],["MCP","1. Objective › 5. Scope","Document","5.2 Out of scope","mcp/docs/requirements.html#out-of-scope","Orders in another currency (merchants with ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY ). They are processed as today, without MCP. Tabby, Tamara and other alternative payment methods. HPP shows “Available in AED only” under them. Flows with no HPP: Direct API where the merchant collects the card details, recurring and merchant-initiated payments. Authorization and capture ( PreAuthorize ), including partial captures. Merchant rebate on the markup. VPN and proxy users. A wrong location is an accepted risk."],["MCP","1. Objective › 5. Scope","Document","5.3 Phase 2","mcp/docs/requirements.html#phase-2","Zero and three-decimal currencies (JPY, KWD, BHD, OMR). They need PGW changes to amount handling, display, rounding and refunds, and enablement on APEX, Postilion and Planet. Their country mappings (JP, KW, BH, OM) stay inactive in MVP. Every interface format in MVP states the number of decimals, so Phase 2 needs no format change."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","6. Solution approach","mcp/docs/requirements.html#solution-approach",""],["MCP","1. Objective › 6. Solution approach","Document","6.1 How it works","mcp/docs/requirements.html#how-it-works","End-to-end view Planet publishes a daily rate file over SFTP. The rates include the markup. PGW loads, checks and caches the file. The merchant creates an AED order. The customer opens HPP . PGW looks up the customer’s IP in the MaxMind GeoIP2 database that PGW holds, and gets the country. PGW maps the country to a currency. If MCP is on for the merchant and the merchant offers that currency, PGW takes the rate from the cached file and shows the converted amount. The rates are fixed for the payment session. The customer pays. PGW authorizes in the chosen currency through MPGS or CyberSource and stores the rate on the transaction. PGW federates the transaction to APEX with the AED order amount in the main fields and the transaction amount, currency and rate in the new cardholder fields (section 8.3). The scheme file reaches Postilion in the transaction currency. Postilion clears in that currency. PGW’s enrichment file gives Postilion the AED view, so the PTLF to APEX matches the federation (section 8.4). APEX prices and pays out the merchant from the AED amount, as today. APEX includes the MCP transactions in the Daily Transaction File (DTF) to Planet , as for DCC. Planet accounts for the markup (section 8.5). A refund is made in AED by the merchant. PGW converts it at the rate stored on the original transaction."],["MCP","1. Objective › 6. Solution approach","Document","6.2 Systems and their roles","mcp/docs/requirements.html#systems-and-their-roles","System Role in MCP Change PGW Configuration, rate file, geolocation, HPP currency offer, payment, refunds, merchant outputs, federation to APEX, enrichment file Main build APEX Holds AED in the main fields and the transaction currency in new cardholder fields; flags MCP; produces the DTF to Planet New fields (parked, section 8.3); MCP rows in the DTF Postilion Clears in the transaction currency as today; builds the PTLF with the AED view from the enrichment file Enrichment processing (parked, section 8.4) MPGS, CyberSource Authorize and clear in the transaction currency No change. Already set up for the full ISO currency list. Merchant Portal Shows what APEX returns: order and settlement currency No change Planet Payment (external) Daily rate file with markup; MCP merchant registration; DTF processing, reports and markup share Existing DCC rails, MCP product type MaxMind (external) GeoIP2 database: IP address to country New subscription (approved) MW, TMS, Direct Debit Backend, DDS, GSDK, Noon, Lean Not involved No change Business functions: Operations (merchant enablement with Planet), FinOps (reporting), Risk & Compliance (scheme position, section 7)."],["MCP","1. Objective › 6. Solution approach","Document","6.3 Design principles","mcp/docs/requirements.html#design-principles","The merchant world stays in AED. No merchant-facing output carries the transaction currency, the rate or an MCP flag. One conversion, at PGW. PGW converts once and stores the result. No downstream system recalculates an amount. Location decides the offer. MCP is offered only when the customer’s location gives a currency the merchant offers. The customer can then switch between the offered currencies and AED. Rates come from a cached file. No rate is fetched during a payment session. Refunds use the original rate. Never a newer rate."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","7. Scheme position and known risks","mcp/docs/requirements.html#scheme-position-and-known-risks","Outside DCC. Visa’s DCC rules apply when the currency is derived from the card (BIN). In MCP the currency comes from the customer’s IP location, the AED amount is shown next to it, and the customer can switch back to AED. The scheme clears in the currency the customer chose. Planet processes and reports these transactions as MCP (DTF Product Indicator 2 , “Shop in Your Currency”), separate from DCC. Double markup (accepted). A customer whose card is in AED may be shown a foreign currency while abroad. Both amounts are shown and the customer can switch to AED. No further disclosure is shown. No rounding drift. Amounts are stored once by PGW and copied downstream. Rate file availability. When no valid rate file is cached, MCP is suspended and HPP shows AED only (section 8.1). For Risk & Compliance to assess: the IP-based offer as outside DCC obligations; the HPP display (section 8.1, HPP)."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","8. Requirements","mcp/docs/requirements.html#requirements",""],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.1 PGW: PGW engineering team","mcp/docs/requirements.html#pgw-pgw-engineering-team","HPP simulator End-to-end view Build-level detail is in the PGW dev stories S1 to S7. Merchant configuration (S1) Setting Level Purpose MCP toggle in PGW Configuration (name to be set by PGW, for example ENABLE_DYNAMIC_MCP ) Per MID, Live and Test Turns MCP on for the merchant MCP currencies Per MID The transaction currencies the merchant offers, chosen from the MCP currency list MCP currency list System Currencies MCP can offer. A currency is listed only if APEX supports it and Planet’s rate file carries it. 2-decimal currencies only in MVP. Set before go-live: see below. Country-to-currency map System ISO country code → currency (GB → GBP, FR → EUR…). Phase 2 countries inactive. MCP order currencies System Order currencies MCP applies to. AED at launch. The MCP toggle must have a name that is clearly different from ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY and ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY_SETTLEMENT , which mean other things. No markup is set in PGW. Markup is held at Planet and is included in the rates. MCP currency list at go-live. Before production, Product gets the latest list of currencies APEX supports, agrees the list with Business and Commercial, and asks the PGW team to configure it. The list is configuration, so later changes need no code change. The PGW integration team switches MCP on only after Operations confirms the merchant is registered with Planet for MCP (section 8.6). Rate file (S2) - Fetch Planet’s daily rate file over SFTP, decrypt it (if Planet confirms PGP encryption, with Geidea’s private key; Planet holds the public key), parse it and store the rates in a PGW table. Layout: Planet MAS template 194 (Visa and Mastercard sections). Until the SFTP feed is live, load Planet’s sample file. - Basic checks only: header and trailer present, record count matches, file not loaded before. Planet guarantees its rates. A file that fails is not loaded, and Operations is alerted. - Quote from the Visa section . Rate direction: units of transaction currency for 1 unit of order currency (AED → GBP 0.2137000). Converted amount = order amount × rate. - Each rate has a validity window (48 hours in Planet’s sample, so daily files overlap). Use the rate from the latest loaded file that is valid at the time of the quote (S4). - If no valid rate exists for a currency, that currency is not offered. If no rate is valid at all, MCP is suspended for all merchants and Operations is alerted (S4). Geolocation (S3) - Fetch the MaxMind GeoIP2 database (CSV) when MaxMind publishes a new release, parse it and store IP networks with their country in a PGW table. - Look up the customer’s IP address in this table before HPP shows the amount (S4). No external call during the session. - No country found: no MCP for the session. The payment is a regular AED payment. HPP (S4) - MCP is offered only when all of these are true: the order currency is an MCP order currency (AED), paymentOperation = Pay , the MCP toggle is on, a valid rate file is cached, the IP gives a country, the country maps to an active currency, the merchant offers that currency, and the file has a valid rate for it. - Then HPP shows: the total in the proposed currency, the order amount in AED and the rate (“1 AED = 0.2137 GBP”), and a currency selector. The selector lists AED and every currency the merchant offers that has a valid rate. - When MCP is not offered, HPP shows AED only, with no selector. A customer in the UAE gets no selector. - The rates are taken once when HPP first loads and are fixed for the session. Switching currency re-prices from these rates. - The converted amount is rounded up to the currency’s minor unit. Example: AED 99.99 × 0.2137000 = GBP 21.367863 → GBP 21.37. - The selector and the amounts are shown above the wallet buttons. Wallet buttons use the currency and amount on screen. - Tabby and Tamara are available only when the selected currency is AED, with “Available in AED only” under them. - The confirmation shows the amount paid and the AED order amount, for example “GBP "],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.2 MPGS and CyberSource: technical integration team","mcp/docs/requirements.html#mpgs-and-cybersource-technical-integration-team","No change. PGW sends the transaction currency and amount as for any non-AED payment. MPGS and CyberSource are already set up for the full list of ISO currencies."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.3 APEX: APEX team — parked","mcp/docs/requirements.html#apex-team-parked","Agreed approach (APEX team, 23-Nov-2026). The exact field names and formats are awaited from APEX. The PGW federation story (S8) waits on them. Field Today For an MCP transaction amount Transaction amount Order amount (AED 100.00) transactionCurrency Transaction currency Order currency (AED) settlementAmount , settlementCurrency , exchangeRate Settlement view No change Cardholder Amount (new) — Transaction amount (21.37) Cardholder Currency (new) — Transaction currency (GBP) Transaction Identifier (new) — Y for MCP Cardholder ConvRate (new) — Rate order → transaction currency (0.2137000) Required outcomes - The same fields come from the PGW federation and from the Postilion PTLF, so the two records match. - Refunds carry the same fields: the refund’s converted amount and the original rate. - Chargebacks arrive in the transaction currency. APEX matches them to the original by transaction reference (ARN or RRN), not by amount and currency, and uses the cardholder fields to apply them in AED. Partial chargebacks must never total more than the original AED amount. - A transaction flagged MCP in the PGW federation whose PTLF row does not carry the MCP fields, or the reverse, goes to an exception visible to Operations daily. - Merchant pricing, payout, refunds, merchant APIs and the Merchant Portal continue on the AED fields with no change. - DTF to Planet. APEX produces the DTF, as for DCC. MCP transactions (purchases and refunds) are included with field 22 Product Indicator = 2 and field 20 = the applied rate as a decimal, subject to Planet’s confirmation (section 8.5). Required to be confirmed - Field keys for the API and the PTLF; currency format (alpha GBP or numeric 826 ); amount format and decimals; rate decimals (Planet uses 7); value of the identifier for non-MCP transactions. - Rounding for partial chargebacks (AED = transaction amount ÷ rate). - Exception handling for MCP mismatches."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.4 Postilion: Postilion team — parked","mcp/docs/requirements.html#postilion-team-parked","The enrichment file format and its data set are being finalized. The PGW enrichment story (S9) waits on this. Required outcomes - Clearing is unchanged: Postilion receives the DCF/TC33 in the transaction currency and clears in it. - For each MCP leg (purchase, refund, partial refund), PGW sends an enrichment record. Approach under discussion: reuse Postilion’s existing enrichment-file processing for PayGlocal transactions, with PGW supplying (a) the matching key (PGW order ID, RRN, authorization code), (b) the order view (AED amount and currency) and the transaction view (amount and currency), (c) the rate and the MCP flag. - Postilion builds the PTLF row for APEX with the order view in amount / transactionCurrency and the transaction view and rate in the new cardholder fields, copied with no recalculation. - Non-MCP ecommerce, POS, and POS DCC with Planet are unchanged. Required to be confirmed - The enrichment layout (columns, positions, decimals), and that MCP records are processed before the matching DCF/TC33. - Matching on PGW order ID + RRN + authorization code for MPGS-routed transactions as well as CyberSource."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.5 Planet Payment: Jose Albarran Sierra","mcp/docs/requirements.html#planet-payment-jose-albarran-sierra","# Item Status 1 Daily rate file (template 194) over SFTP: connection, folder, whether the file is PGP-encrypted (if so, Geidea shares its public key), file naming, publishing time Asked 13-Nov 2 Rate validity: confirm the 48-hour window, and that the latest file applies where two files are valid Asked 13-Nov 3 Rate file covers every currency pair Geidea offers Asked 13-Nov 4 DTF v1.10 for MCP rows: field 22 Product Indicator = 2 ; field 20 = applied rate as a decimal; card number and markup fields Asked 13-Nov 5 Merchant registration: existing bulk load file with field 47 Product Type = MCP , same acquirer set-up as DCC Confirmed 13-Nov 6 Markup per currency pair held at Planet; Planet guarantees the rate Confirmed APEX produces the DTF and includes the MCP rows (section 8.3)."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.6 Operations: owner to confirm","mcp/docs/requirements.html#operations-owner-to-confirm","Merchant enablement with Planet. For each merchant approved for MCP, register the merchant with Planet through the existing DCC enablement process (bulk load file, field 47 Product Type = MCP ). The department that runs this process for DCC is to be identified and to agree to run it for MCP. PGW enablement. After Planet confirms, ask the PGW integration team to switch MCP on and set the merchant’s MCP currencies. Act on alerts when a rate file fails or MCP is suspended. Markup changes for a merchant go through Planet and take effect from the rate file."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.7 Merchant Portal: Merchant Portal team","mcp/docs/requirements.html#merchant-portal-team","No change. The portal shows what APEX returns: order currency and settlement currency. To validate in UAT with an MCP transaction."],["MCP","1. Objective › 8. Requirements","Document","8.8 Reporting: Operations & Finance to provide","mcp/docs/requirements.html#reporting-operations-finance-to-provide","Merchant reports need no change. Internal reporting is defined by Operations & Finance (FinOps), then built by APEX. Areas: MCP activity (both currencies, rate, flag), markup revenue from Planet’s reports, Planet invoice reconciliation, scheme funding in the transaction currency, refunds and chargebacks with both currencies, exceptions (MCP mismatches, rate file failures)."],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","9. End-to-end flow","mcp/docs/requirements.html#end-to-end-flow","End-to-end view: purchase and refunds Daily Planet -> PGW Rate file (template 194, markup included). PGW checks and caches it. Purchase: order AED 100.00, customer in the UK pays GBP 21.37, merchant settled in SAR Merchant -> PGW Create Session, AED 100.00 Customer -> HPP Opens the payment page PGW IP -> MaxMind -> GB -> GBP; GBP on for the merchant; rate 0.2137000 (Visa section) HPP -> Customer GBP 21.37, AED 100.00, 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP, currency selector Customer -> HPP Pays in GBP (card or wallet) PGW -> MPGS/CYBS Authorize GBP 21.37 -> approved PGW -> Merchant Callback: AED 100.00 PGW -> APEX Federation: AED 100.00 in main fields; GBP 21.37, rate, MCP flag in cardholder fields PGW -> Postilion Enrichment record (day end) Scheme -> Postilion DCF/TC33 in GBP 21.37; Postilion clears in GBP Postilion -> APEX PTLF: same convention as the federation APEX Prices on AED 100.00, pays the merchant in SAR APEX -> Planet DTF with the MCP row (Product Indicator 2) Refund: merchant refunds AED 60.00, then AED 40.00 Merchant -> PGW Refund AED 60.00 -> PGW refunds GBP 12.82 (stored rate, rounded down) Merchant -> PGW Refund AED 40.00 -> PGW refunds GBP 8.55 (last-cent rule) PGW -> APEX Each refund federated in AED, with its GBP amount and the original rate"],["MCP","1. Objective","Document","10. Open items","mcp/docs/requirements.html#open-items","# Item Section Team Owner 1 APEX field keys and formats for the four cardholder fields; partial-chargeback rounding; MCP mismatch exception; MCP rows in the DTF 8.3 APEX APEX team 2 Enrichment file layout and data set; processing before the DCF/TC33; MPGS matching 8.4 Postilion, PGW Postilion team, Ghulam Rabbani 3 Rate file SFTP delivery, PGP encryption and key exchange, validity, currency coverage; DTF fields for MCP 8.5 Planet Jose Albarran Sierra 4 Department that runs merchant enablement with Planet for DCC, and its agreement to do it for MCP 8.6 Operations To identify 5 Final name of the MCP toggle 8.1 PGW PGW engineering team 6 Internal MCP reporting requirements 8.8 Operations & Finance FinOps 7 Phase 2: 0 and 3-decimal currencies on PGW, APEX, Postilion and Planet 5.3 All —"],["MCP","Story map","Document","Story map","mcp/docs/stories.html","v0.1 25-Nov-2026 Source: MCP - PGW Dev Stories v0.1 (25-Nov-2026).docx Version 0.1 draft · 25-Nov-2026 · Prepared by Ghulam Rabbani (Product) Team: PGW engineering Reference: MCP – Solution Requirements v3.0 (25-Nov-2026) These stories are the requirement. Each story can be read alone. A story refers to another story only for work that must be built first. Story map # Story What it delivers Depends on Status S1 FE/BE – MCP configuration MCP toggle and currency list per MID in PGW configuration. System lists: MCP currencies, country-to-currency map, MCP order currencies. — Written S2 BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store PGW fetches Planet’s daily rate file, decrypts it, parses it and stores the rates in a table. — Written. Build on Planet’s sample file until SFTP is live (P3). S3 BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store PGW fetches the MaxMind GeoIP2 database, parses it and stores IP networks with their country in a table. P2 Written S4 FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection Country and rate lookups. HPP proposes the customer’s currency, shows both amounts and the rate, lets the customer switch. APMs AED only. MCP suspended when no rate is valid. S1, S2, S3 Written S5 BE – MCP payment and transaction record Payment in the chosen currency. MCP fields on the order and transaction. Wallet check. Order totals. S4 Written S6 BE – MCP refunds Refund in AED converted at the stored rate. Last-cent rule. S5 Written S7 BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED Callback, order inquiry, pay and refund responses, Pay-by-Link inquiry show AED only. S5 Written S8 BE – Federation to APEX MCP fields in createTransaction. S5, P4 Parked: waiting on APEX field names S9 BE – Enrichment file to Postilion MCP records in the enrichment file. S5, P5 Parked: waiting on the file format Build order: S1, S2 and S3 in parallel → S4 → S5 → S6, S7. S8 after P4. S9 after P5."],["MCP","Story map","Document","Prerequisites (not PGW work)","mcp/docs/stories.html#prerequisites-not-pgw-work","# Item Needed for Owner P1 The merchant is registered with Planet for MCP (bulk load file, field 47 Product Type = MCP ). Operations confirms before the PGW team switches MCP on. Before a MID is set up (S1) Operations (department to identify) P2 MaxMind GeoIP2 subscription (monthly first) and evaluation of the IP database. S3 Ghulam Rabbani, PGW engineering P3 Planet rate file delivery: SFTP connection, folder, file name, publishing time, and whether the file is PGP-encrypted (if so, key exchange). S2 (live feed) Planet (Jose Albarran Sierra), PGW P4 APEX field names and formats for the cardholder fields. S8 APEX team P5 Enrichment file format and data set for MCP. S9 Ghulam Rabbani with the Postilion team P6 MCP currency list for production: latest APEX-supported list, agreed with Business and Commercial, given to the PGW team to configure. S1 (go-live) Ghulam Rabbani"],["MCP","Story map","Document","Rules for every story","mcp/docs/stories.html#rules-for-every-story","Terms. Order currency = the currency the merchant created the order in (AED). Transaction currency = the currency the customer pays in; the scheme authorizes and clears in it. Rate = Planet’s rate from the order currency to the transaction currency, markup included. MCP transaction = a transaction where PGW converted the amount. Field names. PGW field names are camelCase . New names in these stories are proposals, except mcpBaseAmount and mcpBaseCurrency (agreed). PGW engineering can rename them. Keep the meaning. The PGW backend applies every rule, also when the screen already blocks the action. Identify the merchant by MID in every API and in all documentation. New fields in merchant APIs are additions. Do not change or remove existing fields. Times are UAE time (UTC+4). Rate validity times in Planet’s file are UTC. Amounts. Calculate with exact decimals, never floating point. Every amount is stored with the number of decimals of its currency (2 in MVP). The merchant never sees the transaction currency, the rate or an MCP flag (S7)."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","mcp/docs/stories.html#s1-febe-mcp-configuration","Simulator: merchant set-up"],["MCP","Story map › S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background","The PGW integration team sets merchant settings in PGW Configuration. The settings are stored on the MID’s PAYMENT_GATEWAY product instance, in its data object. The screen saves with the existing product instance update ( PATCH /product/api/v1/productInstance/{productInstanceId} , JSON-Patch replace on data/<key> ). Live and Test instances are separate. The Gateway Settings tab already has ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY ( isMulticurrencyEnabled , currencies ). That setting lets a merchant create orders in other currencies. MCP is a different setting: it lets the customer pay in another currency. The two must stay separate."],["MCP","Story map › S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal","The PGW integration team can turn MCP on for a MID and choose the currencies the merchant offers. PGW holds three system lists that MCP reads: MCP currencies, the country-to-currency map and MCP order currencies."],["MCP","Story map › S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary","Item Value Story ID S1 Users PGW integration team (PGW Configuration) Fields written isDynamicMcpEnabled , dynamicMcpCurrencies Save Existing product instance update Depends on — . Before a MID is set up: P1. Followed by S4 Out of scope Markup (held at Planet). Merchant portal login (no access)."],["MCP","Story map › S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Settings in data (Live and Test separately)","mcp/docs/stories.html#settings-in-data-live-and-test-separately","Field Type Default Values isDynamicMcpEnabled Boolean false true = MCP on for this MID dynamicMcpCurrencies Array of String [] ISO 4217 alpha codes, each from the MCP currency list (section 2) Existing MIDs: add both fields with the defaults. The existing product instance search returns the fields. The existing update accepts them."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. System lists (configuration, not per MID)","mcp/docs/stories.html#system-lists-configuration-not-per-mid","Store as configuration. Do not write the values in code. List Content Initial value MCP currency list Currencies MCP can offer: currency code, numeric code, decimals, active 2-decimal currencies that APEX supports and Planet’s file carries. For build and test: GBP, EUR, INR, USD, SAR. Production list from P6. Country-to-currency map ISO 3166 alpha-2 country → currency code, active flag From the Feature Brief: GB → GBP, US → USD, SA → SAR, QA → QAR, IN → INR, CN → CNY, RU → RUB, CH → CHF, AU → AUD, CA → CAD, SG → SGD, Eurozone countries → EUR. JP, KW, BH, OM inactive (Phase 2). MCP order currencies Order currencies MCP applies to AED"],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Screen","mcp/docs/stories.html#screen","Add the section Dynamic multi-currency pricing in PGW Configuration (tab position: PGW engineering, next to Gateway Settings). Toggle with label Dynamic multi-currency pricing and one line of text. Use a label that is clearly different from ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY and ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY_SETTLEMENT . Ship the label translated (not as a raw key). Under the toggle: a table with one row per active currency in the MCP currency list: currency code, decimals, an Offered toggle. When MCP is off, the currency table is disabled. The selected currencies stay stored. A note under the table: “No markup is set here. Markup is held at Planet and is included in the rates.” Discard Changes and Save changes work as on the other tabs."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Checks on Save changes","mcp/docs/stories.html#checks-on-save-changes","# Check Message 4.1 MCP on → at least one currency offered. Select at least one currency. 4.2 Each currency is in the MCP currency list and active. {code} is not available for MCP. Any failure: do not save. Show the message and the banner “Changes not saved. Fix the highlighted fields.” No failure: save the changed fields."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Effect of a saved change","mcp/docs/stories.html#effect-of-a-saved-change","Change Effect MCP turned on Applies to HPP sessions opened after the save. MCP turned off, or a currency removed New HPP sessions do not offer it. Payments already made and their refunds keep their stored rate (S6)."],["MCP","Story map › S1 — FE/BE – MCP configuration","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria","New MID: MCP off, no currencies. Turn MCP on, save with no currency: message 4.1. Turn MCP on, offer GBP and EUR, save, reload: values shown. Turn MCP off, save, reload: MCP off, GBP and EUR still selected and disabled. Change on Test: Live does not change. Remove INR from the MCP currency list in configuration: INR is not shown on the screen and a save with INR is rejected (4.2)."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","mcp/docs/stories.html#s2-be-planet-rate-file-fetch-parse-and-store","Simulator: yesterday's rates Simulator: no valid file End-to-end: no valid file"],["MCP","Story map › S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-1","Planet publishes one rate file each day. The rates include the markup. This story only brings the file into PGW: fetch it, decrypt it, parse it and store the rates in a table. S4 reads the table when HPP loads. Layout: Planet MAS template 194, comma-separated, with a Visa section and a Mastercard section. Planet’s sample (USD base; Geidea’s file will have AED as the base currency): PFH,20260214,01 VILFH,HPLANET VISA,20260214,01 VID,1023,$,840,2,€,978,2,0.9123456,2026-02-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-02-15T23:59:59.000Z VID,1024,$,840,2,£,826,2,0.7890123,2026-02-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-02-15T23:59:59.000Z VILFT,TPLANET VISA,1804,1.7013579,2 MCLFH,HPLANET MASTERCARD,20260214,01 MCD,1025,$,840,2,€,978,2,0.9121000,2026-02-14T00:00:00.000Z,2026-02-15T23:59:59.000Z MCLFT,TPLANET MASTERCARD,978,0.9121000,1 PFT,TXN RATES,2782,2.6134579,3"],["MCP","Story map › S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-1","Each day’s rates are in the PGW rate table, one row per rate."],["MCP","Story map › S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-1","Item Value Story ID S2 Source Planet, SFTP, once a day Table written mcp_rate (name is a proposal) Depends on P3 for the live feed. Until then, load Planet’s sample file. Followed by S4 Out of scope Rate lookup and MCP suspension (S4). Refunds use the rate stored on the transaction, not this table (S6)."],["MCP","Story map › S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-1",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Fetch","mcp/docs/stories.html#fetch","Collect the file from Planet’s SFTP folder once a day, after Planet’s publishing time (P3). Retry until a set time (configuration). Alert Operations when no file has arrived by then. Encryption. Planet is to confirm whether the file is PGP-encrypted (P3). If it is: Geidea creates a PGP key pair for PGW and gives Planet the public key. Planet encrypts with it. PGW decrypts with the private key. Keep the private key in PGW’s secrets store, never in code or configuration files. Keep the received file as it is, for audit."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Basic checks","mcp/docs/stories.html#basic-checks","# Check 2.1 The first record is PFH and the last record is PFT . 2.2 PFT recordCount = the number of detail records ( VID + MCD ). 2.3 The file date and version have not been loaded before. Any failure: do not load the file. Keep the rows already in the table. Alert Operations with the file name and the failed check. Why only basic checks. Planet guarantees its rates and pays any difference. The checks only make sure the whole file arrived and is not loaded twice."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Parse: what to keep and what to drop","mcp/docs/stories.html#parse-what-to-keep-and-what-to-drop","Records Record Code Action Physical file header PFH Take date and version onto every row. Do not store the record. Section header VILFH , MCLFH Take the card network ( VISA or MASTERCARD ) onto the rows of the section. Do not store the record. Detail record VID , MCD Store one row each (section 4). Section trailer VILFT , MCLFT Drop. Physical file trailer PFT Use for check 2.2. Do not store. Fields of a detail record (in file order) # Field Keep or drop Reason 1 rateId Keep Planet’s ID of the rate. Stored on each MCP transaction. 2 baseCurr Drop Currency symbol (e.g. $ ). Display only. 3 baseCurr2 Keep ISO numeric code of the base (order) currency. 4 baseMinorUnit Keep Decimals of the base currency. 5 targetCurr Drop Currency symbol. Display only. 6 targetCurr2 Keep ISO numeric code of the target (transaction) currency. 7 targetMinorUnit Keep Decimals of the target currency. 8 rate Keep The rate, markup included. 9 validFrom Keep Start of validity (UTC). 10 validTo Keep End of validity (UTC)."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Table mcp_rate","mcp/docs/stories.html#table-mcp_rate","One row per detail record. Example: the Geidea file of 24-Nov-2026, Visa row for GBP. Column Type Value Example rateFileDate Date PFH date 2026-11-24 rateFileVersion String PFH version 01 cardNetwork String VISA for VID rows, MASTERCARD for MCD rows VISA rateId String rateId 2001 baseCurrency String (3) ISO alpha code of baseCurr2 AED (from 784) baseMinorUnit Integer baseMinorUnit 2 targetCurrency String (3) ISO alpha code of targetCurr2 GBP (from 826) targetMinorUnit Integer targetMinorUnit 2 rate Decimal (7 decimals) rate , exactly as in the file. Meaning: 1 unit of baseCurrency = rate units of targetCurrency , markup included. 0.2137000 (1 AED = 0.2137 GBP) validFrom Timestamp (UTC) validFrom 2026-11-24 00:00:00 validTo Timestamp (UTC) validTo 2026-11-25 23:59:59 loadedAt Timestamp When PGW loaded the file 2026-11-24 04:10 UAE Store both sections. S4 quotes from VISA rows only. Keeping the Mastercard rows lets Geidea switch later by configuration. Do not delete the rows of earlier files. Each daily file overlaps the next (48-hour validity in Planet’s sample). Rows older than the retention period (configuration) can be removed."],["MCP","Story map › S2 — BE – Planet rate file: fetch, parse and store","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-1","Load Planet’s sample file: 3 rows. Row rateId 1024: VISA , USD → GBP, 0.7890123, valid 14-Feb 00:00 to 15-Feb 23:59:59 UTC. No currency symbols are stored. Change the PFT record count to 4: the file is not loaded (2.2). Operations is alerted. Earlier rows stay. Load the same file twice: the second load is rejected (2.3). When P3 confirms PGP: an encrypted file is decrypted with the private key and loaded."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","mcp/docs/stories.html#s3-be-maxmind-database-fetch-parse-and-store","Simulator: no country found Simulator: customer in the UAE"],["MCP","Story map › S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-2","MCP proposes a currency from the customer’s country. PGW finds the country from the customer’s IP address with the MaxMind GeoIP2 database (approved 23-Nov-2026). MaxMind publishes the database as a zip file of CSV files. This story only brings it into PGW: fetch it, parse it and store it in a table. S4 looks up the IP address when HPP loads."],["MCP","Story map › S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-2","The latest MaxMind data is in the PGW geolocation table."],["MCP","Story map › S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-2","Item Value Story ID S3 Source MaxMind download permalink from the MaxMind account portal, for example https://download.maxmind.com/geoip/databases/GeoIP2-Country-CSV/download?suffix=zip . Basic authentication with the MaxMind account ID and licence key. Table written mcp_geoip_network (name is a proposal) Depends on P2 Followed by S4 Out of scope IP lookup (S4). VPN and proxy detection (accepted risk)."],["MCP","Story map › S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-2",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Fetch","mcp/docs/stories.html#fetch-1","Each day, check the release date with a HEAD request on the permalink (MaxMind’s recommended method). Download only when the release is newer than the one loaded. Keep the account ID and licence key in PGW’s secrets store. Keep the downloaded zip for audit. The zip name carries the release date: GeoIP2-Country-CSV_YYYYMMDD.zip . Download or load failure: keep the current data. Alert Operations."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Files to use","mcp/docs/stories.html#files-to-use","File Use GeoIP2-Country-Blocks-IPv4.csv Load GeoIP2-Country-Blocks-IPv6.csv Load GeoIP2-Country-Locations-en.csv Use to find the country code of each network Other files (other languages, licence, copyright) Do not load If the subscription is the City edition, the file names start with GeoIP2-City . Use the same columns only."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Parse: what to keep and what to drop","mcp/docs/stories.html#parse-what-to-keep-and-what-to-drop-1","Blocks files (IPv4 and IPv6) Column Keep or drop Reason network Keep The IP network in CIDR format, e.g. 81.2.69.0/24 . geoname_id Keep (for the join) Location of the network. Leads to the country code. registered_country_geoname_id Keep (for the join) Country where the ISP registered the network. Used when geoname_id is empty. represented_country_geoname_id Drop Not used for MCP. is_anonymous_proxy , is_satellite_provider , is_anycast Drop Not used for MCP. City edition only: postal_code , latitude , longitude , accuracy_radius Drop Not used for MCP. Locations file Column Keep or drop Reason geoname_id Keep (for the join) Joins to the blocks files. country_iso_code Keep ISO 3166 alpha-2 country code. locale_code , continent_code , continent_name , country_name , is_in_european_union Drop Not used for MCP."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Table mcp_geoip_network","mcp/docs/stories.html#table-mcp_geoip_network","One row per network. The join columns are not stored. Column Type Value Example (illustrative) ipVersion Integer 4 or 6, from the file 4 networkStart IP address First address of network 81.2.69.0 networkEnd IP address Last address of network 81.2.69.255 countryIsoCode String (2) country_iso_code of geoname_id . If geoname_id is empty, of registered_country_geoname_id . Empty if neither has a country. GB databaseDate Date Release date from the zip name 2026-11-24 Load a new release completely before PGW uses it. Until then, S4 uses the previous release. Keep only the release in use and the one before it."],["MCP","Story map › S3 — BE – MaxMind database: fetch, parse and store","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-2","Load a release: one row per network in the two blocks files. No dropped column is stored. A network with an empty geoname_id gets the country of registered_country_geoname_id . The HEAD check finds no newer release: nothing is downloaded. A failed download keeps the current data and alerts Operations. While a new release loads, lookups still use the previous release."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","mcp/docs/stories.html#s4-febe-hpp-currency-offer-and-selection","Simulator: GBP offered Simulator: rounding up Simulator: Tabby End-to-end view"],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-3","The customer pays on Geidea HPP. HPP opens from Create Session ( POST /payment-intent/api/v2/direct/session ), from an SDK that shows Geidea HPP, or from Pay-by-Link. MCP is decided when HPP loads. Flows that never show HPP (Direct API with card details from the merchant, recurring and merchant-initiated payments) are never MCP. MCP is offered strictly on location. When PGW does not propose a currency, HPP is the same as today: AED only, no selector."],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-3","When the customer’s location gives a currency the merchant offers, HPP shows the amount in that currency, the AED amount and the rate. The customer can switch between the offered currencies and AED. The quote stays fixed for the session."],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-3","Item Value Story ID S4 Reads isDynamicMcpEnabled , dynamicMcpCurrencies (S1), system lists (S1), mcp_rate (S2), mcp_geoip_network (S3) Session fields written mcpCountry , mcpProposedCurrency , mcpQuotes[] , isMcpOffered Depends on S1, S2, S3 Followed by S5"],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Flow","mcp/docs/stories.html#flow","The classic MCP path: a UK customer pays an AED 100.00 order in GBP. MCP payment on HPP"],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-3",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Decide the offer (when HPP first loads)","mcp/docs/stories.html#decide-the-offer-when-hpp-first-loads","PGW runs these checks in order. The first “no” stops the check: MCP is not offered and HPP shows AED only, with no selector. # Check Source 1.1 The order currency is in the MCP order currencies list ( AED ). S1 1.2 paymentOperation = Pay . Session 1.3 isDynamicMcpEnabled = true for the MID and instance. S1 1.4 MCP is not suspended (section 2). S2 1.5 The country lookup (section 2) returns a country. S3 1.6 The country maps to an active currency, other than the order currency. S1 1.7 The currency is in dynamicMcpCurrencies of the MID. S1 1.8 The rate lookup (section 2) returns a rate for order currency → that currency. S2 All “yes”: the mapped currency is the proposed currency . Set isMcpOffered = true . Why 1.6 excludes the order currency. A customer in the UAE maps to AED. Nothing is converted, so MCP is not offered and HPP shows no selector."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Lookups","mcp/docs/stories.html#lookups","Country lookup (table from S3) 1. Take the customer’s public IP address as received by HPP, after any Geidea load balancer. 2. Find the row of mcp_geoip_network with the same ipVersion where networkStart ≤ IP ≤ networkEnd . Result: countryIsoCode . 3. No row, an empty countryIsoCode or a private address (e.g. 10.0.0.1): no country. 4. Store the IP address and the country on the session, for support. Rate lookup (table from S2) 1. Take the rows of mcp_rate with cardNetwork = VISA , baseCurrency = order currency, targetCurrency = the currency, and validFrom ≤ now ≤ validTo . 2. Use the row of the latest file (highest rateFileDate , then rateFileVersion ). 3. No row: no rate. The currency is not offered. Example: file 20261123 has GBP valid to 24-Nov 23:59:59 UTC. File 20261124 has GBP valid to 25-Nov 23:59:59 UTC. At 24-Nov 10:00 UTC both are valid. PGW uses 20261124. MCP suspended 1. When mcp_rate has no VISA row valid now, MCP is suspended for all merchants. Every HPP shows AED only. 2. Alert Operations when MCP becomes suspended and when it resumes."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Quotes (fixed for the session)","mcp/docs/stories.html#quotes-fixed-for-the-session","Calculator: rounding up When MCP is offered, build one quote for each currency in dynamicMcpCurrencies that has a rate (section 2), at the time HPP first loads: Quote field Value currency Transaction currency amount Order amount × rate , rounded up to the currency’s decimals rate From the rate lookup (7 decimals) rateId , rateFileDate , rateFileVersion From the rate lookup Store the quotes on the session ( mcpQuotes[] ). A reload of the same session uses the stored quotes. A newer rate file does not change them. Never recalculate an amount from a newer rate during the session. Rounding up, examples (rate AED → GBP 0.2137000): Order amount (AED) × rate Quote (GBP) 100.00 21.3700000 21.37 99.99 21.3678630 21.37 0.01 0.0021370 0.01"],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Display","mcp/docs/stories.html#display","# Element Content 4.1 Total The quote amount and currency of the selected currency (first: the proposed currency), e.g. “GBP 21.37”. 4.2 Order amount “Order amount AED 100.00”. Shown only when the selected currency is not AED. 4.3 Rate “Exchange rate 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP”. The rate as in the file, trailing zeros removed. Shown only when the selected currency is not AED. 4.4 Currency selector Paying in : AED and every currency with a quote. Shown only when MCP is offered. 4.5 Wallet buttons Apple Pay, Google Pay, Samsung Pay built with the selected currency and amount. Shown below 4.1 to 4.4. 4.6 Tabby, Tamara Selectable only when the selected currency is AED. Show “Available in AED only” under them when MCP is offered. 4.7 Pay button “Pay GBP 21.37” (selected currency and amount). Changing the selector updates 4.1 to 4.7 from the stored quotes. AED shows the order amount. When the customer selects a non-AED currency while Tabby or Tamara is selected, select card. No further disclosure text about the conversion."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Backend checks when HPP submits the payment","mcp/docs/stories.html#backend-checks-when-hpp-submits-the-payment","# Check On failure 5.1 The submitted currency is AED or a currency in mcpQuotes[] . Reject. Message: “Currency not available. Reload the page.” 5.2 The submitted amount equals the stored quote (or the order amount for AED). Reject. Same message. 5.3 Tabby or Tamara only with AED. Reject. Message: “This payment method is available in AED only.” PGW engineering sets the error codes."],["MCP","Story map › S4 — FE/BE – HPP currency offer and selection","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-3","MID with MCP on, GBP offered. Customer IP in the UK, order AED 100.00: HPP shows GBP 21.37, AED 100.00, “1 AED = 0.2137 GBP” and the selector. isMcpOffered = true . Same customer selects AED: total AED 100.00, no order amount line, no rate line. Tabby is selectable. Customer in the UAE: AED only, no selector. isMcpOffered = false . Customer in India, INR not offered by the MID: AED only, no selector. Customer in Japan: AED only, no selector (Phase 2 country). No country found: AED only, no selector. MCP suspended (no valid rate file): AED only, no selector. Order in USD, or paymentOperation = PreAuthorize : no MCP. Order AED 99.99, customer in the UK: GBP 21.37. A new rate file loads while the page is open, then the customer reloads: the amount does not change. Two valid rate files: the quote uses the later file. No VISA rate valid now: MCP suspended, AED only, Operations alerted. A customer IP with no matching network: no country, AED only. A tampered submit with GBP 20.00: rejected (5.2). Pay-by-Link opened from the UK: same behaviour as 1."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","mcp/docs/stories.html#s5-be-mcp-payment-and-transaction-record","Order model: after the purchase Simulator: Apple Pay Simulator: wallet mismatch End-to-end view"],["MCP","Story map › S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-4","S4 gives a fixed quote. When the customer pays in a non-AED currency, PGW authorizes in that currency through MPGS or CyberSource, as for any non-AED payment. PGW must keep two views of the payment: the order view in AED, which the merchant and APEX use, and the transaction view in the paid currency, which the scheme uses."],["MCP","Story map › S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-4","PGW authorizes in the currency the customer chose, at the quoted amount. PGW stores both views and the rate on the transaction. Order totals stay in the order currency."],["MCP","Story map › S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-4","Item Value Story ID S5 Geidea endpoints HPP pay flow; POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay , POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token Fields written Order: isMcpOffered . Transaction: isMcp , mcpBaseAmount , mcpBaseCurrency , mcpRate , mcpRateId , mcpRateFileDate , mcpRateFileVersion Depends on S4 Followed by S6, S7, S8, S9"],["MCP","Story map › S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-4",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Authorization","mcp/docs/stories.html#authorization","Send the selected currency and the quote amount to MPGS or CyberSource, as for any non-AED payment. No new processor fields. MPGS and CyberSource are set up for the full ISO currency list. AED selected: process as today. A declined payment can be retried in the same session with the same quote."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Wallet check","mcp/docs/stories.html#wallet-check","For Apple Pay, Google Pay and Samsung Pay, compare the amount and currency in the wallet payment data with the quote of the selected currency. Different: reject the payment. Message: “Payment amount does not match. Try again.” Do not send it to the processor."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Fields","mcp/docs/stories.html#fields","Order | Field | Type | Value | |—|—|—| | amount , currency | Existing | Order amount and currency (AED 100.00). Not changed by MCP. | | isMcpOffered | Boolean | From S4. Internal. Not sent to the merchant. | Transaction (every transaction of the order: purchase and refund) | Field | Type | Value (purchase in the example) | |—|—|—| | amount , currency | Existing | Transaction view: 21.37 GBP | | isMcp | Boolean | true only when a conversion was applied to this transaction | | mcpBaseAmount | Decimal | Order view of this transaction: 100.00. For non-MCP transactions = amount . | | mcpBaseCurrency | String | AED . For non-MCP transactions = currency . | | mcpRate | Decimal (7) | 0.2137000. Empty when isMcp = false . | | mcpRateId , mcpRateFileDate , mcpRateFileVersion | String | From the quote. Empty when isMcp = false . | Why mcpBaseAmount is filled for every transaction. Order totals, the merchant outputs (S7) and the federation (S8) read one field for all transactions. Why the name is not originalAmount . PGW already uses originalAmount for the amount before fees."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Order totals","mcp/docs/stories.html#order-totals","Compute every order total (paid, refunded, remaining to refund) from mcpBaseAmount . Never add amount values of transactions in different currencies. Example: purchase mcpBaseAmount 100.00, refund mcpBaseAmount 60.00 → refunded AED 60.00, remaining AED 40.00."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Confirmation","mcp/docs/stories.html#confirmation","The HPP confirmation shows the paid amount and the AED order amount: “GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00)”. Pay-by-Link: PGW sends the customer an email receipt when the customer has an email address. For an MCP payment it shows the same: “GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00)”. AED payments: as today."],["MCP","Story map › S5 — BE – MCP payment and transaction record","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-4","Pay GBP 21.37 on an AED 100.00 order by card: processor receives GBP 21.37. Transaction: amount 21.37, currency GBP, isMcp true, mcpBaseAmount 100.00, mcpBaseCurrency AED, mcpRate 0.2137000. Pay in AED on an MCP-offered session: isMcp false, mcpBaseAmount 100.00 AED. isMcpOffered true on the order. Apple Pay with GBP 21.37 in the token: approved. Token with GBP 21.36: rejected before the processor. Decline, then retry in the same session: same quote and rate. Order inquiry totals are in AED. Confirmation shows “GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00)”. Pay-by-Link paid in GBP by a customer with an email address: the email receipt shows “GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00)”."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S6 — BE – MCP refunds","mcp/docs/stories.html#s6-be-mcp-refunds","Order model: refunds 60 + 40 Calculator: refunds AED 60 + 40 End-to-end: refunds AED 60 + 40"],["MCP","Story map › S6 — BE – MCP refunds","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-5","The merchant refunds in AED with the existing refund API (refund v2, signed with timestamp + merchantPublicKey + refundAmount + orderId ). For an MCP transaction the customer paid in another currency, so the refund must go to the processor in that currency. PGW converts it at the rate stored on the original transaction. Converting each partial refund on its own can leave a cent unrefunded. The last-cent rule closes the gap at PGW."],["MCP","Story map › S6 — BE – MCP refunds","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-5","A refund of an MCP transaction is sent in the transaction currency at the stored rate. The refunds of a transaction never total more or less than the amount paid, in both currencies."],["MCP","Story map › S6 — BE – MCP refunds","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-5","Item Value Story ID S6 Geidea endpoint Existing refund v2. refundAmount in the order currency. No new request fields. Fields written Refund transaction: amount , currency , isMcp , mcpBaseAmount , mcpBaseCurrency , mcpRate , mcpRateId , mcpRateFileDate , mcpRateFileVersion Depends on S5 Out of scope Manual refunds by FinOps through Postilion. Void (as today)."],["MCP","Story map › S6 — BE – MCP refunds","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-5",""],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Checks","mcp/docs/stories.html#checks","Calculator: refund too much # Check Message 1.1 Existing refund checks, on AED: refundAmount ≤ AED paid − AED already refunded (from mcpBaseAmount ). Existing message 1.2 Existing minimum refund amount (0.10). Existing message Why no MCP-specific minimum. The existing minimum of AED 0.10 always converts to at least one minor unit in every MVP currency, because each of them has a rate of 0.1 or more per AED. Example: AED 0.10 × 0.2137000 = GBP 0.021370 → GBP 0.02."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Conversion (original purchase isMcp = true)","mcp/docs/stories.html#conversion-original-purchase-ismcp-true","Calculator: why round down Final refund: AED already refunded + refundAmount = AED paid. Refund amount in transaction currency = purchase amount − all earlier refunds’ amount . Other refunds: refundAmount × purchase mcpRate , rounded down to the currency’s decimals. Use the purchase mcpRate . Never look up a new rate. Send the refund to the processor in the transaction currency. Store on the refund transaction: amount and currency = converted amount and transaction currency; mcpBaseAmount = refundAmount ; mcpBaseCurrency = AED; isMcp = true ; rate fields copied from the purchase. Original purchase isMcp = false : refund as today. Why round down. Each earlier refund then stays at or below its exact value, so the final refund is never negative."],["MCP","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Examples (purchase AED 100.00 = GBP 21.37, rate 0.2137000)","mcp/docs/stories.html#examples-purchase-aed-100.00-gbp-21.37-rate-0.2137000","Calculator: 60 + 40 Calculator: thirds Refund (AED) Calculation Refund (GBP) 60.00 60.00 × 0.2137000 = 12.822 → round down 12.82 40.00 (final) 21.37 − 12.82 8.55 Total 100.00 21.37 Refund (AED) Calculation Refund (GBP) 33.33 7.122621 → round down 7.12 33.33 7.122621 → round down 7.12 33.34 (final) 21.37 − 7.12 − 7.12 7.13 Total 100.00 21.37"],["MCP","Story map › S6 — BE – MCP refunds","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-5","Refund AED 60.00 then AED 40.00 on the example: processor receives GBP 12.82 then GBP 8.55. Order refunded total AED 100.00. Refund AED 33.33, 33.33, 33.34: GBP 7.12, 7.12, 7.13. Full refund AED 100.00 in one call: GBP 21.37. A new rate file has loaded since the purchase: refund still uses 0.2137000. Refund AED 100.01: rejected (1.1)."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","mcp/docs/stories.html#s7-be-merchant-facing-outputs-in-aed","Order model: merchant sees AED Simulator: after Pay End-to-end view"],["MCP","Story map › S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-6","The merchant must never see the conversion. Existing merchant integrations read transaction.amount and transaction.currency . These fields must stay in the payloads and carry the AED values for MCP transactions, so no merchant integration breaks."],["MCP","Story map › S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","Document","Goal","mcp/docs/stories.html#goal-6","Every merchant-facing output shows an MCP transaction in AED, with no rate and no MCP flag."],["MCP","Story map › S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-6","Item Value Story ID S7 Outputs Callback to callbackUrl ; order inquiry GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order/{orderId} and GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order?MerchantReferenceId= ; pay responses ( /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay , /pay/token ); refund response; Pay-by-Link ( …/v1/direct/eInvoice ) inquiry Depends on S5 Out of scope Merchant Portal (shows APEX data, no change). Setting to send the conversion fields (none)."],["MCP","Story map › S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","Document","Requirements","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-6","For a transaction with isMcp = true , fill amount with mcpBaseAmount and currency with mcpBaseCurrency in every output listed above. This applies to purchases and refunds. Order totals in these outputs come from mcpBaseAmount (S5 section 4). Do not return isMcp , isMcpOffered , mcpRate , mcpRateId , mcpRateFileDate , mcpRateFileVersion , mcpBaseAmount or mcpBaseCurrency . Transactions with isMcp = false : no change. Example (purchase of the example, then refund AED 60.00): \"transactions\": [ { \"type\": \"Pay\", \"amount\": 100.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"status\": \"Success\" }, { \"type\": \"Refund\", \"amount\": 60.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"status\": \"Success\" } ] Field names other than amount and currency are as in today’s payload."],["MCP","Story map › S7 — BE – Merchant-facing outputs in AED","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-6","MCP purchase GBP 21.37 / AED 100.00: callback and order inquiry show 100.00 AED. Refund AED 60.00 (GBP 12.82 to the processor): refund response and inquiry show 60.00 AED. No output contains GBP, the rate or an MCP field. A non-MCP USD order ( ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY ): unchanged."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S8 — BE – Federation to APEX (parked: waiting on P4)","mcp/docs/stories.html#s8-be-federation-to-apex-parked-waiting-on-p4","End-to-end: federation (parked)"],["MCP","Story map › S8 — BE – Federation to APEX (parked: waiting on P4)","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-7","PGW federates each transaction to APEX in real time (createTransaction). APEX agreed (23-Nov-2026) to hold the order view in its main fields and the transaction view in four new cardholder fields. The exact field names and formats are awaited."],["MCP","Story map › S8 — BE – Federation to APEX (parked: waiting on P4)","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-7","Item Value Story ID S8 Depends on S5, P4"],["MCP","Story map › S8 — BE – Federation to APEX (parked: waiting on P4)","Document","Requirements (to complete when P4 is received)","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-to-complete-when-p4-is-received","APEX field PGW source (MCP transaction) amount mcpBaseAmount transactionCurrency mcpBaseCurrency settlementAmount , settlementCurrency , exchangeRate No change Cardholder Amount (name from APEX) amount Cardholder Currency (name from APEX) currency Transaction Identifier (name from APEX) Y when isMcp = true Cardholder ConvRate (name from APEX) mcpRate Purchases and refunds carry the same fields. A refund sends its own converted amount and the purchase rate. Non-MCP transactions: as today. APEX produces the DTF to Planet from these records, as for DCC. No PGW file to Planet."],["MCP","Story map › S8 — BE – Federation to APEX (parked: waiting on P4)","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-7","To be completed when P4 is received."],["MCP","Story map","Document","S9 — BE – Enrichment file to Postilion (parked: waiting on P5)","mcp/docs/stories.html#s9-be-enrichment-file-to-postilion-parked-waiting-on-p5",""],["MCP","Story map › S9 — BE – Enrichment file to Postilion (parked: waiting on P5)","Document","Background","mcp/docs/stories.html#background-8","Postilion builds the PTLF to APEX from the scheme file, which is in the transaction currency. PGW’s enrichment file gives Postilion the AED view of each MCP leg, so the PTLF matches the PGW federation. The format and data set are being agreed with Postilion."],["MCP","Story map › S9 — BE – Enrichment file to Postilion (parked: waiting on P5)","Document","Story summary","mcp/docs/stories.html#story-summary-8","Item Value Story ID S9 Depends on S5, P5"],["MCP","Story map › S9 — BE – Enrichment file to Postilion (parked: waiting on P5)","Document","Requirements (to complete when P5 is received)","mcp/docs/stories.html#requirements-to-complete-when-p5-is-received","One record for each MCP leg (purchase, refund, partial refund) in the existing daily enrichment file. Data to supply: matching key (PGW order ID, RRN, authorization code), order view ( mcpBaseAmount , mcpBaseCurrency ), transaction view ( amount , currency ), mcpRate , MCP flag. Decimals stated for each amount."],["MCP","Story map › S9 — BE – Enrichment file to Postilion (parked: waiting on P5)","Document","Acceptance criteria","mcp/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-8","To be completed when P5 is received."],["MCP","Story map","Document","Open points","mcp/docs/stories.html#open-points","# Point Story Owner / status 1 Final name and position of the MCP toggle and section. S1 PGW engineering 2 Daily deadline for the rate file before Operations is alerted, and row retention period. S2 Rabbani with Operations 3 Planet: SFTP delivery details, rate validity and currency coverage (P3). S2 Planet – asked 13-Nov 4 MaxMind database refresh frequency under the subscription. S3 PGW engineering"],["MCP","End-to-end view","Visual page","End-to-end view","mcp/end-to-end.html","visual · mcp End-to-end view One AED order from the daily rate file to the merchant's payout and refunds, across the customer, the merchant, PGW, Planet, the processor and scheme, Postilion and APEX. Change the settings and the flow redraws. Illustrative Reflects solution requirements v3.0 and PGW stories v0.1 (25-Nov-2026) Read the requirement → Stories → HPP simulator → Terms: order currency = AED, what the merchant priced in; transaction currency = what the customer pays in (APEX: cardholder currency). Rates are dummy values. Field names are the stories' proposals. Steps marked parked wait on APEX field names (S8) and the Postilion enrichment format (S9). Customer location UK (GBP offered) UAE / not found / not offered Rate file Valid No valid file Customer pays in GBP (proposed) Switches to AED Method Card Apple Pay Tabby Refund None AED 60 + AED 40 Reset"],["MCP","End-to-end view","Visual page","From the rate file to payout","mcp/end-to-end.html#from-the-rate-file-to-payout","Order AED 100.00 · rate AED → GBP 0.2137000 (dummy) · merchant settled in SAR The customer in the UK pays GBP 21.37 for an AED 100.00 order. The merchant sees AED throughout and is paid out in SAR. Action by the customer or merchant Processing Money moves or is converted Parked or open Failed MCP not applied Daily rates HPP offer Payment Federation and clearing Settlement Customer Merchant PGW / HPP Planet MPGS / CYBS · scheme Postilion APEX 01 Publishes the rate file Template 194, markup included 02 Checks and caches it S2 03 Creates the order AED 100.00 04 Opens the payment page From the site, SDK or Pay-by-Link 05 IP → GB → GBP MaxMind database in PGW · S3 06 Offers GBP 21.37 Rounded up · quote fixed · S4 07 Sees GBP 21.37 and AED 100.00 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP · selector 08 Pays GBP 21.37 by card 09 Checks amount = quote S4, S5 10 Authorizes GBP 21.37 Approved 11 Stores both views Order view, paid view, rate · S5 12 Confirmation GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00) 13 Callback: AED 100.00 No rate, no flag · S7 14 Federation: AED + cardholder fields Parked: field names from APEX · S8 15 Enrichment record Parked: file format · S9 16 Clears GBP 21.37 Scheme file in the paid currency 17 PTLF to APEX Same convention as the federation (parked) 18 DTF with the MCP row From APEX · Product Indicator 2 19 Pays the merchant From AED 100.00, in SAR Scroll sideways to see the whole flow → 01 Planet Publishes the rate file Template 194, markup included 02 PGW / HPP Checks and caches it S2 03 Merchant Creates the order AED 100.00 04 Customer Opens the payment page From the site, SDK or Pay-by-Link 05 PGW / HPP IP → GB → GBP MaxMind database in PGW · S3 06 PGW / HPP Offers GBP 21.37 Rounded up · quote fixed · S4 07 Customer Sees GBP 21.37 and AED 100.00 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP · selector 08 Customer Pays GBP 21.37 by card 09 PGW / HPP Checks amount = quote S4, S5 10 MPGS / CYBS · scheme Authorizes GBP 21.37 Approved 11 PGW / HPP Stores both views Order view, paid view, rate · S5 12 Customer Confirmation GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00) 13 Merchant Callback: AED 100.00 No rate, no flag · S7 14 APEX Federation: AED + cardholder fields Parked: field names from APEX · S8 15 Postilion Enrichment record Parked: file format · S9 16 Postilion Clears GBP 21.37 Scheme file in the paid currency 17 APEX PTLF to APEX Same convention as the federation (parked) 18 Planet DTF with the MCP row From APEX · Product Indicator 2 19 APEX Pays the merchant From AED 100.00, in SAR ← Previous Next step → Step 1 of 19"],["MCP","End-to-end view › From the rate file to payout","Visual page","1. Publishes the rate file","mcp/end-to-end.html#aDetail","Planet → PGW · SFTP, PGP Planet publishes one rate file each day over SFTP. Each rate is from AED to one currency, with the markup already in it, and is valid for 48 hours in Planet's sample, so two daily files overlap. Visa section (VID) and Mastercard section (MCD) Delivery details (folder, keys, file name, time) are still with Planet Simulator: the rate file Dummy row in Planet's layout { \"file\" : \"PFH,20261124,01\", \"visaRow\" : \"VID,2001,AED,784,2,GBP,826,2,0.2137000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z\" }"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","mcp/hpp-simulator.html","mcp · visual page HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees Set up the merchant, place the customer somewhere in the world and choose the rate-file state. The HPP on the right reacts as PGW would. Pay to see what PGW stores and what the merchant sees. Illustrative Reflects solution requirements v3.0 and PGW stories v0.1 (25-Nov-2026) Read the requirement → Stories: S4 → S5 → End-to-end view Back to MCP Terms. Order currency : what the merchant priced in (AED). Transaction currency : what the customer pays in, and what the scheme clears in (APEX calls it cardholder currency ). Settlement currency : what the merchant is paid out in; MCP does not change it. Rate : Planet's rate from AED to the transaction currency, markup included. Decided after PRD v2 (09-Nov) and now in solution requirements v3.0 Geolocation is MaxMind GeoIP2 (a database held by PGW), not Planet. Planet offers no geolocation (13-Nov). Rates come from Planet's daily rate file (template 194). PGW quotes from the Visa section , the higher of the two rates (24-Nov). The converted amount is rounded up to the currency's minor unit (24-Nov). Refunds keep the PRD rule: round down, with the last-cent rule on the final refund. MCP is offered strictly on location. No proposed currency (UAE, no country, currency not offered, Phase 2) means AED only and no currency selector (25-Nov). The confirmation and receipt show the amount paid and the AED order amount (25-Nov). The MCP toggle is in PGW Configuration, built by the PGW team. It is switched on after Operations registers the merchant with Planet for MCP (24-Nov). The rate file gets basic checks only (header, trailer, record count, not loaded twice). The existing minimum refund amount covers MCP (25-Nov). Try UK customer pays in GBP Switches back to AED Germany: EUR US: USD Customer in the UAE No country found INR off for merchant Japan (Phase 2) MCP off Order in USD Direct API Pay-by-Link Yesterday's rates No valid rate file Wants Tabby Rounding up Apple Pay in GBP Wallet amount mismatch 1"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","Merchant set-up","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#merchant-set-up","PGW Configuration General Payment Methods Gateway Settings Multi-currency pricing Webhooks Dynamic multi-currency pricing Offer the customer a price in their own currency on HPP, based on their location. The merchant keeps pricing, reporting and settlement in the order currency. Enabled Currencies offered From the MCP currency list (APEX-supported and present in Planet's rate file). Currency Decimals Offered GBP 2 EUR 2 INR 2 USD 2 SAR 2 JPY Phase 2 0 No markup is set here. Markup is held at Planet and is already in the rates. Geidea screen shown in the Geidea Design System. Toggle name is a placeholder until PGW names it (must differ from ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY and ENABLE_MULTI_CURRENCY_SETTLEMENT ). 2"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","The order","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#the-order","merchant → PGW How the order is paid Create Session (API), customer pays on HPP SDK that shows Geidea HPP Pay-by-Link Direct API (card details collected by the merchant) Recurring or merchant-initiated payment Order currency AED USD Order amount MVP commitment is AED orders only. The solution is provisioned for any order currency (17-Nov). 3"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","Where the customer is","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#where-the-customer-is","customer IP → MaxMind → country United Kingdom GBP France EUR Germany EUR India INR United States USD Saudi Arabia SAR United Arab Emirates AED Japan JPY No country found Customer IP 81.2.69.142 dummy MaxMind result GB Mapped currency GBP PGW looks up the IP in the MaxMind GeoIP2 database it holds (no call out during the session), then maps the country to a currency using its own country-to-currency table. 4"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","Planet rate file","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#planet-rate-file","Planet → PGW, daily over SFTP Today's file loaded Today's file missing, yesterday's still valid No valid file File 20261124 v01 fetched, checked (header, trailer, record count) and stored in the PGW rate table. Every HPP quote today comes from this table. Test Merchant"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees › Planet rate file","Visual page","Choose how to pay","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#hpp","Total GBP 21.37 Order amount AED 100.00 Exchange rate 1 AED = 0.2137 GBP Paying in AED GBP EUR INR USD SAR Apple Pay | GBP 21.37 Google Pay | GBP 21.37 or pay with Credit or debit card Visa, Mastercard Card number · MM/YY · CVV Tabby Available in AED only Tamara Available in AED only Pay GBP 21.37 The amount shown stays fixed for this payment session. HPP as the customer sees it · Geidea Design System · Illustrative Test: the wallet token comes back with a different amount 5"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","Why the HPP looks like this","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#why-the-hpp-looks-like-this","PGW checks, in order 1 Order is paid on Geidea HPP Create Session, then HPP Yes 2 Order currency is AED Yes 3 MCP is on for this merchant Yes 4 A valid rate file is cached File 20261124 v01, valid to 25-Nov 23:59 UTC Yes 5 MaxMind returns a country for the customer IP 81.2.69.142 → GB Yes 6 Country maps to an active MCP currency GB → GBP Yes 7 Currency is on for this merchant Yes 8 Rate AED → currency is in the file (Visa section) 1 AED = 0.2137000 GBP Yes HPP proposes GBP . MCP_offered = Y. The customer can switch to any offered currency or back to AED. 6"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","The rate PGW used","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#the-rate-pgw-used","cached file · Visa section PFH,20261124,01 VILFH,HPLANET VISA,20261124,01 VID,2001,AED,784,2,GBP,826,2,0.2137000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VID,2002,AED,784,2,EUR,978,2,0.2489000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VID,2003,AED,784,2,INR,356,2,23.1200000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VID,2004,AED,784,2,USD,840,2,0.2759000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VID,2005,AED,784,2,SAR,682,2,1.0345000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VID,2006,AED,784,2,JPY,392,0,41.8500000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z VILFT,TPLANET VISA,4074,66.7430000,6 MCLFH,HPLANET MASTERCARD,20261124,01 MCD,3001,AED,784,2,GBP,826,2,0.2135000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCD,3002,AED,784,2,EUR,978,2,0.2486000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCD,3003,AED,784,2,INR,356,2,23.0950000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCD,3004,AED,784,2,USD,840,2,0.2756000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCD,3005,AED,784,2,SAR,682,2,1.0334000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCD,3006,AED,784,2,JPY,392,0,41.8000000,2026-11-24T00:00:00.000Z,2026-11-25T23:59:59.000Z MCLFT,TPLANET MASTERCARD,4074,66.6661000,6 PFT,TXN RATES,8148,133.4091000,12 Layout: Planet template 194 (Visa section VILFH/VID/VILFT, Mastercard section MCLFH/MCD/MCLFT). Rates are dummy, AED-based, markup included. Planet's sample writes the currency symbol in baseCurr/targetCurr; codes are used here for readability. Mastercard rows are greyed: PGW quotes from the Visa section. AED 100.00 × 0.2137000 = 21.3700000 GBP round up to 2 decimals → GBP 21.37 Try an order amount like 99.99 to see the rounding at work. 7"],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Visual page","After Pay","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#after-pay","what PGW stores · what the merchant sees Press Pay on the HPP to see the result. Sources: MCP solution requirements v3.0 section 8.1 and PGW stories S1 to S5, S7 (25-Nov-2026, drafts); Planet rate file template 194 and sample (Project_Feed/MCP/Planet Files); MCP project note, decisions 13-Nov to 24-Nov-2026. All rates, IP addresses and file values on this page are dummy values."],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: UK customer pays in GBP","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=gb-card",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Switches back to AED","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=gb-aed",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Germany: EUR","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=eu",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: US: USD","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=us",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Customer in the UAE","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=uae",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: No country found","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=geo-miss",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: INR off for merchant","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=cur-off",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Japan (Phase 2)","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=jp",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: MCP off","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=mcp-off",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Order in USD","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=order-usd",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Direct API","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=direct-api",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Pay-by-Link","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=pbl",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Yesterday's rates","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=rate-yday",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: No valid rate file","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=rate-none",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Wants Tabby","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=apm",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Rounding up","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=rounding",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Apple Pay in GBP","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=wallet",""],["MCP","HPP simulator: location, rates and what the customer sees","Scenario","Try it: Wallet amount mismatch","mcp/hpp-simulator.html#try=wallet-mismatch",""],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","Hub","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","mcp/index.html","feature MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing A customer on Geidea HPP is offered the price in their own currency, based on where they are, and can pay in it. The merchant prices, sees and is settled in AED as today, and never sees the conversion. Rates come from Planet's daily file, markup included. Launch target Jan-2027."],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","Hub","One order, three currencies: the main change","mcp/index.html#one-order-three-currencies-the-main-change","The change to discuss first. Inside PGW, the existing transaction amount and currency now hold what the customer paid (GBP 21.37). Everything the merchant sees, and APEX's main fields, stay in AED. Two new fields, mcpBaseAmount and mcpBaseCurrency , carry the AED value on every purchase and refund, so no system downstream converts anything. order currency"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing › One order, three currencies: the main change","Hub","What the merchant priced","mcp/index.html#what-the-merchant-priced","AED 100.00 Where Parameter Create Session amount currency existing PGW order amount currency existing PGW transaction mcpBaseAmount mcpBaseCurrency new Callback, order inquiry transaction.amount transaction.currency existing · AED for MCP APEX amount transactionCurrency existing · AED for MCP Seen by the merchant, the Merchant Portal and APEX main fields. MVP: AED orders only. transaction currency"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing › One order, three currencies: the main change","Hub","What the customer pays","mcp/index.html#what-the-customer-pays","GBP 21.37 Where Parameter PGW transaction amount currency existing · paid currency PGW transaction isMcp mcpRate mcpRateId new PGW order isMcpOffered new · internal MPGS / CYBS amount, currency existing APEX Cardholder Amount, Cardholder Currency, Cardholder ConvRate, Transaction Identifier new · names pending Chosen on HPP. Authorized and cleared with the scheme in this currency. Never shown to the merchant. settlement currency"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing › One order, three currencies: the main change","Hub","What the merchant is paid","mcp/index.html#what-the-merchant-is-paid","SAR Where Parameter APEX settlementAmount settlementCurrency existing APEX exchangeRate existing · order → settlement Unchanged by MCP. The AED order amount is converted to it for payout, as today. exchangeRate is not the MCP rate. Worked example: rate AED → GBP 0.2137, markup included. New PGW field names are the stories' proposals, except mcpBaseAmount and mcpBaseCurrency (agreed). Story S5 · Requirement"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","Hub","Documents","mcp/index.html#documents","Solution requirements What each Geidea system and team delivers for MCP v3.0 · 25-Nov-2026 PGW dev stories S1 to S7 written; S8 (APEX federation) and S9 (enrichment file) parked v0.1 · 25-Nov-2026 Interface notes APEX fields, enrichment record, Planet rate file and DTF in preparation"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","Hub","Visual pages","mcp/index.html#visual-pages","End-to-end view One AED order from Planet's rate file to payout and refunds, in one swimlane; switch location, rate file, currency, method and refunds and the flow redraws open HPP simulator Merchant set-up, customer location and rate-file state drive what the HPP offers; pay and see what PGW stores and what the merchant sees open Calculator Quote, rounding up, partial refunds with the last-cent rule; compare with rounding to nearest open Order model One AED 100.00 order step by step: HPP offer, purchase in GBP, EUR or INR (or AED), refunds that close it; order and transaction fields, AED totals, merchant and processor views open Rate file lifecycle Daily load, checks, validity overlap, MCP suspended planned What can go wrong Geolocation miss, missing rate file, wallet mismatch, record mismatches planned Federation and enrichment The same purchase and refunds as sent to APEX in real time and to Postilion in the enrichment file parked: APEX field names, enrichment format"],["MCP","MCP: dynamic multi-currency pricing","Hub","Stories and where to see them","mcp/index.html#stories","S1 · Configuration Simulator 1 S2 · Planet rate file: fetch and store Simulator 4 · End-to-end S3 · MaxMind database: fetch and store Simulator 3 S4 · HPP offer and selection Simulator · Calculator · End-to-end S5 · Payment and record Order model · Simulator 7 · End-to-end S6 · Refunds Order model · Calculator · End-to-end S7 · Merchant outputs in AED Order model · Simulator 7 · End-to-end S8 · Federation to APEX (parked) End-to-end S9 · Enrichment file (parked) End-to-end"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","mcp/order-model.html","mcp · visual page Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund Follow one AED 100.00 order through PGW. Step through the HPP offer, the purchase in the customer's currency and the refunds that close the order. See which fields PGW writes at each step, how order totals stay in AED, and what the merchant and the processor see. Illustrative Reflects PGW stories v0.1 (25-Nov-2026) Stories: S5 → S6 → S7 → Calculator HPP simulator End-to-end view Back to MCP Terms. Order currency : what the merchant priced in (AED). Transaction currency : what the customer pays in and what the scheme clears in. Order view of a transaction: mcpBaseAmount + mcpBaseCurrency (AED). Transaction view : amount + currency (paid currency). Rates are dummy (Visa section of a file dated 20261124, version 01). New field names are the stories' proposals, except mcpBaseAmount and mcpBaseCurrency (agreed). PGW engineering can rename them. Try HPP offer After the purchase GBP, refunds 60 + 40 GBP, refunds in thirds GBP, one full refund EUR, 60 + 40 INR, 60 + 40 Customer picks AED 1"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","The order","mcp/order-model.html#the-order","merchant offers GBP, EUR, INR Customer pays in GBP EUR INR AED (UK customer picks AED) Customer location gives GBP, which the merchant offers. HPP proposes it and the customer pays in it. Merchant refunds (AED) 60 + 40 33.33 × 2 + 33.34 100 in one none Order: AED 100.00 from Create Session. MID with MCP on ( S1 ). 2"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Steps","mcp/order-model.html#steps-2","Order created Create Session · AED 100.00 HPP opens Customer in United Kingdom · GBP proposed Purchase GBP 21.37 (AED 100.00) Refund 1 AED 60.00 → GBP 12.82 Refund 2 (final) AED 40.00 → GBP 8.55 ← Back Next step → 3"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","What happened","mcp/order-model.html#what-happened","S6"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund › What happened","Visual page","The merchant refunds AED 40.00 (final refund)","mcp/order-model.html#nowOut","This refund brings the AED refunded to AED 100.00, so it is the final refund. PGW does not multiply by the rate. It sends what is left of the amount paid, so the refunds add up exactly to GBP 21.37. Final refund (AED already refunded 60.00 + 40.00 = AED 100.00): GBP 21.37 − 12.82 = GBP 8.55 View the order model as JSON Table JSON for developers, table for everyone else. Same data. 4"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","PGW order model","mcp/order-model.html#pgw-order-model","S4 · S5 · S6 // HPP session (S4): fixed when HPP first loads { \"mcpCountry\" : \"GB\" , \"mcpProposedCurrency\" : \"GBP\" , \"isMcpOffered\" : true , \"mcpQuotes\" : [ { \"currency\" : \"GBP\" , \"amount\" : 21.37 , \"rate\" : 0.2137000 , \"rateId\" : \"2001\" , \"rateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"rateFileVersion\" : \"01\" }, { \"currency\" : \"EUR\" , \"amount\" : 24.89 , \"rate\" : 0.2489000 , \"rateId\" : \"2002\" , \"rateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"rateFileVersion\" : \"01\" }, { \"currency\" : \"INR\" , \"amount\" : 2312.00 , \"rate\" : 23.1200000 , \"rateId\" : \"2003\" , \"rateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"rateFileVersion\" : \"01\" } ] } // PGW order { \"orderId\" : \"…\" , \"amount\" : 100.00 , \"currency\" : \"AED\" , \"isMcpOffered\" : true , // other order fields as today \"transactions\" : [ { // purchase \"type\" : \"Pay\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" , \"amount\" : 21.37 , \"currency\" : \"GBP\" , \"isMcp\" : true , \"mcpBaseAmount\" : 100.00 , \"mcpBaseCurrency\" : \"AED\" , \"mcpRate\" : 0.2137000 , \"mcpRateId\" : \"2001\" , \"mcpRateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"mcpRateFileVersion\" : \"01\" // other transaction fields as today }, { // refund 1 \"type\" : \"Refund\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" , \"amount\" : 12.82 , \"currency\" : \"GBP\" , \"isMcp\" : true , \"mcpBaseAmount\" : 60.00 , \"mcpBaseCurrency\" : \"AED\" , \"mcpRate\" : 0.2137000 , \"mcpRateId\" : \"2001\" , \"mcpRateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"mcpRateFileVersion\" : \"01\" // other transaction fields as today }, { // refund 2, final \"type\" : \"Refund\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" , \"amount\" : 8.55 , \"currency\" : \"GBP\" , \"isMcp\" : true , \"mcpBaseAmount\" : 40.00 , \"mcpBaseCurrency\" : \"AED\" , \"mcpRate\" : 0.2137000 , \"mcpRateId\" : \"2001\" , \"mcpRateFileDate\" : \"2026-11-24\" , \"mcpRateFileVersion\" : \"01\" // other transaction fields as today } ] } Order totals, computed from mcpBaseAmount : paid AED 100.00 · refunded AED 100.00 · remaining AED 0.00 Why not amount ? The refunds' amount values are GBP: 12.82 + 8.55 = 21.37. Read as AED, the order would show AED 21.37 refunded and allow AED 78.63 more. The purchase amount (21.37) is GBP too. \"isMcp\" new MCP field \"amount\" existing field, holds the paid currency for an MCP transaction + written at this step Structure and MCP fields only. Other fields are as today and not shown. New names are the stories' proposals, except mcpBaseAmount and mcpBaseCurrency (agreed). 4"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","PGW order and HPP session","mcp/order-model.html#pgw-order-and-hpp-session","S4 · S5 section 3 Field Value Note Order amount existing 100.00 Order amount. Not changed by MCP. currency existing AED Order currency. isMcpOffered new · internal true Set when HPP loads. Never sent to the merchant. HPP session (S4) mcpCountry new GB From the IP lookup. Kept for support. mcpProposedCurrency new GBP First currency shown on HPP. mcpQuotes[] new GBP 21.37 @ 0.2137000 (rateId 2001) EUR 24.89 @ 0.2489000 (rateId 2002) INR 2,312.00 @ 23.1200000 (rateId 2003) One per offered currency. Fixed for the session. Each also holds rateFileDate 2026-11-24, rateFileVersion 01."],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund › PGW order and HPP session","Visual page","Order totals existing · computed from mcpBaseAmount","mcp/order-model.html#order-totals-existing-computed-from-mcpbaseamount","Paid AED 100.00 purchase mcpBaseAmount Refunded AED 100.00 60.00 + 40.00 Remaining to refund AED 0.00 order fully refunded S5 section 4: compute every order total from mcpBaseAmount . Never add amount values of transactions in different currencies. Why not amount ? The refunds' amount values are GBP: 12.82 + 8.55 = 21.37. Read as AED, the order would show AED 21.37 refunded and allow AED 78.63 more. The purchase amount (21.37) is GBP too. 5"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Transactions of the order","mcp/order-model.html#transactions-of-the-order","S5 · S6 Field Purchase type Pay Refund 1 type Refund Refund 2 · final type Refund Transaction view (what the processor and scheme use) amount existing · paid currency 21.37 12.82 8.55 currency existing · paid currency GBP GBP GBP Order view (what totals, merchant outputs and APEX read) mcpBaseAmount new · agreed name 100.00 60.00 40.00 mcpBaseCurrency new · agreed name AED AED AED Conversion isMcp new true true true mcpRate new 0.2137000 0.2137000 0.2137000 mcpRateId new 2001 2001 2001 mcpRateFileDate new 2026-11-24 2026-11-24 2026-11-24 mcpRateFileVersion new 01 01 01 written at this step existing as today existing · paid currency same field, holds the transaction view for MCP new MCP field 5"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Merchant sees","mcp/order-model.html#merchant-sees","S7 Callback and order inquiry, transactions : \"transactions\": [ { \"type\" : \"Pay\" , \"amount\" : 100.00 , \"currency\" : \"AED\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" }, { \"type\" : \"Refund\" , \"amount\" : 60.00 , \"currency\" : \"AED\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" }, { \"type\" : \"Refund\" , \"amount\" : 40.00 , \"currency\" : \"AED\" , \"status\" : \"Success\" } ] For isMcp = true, PGW fills amount with mcpBaseAmount and currency with mcpBaseCurrency . No rate, no MCP field, no transaction currency. Other field names as in today's payload. Merchant Portal shows APEX data (no PGW change). 6"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Processor receives","mcp/order-model.html#processor-receives","MPGS or CyberSource Call amount currency Payment 21.37 GBP Refund 1 12.82 GBP Refund 2 8.55 GBP Existing processor fields only. No new processor fields. MPGS and CyberSource are set up for the full ISO currency list. 7"],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Visual page","Checks on the order","mcp/order-model.html#checks-on-the-order","S5 section 4 · S6 goal 2 pass Order totals in AED, from mcpBaseAmount : paid 100.00, refunded 100.00, remaining 0.00. pass Every transaction of the order carries the purchase rate 0.2137000 (rateId 2001). No new rate is looked up for a refund. pass Refunds add up to the amount paid in both currencies: AED 100.00 = AED 100.00, GBP 21.37 = GBP 21.37. pass Merchant outputs show AED only (3 transactions). Not on this page. The same purchase and refunds as sent to APEX ( S8 ) and in the enrichment file to Postilion ( S9 ): parked until APEX gives the field names and the enrichment format is agreed. Void and chargebacks: not covered here."],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: HPP offer","mcp/order-model.html#try=offered",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: After the purchase","mcp/order-model.html#try=after-pay",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: GBP, refunds 60 + 40","mcp/order-model.html#try=gbp-60-40",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: GBP, refunds in thirds","mcp/order-model.html#try=gbp-thirds",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: GBP, one full refund","mcp/order-model.html#try=gbp-full",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: EUR, 60 + 40","mcp/order-model.html#try=eur-60-40",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: INR, 60 + 40","mcp/order-model.html#try=inr-60-40",""],["MCP","Order model: one MCP order, from purchase to the last refund","Scenario","Try it: Customer picks AED","mcp/order-model.html#try=aed-paid",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html","v1.2 25-Nov-2026 Source: NT PGW Dev Stories v1.2 (Lab copy).docx Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) Version 1.2 · 25-Nov-2026 · Prepared by Ghulam Rabbani (Product) Team: PGW engineering team Changes in v1.2 (25-Nov-2026): Open point 1 and the closed-points note now refer to the master toggle Generate and Use Network Token . Team names in place of people's names. NT-C1 acceptance criteria renumbered (5a, 5b → 6, 7; old 6 → 8). No change to any requirement. Changes in v1.1 (19-Nov-2026): Rule 1 now uses one master toggle, Generate and Use Network Token , per MID, default OFF. NT-C1: one CYBS call only (no enrollment call), no securityCode , adapter returns failures, no secrets in logs. NT-0 acceptance criterion 5 added. These stories are the requirement. Each story can be read alone. A story refers to another story only for work that must be built first."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","Story map","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-map","Payment explorer Token layers # Story What it delivers Depends on Status NT-0 Network token data model and merchant APIs New transaction object networkTokenDetails . New fields on the Geidea token record. Object returned to the merchant. — Written NT-M1 Update MPGS token generation PGW reads the network token provider when it creates the MPGS token. PGW updates the Geidea token record. NT-0 Written NT-M2 MPGS Pay (card number) PGW records network token data on Pay and Authorize with a card number. NT-0 Written NT-M3 MPGS token CIT PGW records network token data on CIT with a Geidea token. NT-0, NT-M1 Written NT-M4 MPGS token MIT PGW records network token data on MIT with a Geidea token. NT-0, NT-M1 Written NT-M5 MPGS capture, refund, void PGW records network token data on follow-on transactions. NT-M2, NT-M3, NT-M4 Written NT-C1 Create CYBS instrument identifier PGW creates a CYBS instrument identifier for a saved card. NT-0 Written NT-C2 CYBS Pay (card number) PGW records network token data on Pay and Authorize with a card number. NT-0 Written NT-C3 CYBS token CIT PGW pays CIT with the instrument identifier. PGW records network token data. NT-0, NT-C1 Written NT-C4 CYBS token MIT PGW pays MIT with the instrument identifier. PGW records network token data. NT-0, NT-C1 Written NT-C5 CYBS capture, refund, void PGW records network token data on follow-on transactions. NT-C2, NT-C3, NT-C4 Written NT-A1 APEX network token keys Network token data sent to APEX in userData . NT-M2–M4, NT-C2–C4 Waiting on APEX team NT-X Token status and retry control PGW stops using a Geidea token after a \"do not retry\" decline. NT-M3, NT-M4, NT-C3, NT-C4 Waiting on Risk & Compliance Build order: NT-0 → NT-M1 → NT-M2, NT-M3, NT-M4 → NT-M5. CYBS in parallel: NT-C1 → NT-C2, NT-C3, NT-C4 → NT-C5."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","Prerequisites (not PGW work)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#prerequisites-not-pgw-work","# Item Needed for Owner P1 MPGS: MDES onboarding, Visa VTS via TRID 40000000000 , Enable Network Tokens per merchant NT-M1 to NT-M5 (to see network tokens in test and live) Merchant integration team, MPGS P2 CYBS: network token provisioning on the vault. Visa and Mastercard token permission per MID. In place on MID TEST-CYBS-01 . NT-C1 to NT-C5 Merchant integration team P3 CYBS Decision Manager rule for MITs (a Mastercard MIT was rejected without DECISION_SKIP in the 11-Nov POC) NT-C4 Risk & Compliance"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","Rules for every story","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#rules-for-every-story","Switches and rollout Master toggle. The existing PGW configuration parameter Generate and Use Network Token is the one master toggle for all work in these stories. It is set per MID. Default: OFF for all MIDs. Toggle OFF: PGW behaves exactly as today. PGW does not create CYBS instrument identifiers. PGW pays CIT and MIT on CYBS with the card number. PGW sets networkTokenDetails = null . PGW does not change the Geidea token record. Toggle ON: the stories apply. The existing toggles still apply as today: Enable tokenization , CUSTOMER_INITIATED_TRANSACTIONS , MERCHANT_INITIATED_TRANSACTIONS . Do not use the other network token parameters ( Use Network Token , Send NT to merchant ). Rollout: switch ON for the production test MID, test in production, then switch ON for all merchants. A later release can remove this toggle. MPGS: MPGS configuration per MID (P1) decides if MPGS pays with a network token. The PGW toggle controls only what PGW records. CYBS: the PGW toggle controls instrument identifier creation and payment with it. CYBS token permission per MID (P2) decides if CYBS uses a network token. A failure to read or record network token data never changes the payment result. Log the failure. Continue. Never store or log a full card number or a full network token number. Gateway field names are as in MPGS REST API version 80 and CyberSource REST API. PGW field names are camelCase . New fields in merchant APIs are additions. Do not change or remove existing fields. Copy gateway values as received, unless a rule in the story says otherwise."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-0-network-token-data-model-and-merchant-apis","What PGW records"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background","Visa charges a fee on card-not-present transactions that do not use a network token. PGW does not record if a transaction used a network token. PGW does not record if a saved card has a network token."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal","PGW has one object to record network token data on each transaction, for MPGS and CYBS. PGW returns this object to the merchant. The Geidea token record has fields for network token data and token status."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary","This story adds the object and the fields. It does not fill them. The gateway stories (NT-M1 to NT-M5, NT-C1 to NT-C5) fill them. Item Value Story ID NT-0 Consumers Merchants (order inquiry, callback, pay responses). PGW stories NT-M1 to NT-C5. Gateway API used None Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails ; Geidea token record Depends on — Followed by NT-M1 to NT-M5, NT-C1 to NT-C5 Out of scope Filling the fields (gateway stories). Token status logic (NT-X)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. New transaction object networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#new-transaction-object-networktokendetails","Field Type Values Meaning isNetworkToken Boolean true / false true = the gateway paid with a network token. tokenProvider String VTS / MDES / null Network token provider. VTS = Visa. MDES = Mastercard. null when isNetworkToken = false . maskedTokenNumber String e.g. 489537xxxxxx0001 (MPGS), 5222220000000000 (CYBS) / null Masked network token number. CYBS returns only the token BIN, so the rest is zero-filled. tokenExpiryMonth String e.g. 11 / null Network token expiry month. tokenExpiryYear String e.g. 28 / null Network token expiry year. paymentAccountReference String e.g. V0010000000000000000000000001 / null PAR. One value per card."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Transactions that carry the object","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#transactions-that-carry-the-object","Add the object to transactions of type Pay , Authorization , Capture , Refund , Void . Do not add the object to Authentication transactions. Before a gateway story fills the object, set it to null . Transactions created before this release: networkTokenDetails = null ."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Return the object to the merchant","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#return-the-object-to-the-merchant","Merchant API Where Order inquiry GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order/{orderId} order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails Callback to callbackUrl order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay response order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token response order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. New fields on the Geidea token record (internal)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#new-fields-on-the-geidea-token-record-internal","Field Type Values Default (new and existing tokens) Meaning schemeTokenProvider String VTS / MDES / null null A network token exists for this saved card. null = none seen yet. tokenStatus String ACTIVE / INACTIVE ACTIVE For NT-X. Not read or changed in this release. tokenStatusReason String free text null For NT-X. Not changed in this release. tokenStatusDate DateTime UAE time null For NT-X. Not changed in this release. cybsInstrumentIdentifierId String 19 digits / null null CYBS instrument identifier. Set by NT-C1. networkTokenState String e.g. ACTIVE / null null Network token state from CYBS. Set by NT-C1. Do not return the token record fields in any merchant API in this release."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","5. Update rules","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#update-rules","Field Rule networkTokenDetails Write once per transaction. Do not update after that. schemeTokenProvider When it is not null , do not change it. tokenStatus , tokenStatusReason , tokenStatusDate Do not change in this release."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-0 — Network token data model and merchant APIs","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria","Order inquiry for an existing order returns networkTokenDetails = null on each Pay , Authorization , Capture , Refund , Void transaction. Authentication transactions do not have the object. Existing Geidea tokens have tokenStatus = ACTIVE and all other new fields = null . Existing merchant API fields do not change. Generate and Use Network Token OFF on a MID: networkTokenDetails = null on all new transactions. The Geidea token record does not change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-m1-update-mpgs-token-generation","Explorer: MPGS save card"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-1","On MPGS, PGW creates an MPGS token after a card is saved. When network tokens are enabled on MPGS (P1), MPGS asks Visa or Mastercard for a network token for the card. The MPGS token response shows if a network token exists. PGW does not read this today."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-1","PGW records on the Geidea token record if a network token exists for the saved card."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-1","Item Value Story ID NT-M1 Gateway MPGS, API version 80 MPGS API used Create or update token: PUT /api/rest/version/80/merchant/{merchantId}/token/{tokenId} Entities written Geidea token record: schemeTokenProvider Depends on NT-0 Followed by NT-M3, NT-M4 Out of scope Payment requests and responses (NT-M2 to NT-M5). Token status (NT-X)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-1",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Trigger","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#trigger","No change. PGW calls the MPGS token endpoint at the same point as today ( SendToken , after a save-card payment)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Response fields to read","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#response-fields-to-read","MPGS field Type Example Meaning schemeToken.provider String VTS A network token exists. Absent if none exists yet. Note: in version 80 the token response has no masked network token number, no token expiry and no network token status."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing","# Condition Action 4.1 schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token is not null Do not change it. Stop. 4.2 schemeToken.provider = VTS or MDES Set schemeTokenProvider = the value received. 4.3 schemeToken.provider is absent Leave schemeTokenProvider = null . 4.4 schemeToken.provider has any other value Leave schemeTokenProvider = null . Log the value. 4.5 The MPGS token call fails No change from today. Why 4.3: MPGS can create the network token after the token call. NT-M3 and NT-M4 set schemeTokenProvider at the first payment with a network token."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M1 — Update MPGS token generation","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-1","Save a Visa card on an MPGS MID with network tokens enabled. Token response has schemeToken.provider = VTS . Geidea token has schemeTokenProvider = VTS . Same for Mastercard: MDES . MID without network tokens enabled: schemeTokenProvider = null . Save the same card again (same tokenId ): schemeTokenProvider does not change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-m2-mpgs-pay-card-number","Mapper: MPGS card"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-2","A Pay or Authorize with a card number does not use a network token. PGW records the result so that every transaction carries the same object."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-2","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on Pay and Authorize with a card number on MPGS."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-2","Item Value Story ID NT-M2 Gateway MPGS, API version 80 Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay ; HPP payment with card number MPGS API used PUT /api/rest/version/80/merchant/{merchantId}/order/{orderId}/transaction/{transactionId} , apiOperation = PAY or AUTHORIZE Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails Depends on NT-0 Followed by NT-M5 Out of scope Token creation (NT-M1). Payments with a Geidea token (NT-M3, NT-M4)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-2",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-1","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Response fields to read","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#response-fields-to-read-1","MPGS field Type Example sourceOfFunds.type String CARD sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand String VISA sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificNumber String 489537xxxxxx0001 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month String 11 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year String 28 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.paymentAccountReference String V0010000000000000000000000001"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails","PGW field MPGS source Rule isNetworkToken sourceOfFunds.type true if SCHEME_TOKEN . false for any other value. tokenProvider sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand If isNetworkToken = true : VISA → VTS , MASTERCARD → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber …card.deviceSpecificNumber Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryMonth …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryYear …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year Copy. null if absent. paymentAccountReference …card.paymentAccountReference Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-1","Fill the object from the MPGS response of the same transaction. If the response has no sourceOfFunds , set the object to null . Apply to approved and declined transactions. Do not change the Geidea token record."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M2 — MPGS Pay (card number)","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-2","Pay with a Visa card number: isNetworkToken = false , tokenProvider = null . PAR in the MPGS response is copied to paymentAccountReference . Same result for AUTHORIZE and for HPP. The object is returned in order inquiry, callback and the /pay response."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-m3-mpgs-token-cit","Explorer: MPGS CIT Mapper"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-3","PGW pays a customer-initiated transaction (CIT) with the MPGS token of a saved card. When network tokens are enabled on MPGS (P1), MPGS sends the network token to the scheme in place of the card. Tests on 16–17 Nov 2026 confirmed this for Visa and Mastercard. PGW does not record it."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-3","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on token CIT. PGW sets schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token when a network token is first seen. The payment request does not change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-3","Item Value Story ID NT-M3 Gateway MPGS, API version 80 Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token ( initiatedBy = Payer ); HPP with tokenId MPGS API used PUT /api/rest/version/80/merchant/{merchantId}/order/{orderId}/transaction/{transactionId} , apiOperation = PAY or AUTHORIZE , sourceOfFunds.token Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails ; Geidea token record: schemeTokenProvider Depends on NT-0, NT-M1 Followed by NT-M5, NT-X Out of scope Token status and retry control (NT-X)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-3",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-2","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Response fields to read","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#response-fields-to-read-2","MPGS field Type Example sourceOfFunds.type String SCHEME_TOKEN sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand String MASTERCARD sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificNumber String masked token number sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month String 11 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year String 28 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.paymentAccountReference String PAR"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-1","PGW field MPGS source Rule isNetworkToken sourceOfFunds.type true if SCHEME_TOKEN . false for any other value. tokenProvider sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand If isNetworkToken = true : VISA → VTS , MASTERCARD → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber …card.deviceSpecificNumber Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryMonth …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryYear …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year Copy. null if absent. paymentAccountReference …card.paymentAccountReference Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-2","Fill the object from the MPGS response of the same transaction. If the response has no sourceOfFunds , set the object to null . Apply to approved and declined transactions. If isNetworkToken = true and schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token is null : set schemeTokenProvider = tokenProvider . If schemeTokenProvider is not null : do not change it. Keep saving authorizationResponse.merchantAdviceCode and response.acquirerCode as today. NT-X uses them."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M3 — MPGS token CIT","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-3","Token CIT, Visa, network tokens enabled: isNetworkToken = true , tokenProvider = VTS , masked number, expiry and PAR filled. Same for Mastercard: MDES . Geidea token with schemeTokenProvider = null gets VTS or MDES after the first network token CIT. Token CIT on a MID without network tokens: isNetworkToken = false . schemeTokenProvider does not change. Same results for AUTHORIZE and for HPP with tokenId ."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-m4-mpgs-token-mit","Explorer: MPGS MIT Mapper"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-4","PGW pays a merchant-initiated transaction (MIT) with the MPGS token of a saved card. When network tokens are enabled on MPGS (P1), MPGS sends the network token in place of the card. Tests on 16–17 Nov 2026 confirmed this for Visa and Mastercard. PGW does not record it."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-4","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on token MIT. PGW sets schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token when a network token is first seen. The payment request does not change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-4","Item Value Story ID NT-M4 Gateway MPGS, API version 80 Geidea endpoint POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token ( initiatedBy = Merchant ) MPGS API used PUT /api/rest/version/80/merchant/{merchantId}/order/{orderId}/transaction/{transactionId} , apiOperation = PAY , sourceOfFunds.token Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails ; Geidea token record: schemeTokenProvider Depends on NT-0, NT-M1 Followed by NT-M5, NT-X Out of scope Token status and retry control (NT-X)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-4",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-3","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Response fields to read","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#response-fields-to-read-3","MPGS field Type Example sourceOfFunds.type String SCHEME_TOKEN sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand String VISA sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificNumber String 489537xxxxxx0001 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month String 11 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year String 28 sourceOfFunds.provided.card.paymentAccountReference String V0010000000000000000000000001"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-2","PGW field MPGS source Rule isNetworkToken sourceOfFunds.type true if SCHEME_TOKEN . false for any other value. tokenProvider sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand If isNetworkToken = true : VISA → VTS , MASTERCARD → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber …card.deviceSpecificNumber Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryMonth …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryYear …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year Copy. null if absent. paymentAccountReference …card.paymentAccountReference Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-3","Fill the object from the MPGS response of the same transaction. If the response has no sourceOfFunds , set the object to null . Apply to approved and declined transactions. If isNetworkToken = true and schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token is null : set schemeTokenProvider = tokenProvider . If schemeTokenProvider is not null : do not change it. Keep saving authorizationResponse.merchantAdviceCode and response.acquirerCode as today. NT-X uses them."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","5. Example: Visa MIT MIT-0000A001-0000000001","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#example-visa-mit-mit-0000a001-0000000001","MPGS response (excerpt): \"sourceOfFunds\": { \"type\": \"SCHEME_TOKEN\", \"token\": \"0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9\", \"provided\": { \"card\": { \"brand\": \"VISA\", \"deviceSpecificNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\", \"deviceSpecificExpiry\": { \"month\": \"11\", \"year\": \"28\" }, \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\", \"storedOnFile\": \"STORED\" } } } PGW transaction: \"networkTokenDetails\": { \"isNetworkToken\": true, \"tokenProvider\": \"VTS\", \"maskedTokenNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\", \"tokenExpiryMonth\": \"11\", \"tokenExpiryYear\": \"28\", \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" }"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M4 — MPGS token MIT","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-4","The example above gives the PGW object above. Same for Mastercard: MDES . Geidea token with schemeTokenProvider = null gets VTS or MDES after the first network token MIT. MIT on a MID without network tokens: isNetworkToken = false . schemeTokenProvider does not change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-m5-mpgs-capture-refund-void","Explorer: MPGS refund"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-5","Capture, refund and void follow a Pay, Authorize, CIT or MIT. MPGS returns the source of funds on these transactions. Tests on 16–17 Nov 2026 confirmed capture and refund on network tokens."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-5","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on capture, refund and void on MPGS."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-5","Item Value Story ID NT-M5 Gateway MPGS, API version 80 Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v1/direct/capture ; POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/refund ; POST /pgw/api/v3/direct/void MPGS API used PUT /api/rest/version/80/merchant/{merchantId}/order/{orderId}/transaction/{transactionId} , apiOperation = CAPTURE , REFUND or VOID Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails Depends on NT-M2, NT-M3, NT-M4 Out of scope Geidea token record (no change in this story)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-5",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-4","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-3","PGW field MPGS source Rule isNetworkToken sourceOfFunds.type true if SCHEME_TOKEN . false for any other value. tokenProvider sourceOfFunds.provided.card.brand If isNetworkToken = true : VISA → VTS , MASTERCARD → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber …card.deviceSpecificNumber Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryMonth …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month Copy. null if absent. tokenExpiryYear …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year Copy. null if absent. paymentAccountReference …card.paymentAccountReference Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-4","Fill the object from the MPGS response of the same transaction. If the response has no sourceOfFunds : copy networkTokenDetails from the original Pay or Authorization transaction of the order. If the original transaction has no object: set the object to null . Do not change the Geidea token record."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-M5 — MPGS capture, refund, void","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-5","Capture of a network token Authorize: isNetworkToken = true , same provider and PAR as the Authorize. Refund and void: same. Capture of a card-number Authorize: isNetworkToken = false ."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-c1-create-cybs-instrument-identifier","Explorer: save card (T1) On demand (T2) Failure"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-6","On CYBS, PGW does not create a gateway token when a card is saved. PGW sends the card number from the Geidea vault on each CIT and MIT. CYBS cannot use a network token this way. A CYBS instrument identifier links the card to a network token. A POC on 11 Nov 2026 (MID TEST-CYBS-01 ) confirmed: CYBS creates the network token with the instrument identifier, and payments with it use the network token."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-6","PGW creates a CYBS instrument identifier for each saved card on CYBS and stores it on the Geidea token."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-6","Item Value Story ID NT-C1 Gateway CyberSource REST API (Token Management Service) CYBS API used POST /tms/v1/instrumentidentifiers Entities written Geidea token record: cybsInstrumentIdentifierId , networkTokenState Depends on NT-0 Followed by NT-C3, NT-C4 Out of scope Payment requests (NT-C2 to NT-C5). Creating the identifier inside the payment ( actionList: [\"TOKEN_CREATE\"] ): not used. CYBS customer and payment instrument tokens. Network token lifecycle updates from CYBS."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-6",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Triggers","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#triggers","# Trigger When T1 After save card A Pay or Authorize with save card is approved on a CYBS MID, and PGW saves the card. Same point as SendToken on MPGS. T2 On demand NT-C3 or NT-C4 calls it before a CIT or MIT when cybsInstrumentIdentifierId = null . This covers cards saved before go-live and failed T1 calls."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Pre-checks","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#pre-checks","# Check On failure 2.1 The MID is routed to CYBS. Do not call CYBS. No error to the merchant. 2.2 Enable tokenization is ON for the MID. Do not call CYBS. No error to the merchant. 2.2a Generate and Use Network Token is ON for the MID. Do not call CYBS. No error to the merchant. 2.3 The card number and expiry are available in the Geidea vault for this token. Do not call CYBS. Log. No error to the merchant."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-5","CYBS field M/O/C Value type M enrollable card card.number M Card number from the Geidea vault card.expirationMonth M 2 digits, e.g. 02 card.expirationYear M 4 digits, e.g. 2029 card.securityCode — Do not send. { \"type\": \"enrollable card\", \"card\": { \"number\": \"<PAN>\", \"expirationMonth\": \"02\", \"expirationYear\": \"2029\" } } Headers: the same as PGW payment calls on the MID: v-c-merchant-id , v-c-date , Digest , Signature (HTTP Signature, HmacSHA256), Content-Type: application/json . No profile-id header. (Proven in the 11-Nov POC, Postman collection \"CYBS NT POC\", request 2.) HTTP status: Status Meaning Action 201 New instrument identifier created Success (section 5) 200 Instrument identifier already exists for this card Success (section 5) Any other Failure Section 5.3 This is the only CYBS call in NT-C1. Do not call POST /tms/v1/instrumentidentifiers/{id}/enrollment or any other TMS endpoint. (Test log 18-Nov-2026: the Cybersource adapter sent this extra call. CYBS rejected it with HTTP 400 invalidFields , card.number .)"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Response fields to read","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#response-fields-to-read-4","CYBS field Type Example Meaning id String (19 digits) 7000000000000000001 Instrument identifier. CYBS generates it. PGW cannot set it. tokenizedCard.state String ACTIVE Network token state at creation."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","5. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-5","# Outcome Action 5.1 Success, id received Save id in cybsInstrumentIdentifierId . Save tokenizedCard.state in networkTokenState ( null if absent). 5.2 Success, id differs from the stored value Replace the stored value. Log the old and new value. 5.3 Failure (timeout, HTTP 4xx, HTTP 5xx) Leave cybsInstrumentIdentifierId = null . Log the error. Do not change the result of the payment (T1). Return \"not created\" to the caller (T2). The Cybersource adapter returns the failure to PGW. It does not return a success code ( 000 ) when a CYBS call fails. Note: the same card gives the same id . The CYBS test bench showed instrumentidentifierNew = true for a new card and false for a known card."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","6. Sensitive data","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#sensitive-data","Read the card number from the vault only for this call. Do not log the request body. Do not log the merchant SharedSecretKey , MerchantKeyId or the CVV."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C1 — Create CYBS instrument identifier","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-6","Save a Visa card on MID TEST-CYBS-01 : Geidea token gets a 19-digit cybsInstrumentIdentifierId and networkTokenState = ACTIVE . Same for Mastercard. Save the same card again: same cybsInstrumentIdentifierId . CYBS returns an error: the save-card payment result does not change. cybsInstrumentIdentifierId = null . MID routed to MPGS: no call to CYBS. CYBS MID with Enable tokenization OFF: no call to CYBS. CYBS MID with Generate and Use Network Token OFF: no call to CYBS. CIT and MIT go out with the card number, as today. Logs do not contain the card number."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-c2-cybs-pay-card-number","Mapper: CYBS card"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-7","A Pay or Authorize with a card number does not use a network token. PGW records the result so that every transaction carries the same object."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-7","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on Pay and Authorize with a card number on CYBS."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-7","Item Value Story ID NT-C2 Gateway CyberSource REST API Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay ; HPP payment with card number CYBS API used POST /pts/v2/payments Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails Depends on NT-0 Followed by NT-C5 Out of scope Instrument identifier creation after save card (NT-C1). Payments with a Geidea token (NT-C3, NT-C4)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-7",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Request","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-6","No change."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-4","PGW field CYBS response source Rule isNetworkToken processingInformation.paymentSolution true if 015 or 014 . false for any other value or if absent. tokenProvider processingInformation.paymentSolution 015 → VTS . 014 → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber paymentInformation.card.bin (token BIN, 6 digits) If isNetworkToken = true : the 6-digit BIN followed by 10 zeros (16 digits). Example: 522222 → 5222220000000000 . Otherwise null . tokenExpiryMonth Not in the CYBS response null tokenExpiryYear Not in the CYBS response null paymentAccountReference processorInformation.paymentAccountReferenceNumber Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-6","Fill the object from the CYBS response of the same transaction. Apply to approved and declined transactions. Do not change the Geidea token record."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C2 — CYBS Pay (card number)","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-7","Pay with a Visa card number: isNetworkToken = false , tokenProvider = null . PAR in the CYBS response is copied to paymentAccountReference . Same result for Authorize and for HPP."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-c3-cybs-token-cit","Explorer: CYBS CIT Mapper"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-8","On CYBS, PGW pays a CIT with the card number from the Geidea vault. CYBS cannot use a network token this way. A POC on 11 Nov 2026 (MID TEST-CYBS-01 ) confirmed: a CIT with the instrument identifier uses the network token. Test CY-0000C002-0000000002 (Mastercard): 3DS ran, paymentSolution = 014 , PAR returned."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-8","PGW pays token CIT with the CYBS instrument identifier. PGW fills networkTokenDetails . PGW sets schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token when a network token is first seen."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-8","Item Value Story ID NT-C3 Gateway CyberSource REST API Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token ( initiatedBy = Payer ); HPP with tokenId CYBS API used POST /pts/v2/payments Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails ; Geidea token record: schemeTokenProvider Depends on NT-0, NT-C1 Followed by NT-C5, NT-X Out of scope Token status and retry control (NT-X). 3DS flow (no change)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-8",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Choose the funding source","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#choose-the-funding-source","# Condition Action 1.1 cybsInstrumentIdentifierId is not null Send the request in section 2. 1.2 cybsInstrumentIdentifierId = null Call NT-C1 (trigger T2). If it returns an id , send the request in section 2. 1.3 NT-C1 returns \"not created\" Send the request with the card number, as today."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Request change","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-change","Change only paymentInformation . Add tokenInformation . Do not change any other field. CYBS field M/O/C Value paymentInformation.instrumentIdentifier.id M cybsInstrumentIdentifierId paymentInformation.card.number — Do not send. paymentInformation.card.expirationMonth M From the Geidea vault, as today paymentInformation.card.expirationYear M From the Geidea vault, as today paymentInformation.card.securityCode C Send when the cardholder enters the CVV, as today tokenInformation.networkTokenOption M prefer // today \"paymentInformation\": { \"card\": { \"number\": \"<PAN>\", \"expirationMonth\": \"02\", \"expirationYear\": \"2029\", \"securityCode\": \"<CVV>\" } } // new \"paymentInformation\": { \"instrumentIdentifier\": { \"id\": \"7000000000000000001\" }, \"card\": { \"expirationMonth\": \"02\", \"expirationYear\": \"2029\", \"securityCode\": \"<CVV>\" } }, \"tokenInformation\": { \"networkTokenOption\": \"prefer\" } No change to: processingInformation.authorizationOptions.initiator , stored-credential flags, consumerAuthenticationInformation , order and amount fields."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-5","PGW field CYBS response source Rule isNetworkToken processingInformation.paymentSolution true if 015 or 014 . false for any other value or if absent. tokenProvider processingInformation.paymentSolution 015 → VTS . 014 → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber paymentInformation.card.bin (token BIN, 6 digits) If isNetworkToken = true : the 6-digit BIN followed by 10 zeros (16 digits). Example: 522222 → 5222220000000000 . Otherwise null . tokenExpiryMonth Not in the CYBS response null tokenExpiryYear Not in the CYBS response null paymentAccountReference processorInformation.paymentAccountReferenceNumber Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-7","Fill the object from the CYBS response of the same transaction. Apply to approved and declined transactions. If isNetworkToken = true and schemeTokenProvider is null : set schemeTokenProvider = tokenProvider . If schemeTokenProvider is not null : do not change it. A decline on the instrument identifier is final. Do not retry with the card number. Save on the transaction, if PGW does not save them today: processorInformation.responseCode , processorInformation.merchantAdvice.code , processorInformation.merchantAdvice.codeRaw . NT-X uses them."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C3 — CYBS token CIT","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-8","Token CIT, Mastercard, MID TEST-CYBS-01 : request has instrumentIdentifier.id and no card number. Response paymentSolution = 014 . isNetworkToken = true , tokenProvider = MDES , PAR filled. Same for Visa: 015 , VTS . Token without an instrument identifier: NT-C1 is called, then the CIT uses the new id . NT-C1 fails: the CIT is sent with the card number. isNetworkToken = false . 3DS runs as today. CVV is sent when entered. Geidea token with schemeTokenProvider = null gets VTS or MDES after the first network token CIT."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-c4-cybs-token-mit","Explorer: CYBS MIT Mapper"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-9","On CYBS, PGW pays an MIT with the card number from the Geidea vault and the network transaction ID of the first payment. CYBS cannot use a network token this way. A POC on 11 Nov 2026 (MID TEST-CYBS-01 ) confirmed: an MIT with the instrument identifier uses the network token for Visa ( 015 ) and Mastercard ( 014 )."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-9","PGW pays token MIT with the CYBS instrument identifier. PGW fills networkTokenDetails . PGW sets schemeTokenProvider on the Geidea token when a network token is first seen."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-9","Item Value Story ID NT-C4 Gateway CyberSource REST API Geidea endpoint POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token ( initiatedBy = Merchant ) CYBS API used POST /pts/v2/payments Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails ; Geidea token record: schemeTokenProvider Depends on NT-0, NT-C1. Prerequisite P3 (Decision Manager rule). Followed by NT-C5, NT-X Out of scope Token status and retry control (NT-X)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-9",""],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","1. Choose the funding source","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#choose-the-funding-source-1","# Condition Action 1.1 cybsInstrumentIdentifierId is not null Send the request in section 2. 1.2 cybsInstrumentIdentifierId = null Call NT-C1 (trigger T2). If it returns an id , send the request in section 2. 1.3 NT-C1 returns \"not created\" Send the request with the card number, as today."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","2. Request change","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#request-change-1","Change only paymentInformation . Add tokenInformation . Do not change any other field. CYBS field M/O/C Value paymentInformation.instrumentIdentifier.id M cybsInstrumentIdentifierId paymentInformation.card.number — Do not send. paymentInformation.card.expirationMonth M From the Geidea vault, as today paymentInformation.card.expirationYear M From the Geidea vault, as today paymentInformation.card.securityCode — Do not send (MIT). tokenInformation.networkTokenOption M prefer // today \"paymentInformation\": { \"card\": { \"number\": \"<PAN>\", \"expirationMonth\": \"02\", \"expirationYear\": \"2029\" } } // new \"paymentInformation\": { \"instrumentIdentifier\": { \"id\": \"7000000000000000001\" }, \"card\": { \"expirationMonth\": \"02\", \"expirationYear\": \"2029\" } }, \"tokenInformation\": { \"networkTokenOption\": \"prefer\" } No change to: processingInformation.authorizationOptions.initiator , stored-credential flags, processingInformation.authorizationOptions.initiator.merchantInitiatedTransaction.previousTransactionId (the stored transactions[].cybersourceDetails.networkTransactionId ), order and amount fields."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","3. Mapping to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#mapping-to-networktokendetails-6","PGW field CYBS response source Rule isNetworkToken processingInformation.paymentSolution true if 015 or 014 . false for any other value or if absent. tokenProvider processingInformation.paymentSolution 015 → VTS . 014 → MDES . Otherwise null . maskedTokenNumber paymentInformation.card.bin (token BIN, 6 digits) If isNetworkToken = true : the 6-digit BIN followed by 10 zeros (16 digits). Example: 522222 → 5222220000000000 . Otherwise null . tokenExpiryMonth Not in the CYBS response null tokenExpiryYear Not in the CYBS response null paymentAccountReference processorInformation.paymentAccountReferenceNumber Copy. null if absent."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › Requirements","Document","4. Processing","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#processing-8","Fill the object from the CYBS response of the same transaction. Apply to approved and declined transactions. If isNetworkToken = true and schemeTokenProvider is null : set schemeTokenProvider = tokenProvider . If schemeTokenProvider is not null : do not change it. A decline on the instrument identifier is final. Do not retry with the card number. Save on the transaction, if PGW does not save them today: processorInformation.responseCode , processorInformation.merchantAdvice.code , processorInformation.merchantAdvice.codeRaw . NT-X uses them."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C4 — CYBS token MIT","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-9","Token MIT, Visa, MID TEST-CYBS-01 : request has instrumentIdentifier.id , no card number, no CVV, the stored network transaction ID. Response paymentSolution = 015 . isNetworkToken = true , tokenProvider = VTS . Same for Mastercard: 014 , MDES (needs P3). Token without an instrument identifier: NT-C1 is called, then the MIT uses the new id . NT-C1 fails: the MIT is sent with the card number. isNetworkToken = false ."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-c5-cybs-capture-refund-void","Explorer: CYBS refund"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","Document","Background","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#background-10","Capture, refund and void follow a Pay, Authorize, CIT or MIT. They refer to the original CYBS payment. They do not carry a funding source. The CYBS response does not show network token data."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","Document","Goal","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#goal-10","PGW fills networkTokenDetails on capture, refund and void on CYBS."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","Document","Story summary","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#story-summary-10","Item Value Story ID NT-C5 Gateway CyberSource REST API Geidea endpoints POST /pgw/api/v1/direct/capture ; POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/refund ; POST /pgw/api/v3/direct/void CYBS API used Capture POST /pts/v2/payments/{id}/captures ; refund POST /pts/v2/payments/{id}/refunds ; void POST /pts/v2/payments/{id}/voids . No change to the requests. Entities written transactions[].networkTokenDetails Depends on NT-C2, NT-C3, NT-C4 Out of scope Geidea token record (no change in this story)."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","Document","Requirements","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#requirements-10","Request: no change. Copy networkTokenDetails from the original Pay or Authorization transaction of the order. If the original transaction has no object: set the object to null . Do not change the Geidea token record."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource) › NT-C5 — CYBS capture, refund, void","Document","Acceptance criteria","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-10","Capture of a network token Authorize: same networkTokenDetails as the Authorize. Refund and void: same. Capture of a card-number Authorize: isNetworkToken = false ."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-A1 — APEX network token keys (Waiting on APEX team)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-a1-apex-network-token-keys-waiting-on-apex-team","Not yet defined Proposal to discuss: send network token data to APEX in userData , in the existing key format ( TOKEN , CHANNEL_TYPE , AUTH_PERFORMED , AUTH_TXN_ID exist today). Key Values Example NETWORK_TOKEN Y / N 213NETWORK_TOKEN11Y NT_PROVIDER VTS / MDES 211NT_PROVIDER13VTS Questions: Is PAR needed? Display in Merchant Portal or reports? Does next-day clearing already carry a token indicator?"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","NT-X — Token status and retry control (Waiting on Risk & Compliance)","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#nt-x-token-status-and-retry-control-waiting-on-risk-compliance","Not yet defined Uses the NT-0 fields tokenStatus , tokenStatusReason , tokenStatusDate . Proposal for MPGS (to be confirmed): set INACTIVE after merchant advice code 03 , 21 or DE 39 04 , 14 , 15 , 41 , 43 , 46 , 62 , 78 on token CIT or MIT. Exclude 54 , 63 , 88 . Reject payments on an INACTIVE token with a new PGW code (\"Token inactive. Use another card.\"). CYBS values: waiting on Risk & Compliance."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization — PGW Dev Stories (MPGS and CyberSource)","Document","Open points","network-tokenization/docs/stories.html#open-points","Open point 1 # Point Story Status 1 When Generate and Use Network Token is switched ON for a CYBS MID (with Enable tokenization ON), PGW starts to create instrument identifiers and pay CIT/MIT with them. Confirm that a payment with an instrument identifier on a MID without CYBS token permission (P2) goes out as the card, so P2 is the PVT control. NT-C1, NT-C3, NT-C4 Merchant integration team / PGW engineering team to verify on a test MID Closed 17-Nov: CYBS maskedTokenNumber = token BIN + zero fill. CYBS capture, refund and void endpoints (refund and void proven on the test bench 14-Nov). Decision Manager MIT rule = operational, with Risk (P3). TMS headers and HTTP status (headers proven 11-Nov; 201 new / 200 existing per CYBS docs). Closed 19-Nov: master toggle = Generate and Use Network Token per MID, default OFF (rule 1); this replaces the 17-Nov decision \"no new toggle\". NT-C1 = one CYBS call only."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","network-tokenization/index.html","feature Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token Visa charges a PAN Integrity Fee on card-not-present Visa payments that do not use a Visa network token. In the UAE the network token requirement for cards on file started on 18-Apr-2026 and the fee on 17-Oct-2026. Phase 1: every saved-card payment (CIT and MIT) through PGW goes out with the network token, and PGW records it on the transaction."],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Two gateways, two different changes","network-tokenization/index.html#two-gateways-two-different-changes","The point to understand first. On MPGS the network token already works with today's PGW requests; PGW only has to record it. On CyberSource PGW sends the card number today, so PGW must pay differently : create an instrument identifier and pay with it. MPGS · record only"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token › Two gateways, two different changes","Hub","The payment request does not change","network-tokenization/index.html#the-payment-request-does-not-change","PGW already pays CIT and MIT with the MPGS token. With network tokens set up for the MID at MPGS, MPGS sends the network token by itself. Proven through PGW on 16–17 Nov for Visa and Mastercard. New: PGW reads sourceOfFunds.type = SCHEME_TOKEN and records it (NT-M1 to NT-M5). CyberSource · pay differently"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token › Two gateways, two different changes","Hub","PGW pays with an instrument identifier","network-tokenization/index.html#pgw-pays-with-an-instrument-identifier","Today PGW sends the card number on every CIT and MIT, so CYBS cannot use a network token. New: create the instrument identifier at save card (NT-C1) and pay with it and networkTokenOption = prefer (NT-C3, NT-C4). Proven in the 11-Nov POC and the 14-Nov test bench: Visa 015 , Mastercard 014 . Both: new object transactions[].networkTokenDetails returned to the merchant (NT-0). One master toggle per MID, default OFF (Rule 1). Story map"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Documents","network-tokenization/index.html#documents","PGW dev stories NT-0, MPGS NT-M1 to NT-M5, CYBS NT-C1 to NT-C5 written; NT-A1 (APEX) and NT-X (token status) parked v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Visual pages","network-tokenization/index.html#visual-pages","Token layers Card number, Geidea token, gateway token, network token: who holds what, how each is created, PAR open Payment explorer Sequence diagram per gateway: save card, CIT, MIT, refund; switch the toggles and the card's state; see what changes, how the payment goes to the scheme and what PGW records open What PGW records Gateway response to networkTokenDetails , field by field; where the merchant sees it; the Geidea token record open Switches and rollout PGW master toggle versus gateway set-up on MPGS and CYBS; rollout steps; partners on Geidea's MSO or their own open Not yet defined NT-A1 APEX keys, NT-X token status, open point 1, guest checkout POC parked and in POC"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Stories and where to see them","network-tokenization/index.html#stories","NT-0 · Data model and merchant APIs What PGW records · Token layers NT-M1 · MPGS token generation Explorer: save card NT-M2 · MPGS Pay (card number) Mapper · Explorer NT-M3 · MPGS token CIT Explorer · Not provisioned yet · Mapper NT-M4 · MPGS token MIT Explorer · Mapper NT-M5 · MPGS capture, refund, void Explorer · No sourceOfFunds NT-C1 · Create CYBS instrument identifier Explorer: save card (T1) · On demand (T2) · Failure NT-C2 · CYBS Pay (card number) Mapper NT-C3 · CYBS token CIT Explorer · Mapper NT-C4 · CYBS token MIT Explorer · Mapper NT-C5 · CYBS capture, refund, void Explorer NT-A1 · APEX keys (parked) Not yet defined NT-X · Token status and retry (parked) Not yet defined"],["Network Tokenization","Network Tokenization: saved-card payments with the scheme token","Hub","Proven in tests","network-tokenization/index.html#proven-in-tests","11-Nov · CYBS POC Instrument identifier created with the network token ACTIVE ; CIT and MIT approved on the network token (Visa 015 , Mastercard 014 ). Mastercard MIT needed the Decision Manager rule (P3). 14-Nov · CYBS test bench Save card, then CIT with the instrument identifier : 3DS ran, paymentSolution 014 , token BIN and PAR returned; refund and void. 16–17 Nov · MPGS through PGW Token CIT and MIT went out as SCHEME_TOKEN for Visa and Mastercard, with no change to PGW requests; 3DS, capture and refunds on the network token. 25-Nov · MPGS POC Token then pay, back to back : card number with asynchronous provisioning, network token with attempt-synchronous. Guest checkout POC"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html","visual page Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout What is outside the agreed stories today. Proposals are shown as proposals; nothing on this page is a requirement until the stories say so. Illustrative Reflects PGW dev stories v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026, and tests to 25-Nov-2026 Open points"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","NT-A1: APEX network token keys","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#nt-a1-apex-network-token-keys","PARKED · waiting on APEX team NT-A1 Proposal to discuss: send network token data to APEX in userData , in the format of the existing keys ( TOKEN , CHANNEL_TYPE , AUTH_PERFORMED , AUTH_TXN_ID ). Key Values Example NETWORK_TOKEN Y / N 213NETWORK_TOKEN11Y NT_PROVIDER VTS / MDES 211NT_PROVIDER13VTS"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout › NT-A1: APEX network token keys","Visual page","How the example reads (our reading; to confirm with the APEX team)","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#how-the-example-reads-our-reading-to-confirm-with-the-apex-t","2 digits in key length 13 key length NETWORK_TOKEN key 1 digits in value length 1 value length Y value"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout › NT-A1: APEX network token keys","Visual page","Questions","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#questions","Is PAR needed? Should it show in the Merchant Portal or reports? Does next-day clearing already carry a token indicator?"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","NT-X: token status and retry control","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#nt-x-token-status-and-retry-control","PARKED · waiting on Risk & Compliance NT-X PGW stops using a Geidea token after a \"do not retry\" decline. NT-0 already adds tokenStatus (default ACTIVE ), tokenStatusReason and tokenStatusDate ; nothing reads or changes them in this release. The CYBS stories save processorInformation.responseCode and merchantAdvice.code / codeRaw so NT-X can use them."],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout › NT-X: token status and retry control","Visual page","Proposal for MPGS (to be confirmed)","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#proposal-for-mpgs-to-be-confirmed","On token CIT or MIT Codes Proposed action Merchant advice code 03 , 21 Set the token INACTIVE DE 39 response code 04 , 14 , 15 , 41 , 43 , 46 , 62 , 78 Set the token INACTIVE DE 39 response code 54 , 63 , 88 Excluded: token stays ACTIVE Payment on an INACTIVE token new PGW code Reject: \"Token inactive. Use another card.\" Not defined: CYBS fields and values, CIT versus MIT differences, soft-decline retry limits."],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","Open point 1: no token permission on CYBS","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#open-point-1-no-token-permission-on-cybs","TO VERIFY · PGW engineering team, during build Open point 1 With the PGW toggle ON, PGW creates an instrument identifier and pays with it and networkTokenOption = prefer . On a MID without CYBS token permission (P2), the payment must go out as the card, so P2 stays the control. CYBS documentation says prefer falls back to the card. This is not tested on a Geidea MID yet. See the case in the Payment explorer · Switches"],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","Guest checkout: tokenize before pay","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#guest-checkout-poc","IN POC · not a work item Phase 1 covers saved cards (CIT and MIT). Visa's PAN Integrity Fee also applies to guest-checkout Visa payments that are not network-tokenized (from 17-Oct-2026 in the UAE). Visa's answer for guest checkout is Click to Pay. A POC on MPGS tests another route: create the gateway token for every new card before the payment, so the first payment can already go out with a network token. The question: can the network token exist in time when the payment follows straight after the token is created? run 1 · repository provisioning: asynchronous token pay 0.6 s: CARD NT ~30 s Payment approved but sent with the card number. The network token (VTS) appeared about 30 seconds later. Asynchronous provisioning loses the race. Card number run 2 · repository provisioning: attempt synchronous token + NT ~1 s pay: SCHEME_TOKEN Token creation took about 1 second and returned with the network token. The payment straight after went out as SCHEME_TOKEN . Network token Context. Geidea e-commerce payments run 3DS, so in a real flow the customer's 3DS time sits between token creation and payment. Visa test card, MPGS test MID TEST-MPGS-01 , 25-Nov-2026. Not tested on CyberSource. Whether this meets the guest-checkout requirement is not confirmed."],["Network Tokenization","Not yet defined: parked stories, open point, guest checkout","Visual page","Not in this release","network-tokenization/not-yet-defined.html#not-in-this-release","OUT OF SCOPE Token inquiry or token-state check before payment · CYBS network token webhooks and lifecycle updates · returning gateway tokens to merchants, or accepting them · MPGS API upgrade (version 80 is enough) · creating the instrument identifier inside the payment ( actionList: [\"TOKEN_CREATE\"] ) · CYBS customer and payment instrument tokens."],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html","visual page Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side Pick a gateway, a card, the switches and the saved card's state. The sequence shows each call between the merchant, PGW, the gateway and the scheme, what changes for PGW, and how the payment goes to the scheme: with the network token or with the card number. Illustrative Reflects PGW dev stories v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026 Story map Rules for every story Terms. Geidea token = the tokenId the merchant holds. Gateway token = MPGS token (MPGS) or instrument identifier, II (CyberSource). Network token = the token Visa (VTS) or Mastercard (MDES) issues for the card; the gateway sends it with a cryptogram. PGW never sees the full network token or the cryptogram. CIT = customer-initiated, MIT = merchant-initiated payment with a saved card. All identifiers are dummy values. Token layers explains the layers."],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","Try a case","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try-a-case","try MPGS: token CIT, Visa MPGS: token MIT, Mastercard MPGS: first payment, save card MPGS: network token not provisioned yet MPGS: PGW toggle OFF MPGS: MID without NT set-up MPGS: refund of a token CIT CYBS: first payment, save card CYBS: token CIT, Mastercard CYBS: token MIT, Visa CYBS: card saved before go-live CYBS: instrument identifier not created CYBS: PGW toggle OFF CYBS: MID without token permission CYBS: refund of a token CIT"],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","Settings","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#h-set","Gateway MPGS CyberSource Card Visa Mastercard Payment First payment, save card Token CIT Token MIT Refund of a token CIT PGW: Generate and Use Network Token ON OFF MPGS: network tokens set up for the MID (P1) Yes No Saved card on MPGS Network token provisioned Not provisioned yet MPGS: the gateway set-up decides if the network token is used. The PGW toggle decides only what PGW records. Rule 1"],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","Result","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#h-out","MPGS · Visa went to the scheme with Network token (VTS) fee exposure · PGW record No Visa PAN Integrity Fee PGW records it"],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","Sequence","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#h-seq","click a step for the payload Merchant / HPP Geidea PGW MPGS TEST-MPGS-01 Scheme VTS / MDES Token CIT: the customer pays with the saved card 1 POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token , initiatedBy = Payer (or HPP with tokenId ) NO CHANGE The merchant sends only the Geidea token: { \"tokenId\": \"0a1b2c3d-4e5f-6071-8293-a4b5c6d7e8f9\", \"initiatedBy\": \"Payer\" } 3DS runs as today. No change. 2 Pay with the MPGS token: sourceOfFunds.token = 0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9 NO CHANGE NT-M3 No change to the request. The MPGS token is the Geidea tokenId without dashes, in upper case (merchant-supplied token). { \"apiOperation\": \"PAY\", \"sourceOfFunds\": { \"token\": \"0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9\" } } 3 Authorisation with the VTS network token and a cryptogram GATEWAY The gateway swaps the gateway token for the network token and gets a cryptogram from VTS. PGW does not see either. Proven through PGW on 16–17 Nov for Visa and Mastercard CIT, MIT and 3DS on the network token. 4 Approved NO CHANGE 5 Payment response: sourceOfFunds.type = SCHEME_TOKEN NO CHANGE Response excerpt. Highlighted: the fields PGW reads. { \"result\": \"SUCCESS\", \"response\": { \"gatewayCode\": \"APPROVED\", \"acquirerCode\": \"00\" }, \"sourceOfFunds\": { \"type\": \"SCHEME_TOKEN\" , \"token\": \"0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9\", \"provided\": { \"card\": { \"brand\": \"VISA\" , \"deviceSpecificNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\" , \"deviceSpecificExpiry\": { \"month\": \"11\", \"year\": \"28\" } , \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" , \"storedOnFile\": \"STORED\" } } } } 6 Fill transactions[].networkTokenDetails (approved and declined) NEW NT-M3 7 First network token seen: set schemeTokenProvider = VTS on the Geidea token (only when it is null ) NEW NT-M3 8 Response, callback and order inquiry carry networkTokenDetails NEW NT-0 NO CHANGE today's behaviour CHANGED an existing call changes NEW build needed GATEWAY done by the gateway ASYNC in the background SKIPPED not done in this case"],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Visual page","What PGW records","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#h-rec","Field-by-field mapping transactions[].networkTokenDetails (returned to the merchant) { \"isNetworkToken\": true, \"tokenProvider\": \"VTS\", \"maskedTokenNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\", \"tokenExpiryMonth\": \"11\", \"tokenExpiryYear\": \"28\", \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" } Geidea token record (internal, not returned) Field Before After schemeTokenProvider null VTS tokenStatus ACTIVE ACTIVE tokenStatus is added now; nothing reads or changes it in this release (NT-X). Green rows changed in this case."],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: token CIT, Visa","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-cit",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: token MIT, Mastercard","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-mit",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: first payment, save card","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-save",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: network token not provisioned yet","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-pending",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: PGW toggle OFF","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-toggle-off",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: MID without NT set-up","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-no-nt",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: MPGS: refund of a token CIT","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=mpgs-refund",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: first payment, save card","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-save",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: token CIT, Mastercard","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-cit",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: token MIT, Visa","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-mit",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: card saved before go-live","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-old-card",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: instrument identifier not created","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-ii-fail",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: PGW toggle OFF","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-toggle-off",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: MID without token permission","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-no-permission",""],["Network Tokenization","Payment explorer: MPGS and CyberSource side by side","Scenario","Try it: CYBS: refund of a token CIT","network-tokenization/payment-explorer.html#try=cybs-refund",""],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","Visual page","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html","visual page Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used Two switches decide the outcome: one in PGW, one at the gateway. They do different things on MPGS and on CyberSource. The PGW switch is a safety switch for the rollout, per MID, default OFF. Illustrative Reflects PGW dev stories v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026 Rule 1: master toggle Prerequisites P1–P3"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","Visual page","The switches","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#the-switches","PGW configuration · per MID · default OFF"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › The switches","Visual page","Generate and Use Network Token","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#generate-and-use-network-token","The one master toggle for all NT work (Rule 1). Exists today; v1.1 gives it this meaning. A later release can remove it. PGW configuration · existing, unchanged"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › The switches","Visual page","Enable tokenization, CIT, MIT","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#enable-tokenization-cit-mit","Enable tokenization , CUSTOMER_INITIATED_TRANSACTIONS , MERCHANT_INITIATED_TRANSACTIONS still apply as today. MPGS · per MID and token repository (P1)"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › The switches","Visual page","Network tokens on MPGS","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#network-tokens-on-mpgs","MDES onboarding, Visa VTS via an existing TRID, Enable Network Tokens per merchant. Set by the merchant integration team. CYBS · per MID (P2)"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › The switches","Visual page","Token permission on CYBS","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#token-permission-on-cybs","Network token provisioning on the vault; Visa and Mastercard token permission per MID. PGW configuration · not used"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › The switches","Visual page","Use Network Token, Send NT to merchant","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#use-network-token-send-nt-to-merchant","Exist from an earlier project. Not used in this release."],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","Visual page","Who decides: click a row","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#who-decides",""],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › Who decides: click a row","Visual page","MPGS","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#mpgs-matrix","token CIT or MIT PGW toggle MPGS set-up (P1) Payment goes with PGW records ON Yes Network token Yes OFF Yes Network token null ON No Card number Yes OFF No Card number null The target state. MPGS already pays with the network token; PGW records it (NT-M3, NT-M4). Try it"],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › Who decides: click a row","Visual page","CyberSource","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#cybs-matrix","token CIT or MIT PGW toggle Token permission (P2) Payment goes with PGW records ON Yes Network token Yes OFF Yes Card number null ON No Expected card (not verified) Yes OFF No Card number null The target state. PGW creates the instrument identifier and pays with it; CYBS uses the network token (NT-C1, NT-C3, NT-C4). Try it Both tables assume the existing tokenization, CIT and MIT toggles are ON. See a case in the Payment explorer ."],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","Visual page","Rollout","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#rollout","Release with the toggle OFF on every MID. PGW behaves exactly as today: no instrument identifiers, CYBS CIT and MIT with the card number, networkTokenDetails = null . Switch ON for the production test MID and test in production. Without the toggle, a fault would hit every card-on-file merchant at release and the only fix would be a code rollback. Switch ON per card-on-file MID. The MID list is reviewed with Business and Risk & Compliance first. Gateway set-up (P1, P2) must be in place for the MID. New card-on-file merchants: network tokens are mandatory. Agreed in the 19-Nov mandate alignment meeting. A later release removes the toggle. Network tokens then apply wherever save card, CIT or MIT is enabled."],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used","Visual page","Partners that connect to the gateway directly","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#partners",""],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › Partners that connect to the gateway directly","Visual page","On Geidea's MSO","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#on-geidea-s-mso","Geidea switches network tokens on for their MIDs at the gateway, sends an advisory, and spot-checks their CIT and MIT. The PGW toggle does not apply: these partners do not pay through PGW."],["Network Tokenization","Switches and rollout: who decides if a network token is used › Partners that connect to the gateway directly","Visual page","On their own MSO","network-tokenization/switches-and-rollout.html#on-their-own-mso","Risk & Compliance sends an advisory. The partner generates and uses network tokens on its own set-up."],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what","Visual page","Token layers: who holds what","network-tokenization/token-layers.html","visual page Token layers: who holds what One saved card has up to four identities. The merchant only ever holds the Geidea token. The scheme fee depends on the last layer: did the gateway send a network token to Visa, or the card number? Illustrative Reflects PGW dev stories v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026 NT-0 NT-C1"],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what","Visual page","The four layers of one saved card","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#the-four-layers","Gateway MPGS CyberSource Card Visa Mastercard See it as All layers Merchant Geidea PGW Gateway Scheme and issuer Card number PAN 411111xxxxxx1111 Held by the Geidea vault (PGW) and the gateway. Sent to the gateway on card-number payments. PGW maps it to Geidea token tokenId 0a1b2c3d-4e5f-6071-8293-a4b5c6d7e8f9 Held by PGW and the merchant. The only token the merchant sends. One per card per merchant and gateway. PGW pays MPGS with MPGS token gateway token · exists today 0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9 Created by PGW at save card ( SendToken ): the Geidea tokenId without dashes, upper case. Stored by MPGS. the gateway swaps it for Network token VTS · plus a cryptogram per payment 489537xxxxxx0001 Issued by Visa (VTS), held by the gateway. PGW sees only the masked number and expiry in the payment response. Green edge: the layer that avoids the Visa fee. Red edge: the layer the mandate wants out of the payment. Values are dummy; the network token number is shown as PGW records it (masked)."],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what","Visual page","How the layers are created","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#how-the-layers-are-created","1 · save card"],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what › How the layers are created","Visual page","Card saved","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#timeline","The customer pays with the card number and ticks save card. PGW creates the Geidea token. No change. 2 · save card"],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what › How the layers are created","Visual page","MPGS token","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#timeline","PGW sends SendToken with its own token value. No change. New: PGW reads schemeToken.provider (NT-M1). 3 · async, 20–30 s in tests"],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what › How the layers are created","Visual page","Network token","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#timeline","With network tokens set up for the MID (P1), MPGS asks VTS for a network token. Existing MPGS tokens get one automatically. 4 · each CIT / MIT"],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what › How the layers are created","Visual page","Payment","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#timeline","PGW pays with the MPGS token, as today. MPGS sends the network token and cryptogram. New: PGW records it (NT-M3, NT-M4)."],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what","Visual page","PAR: one value per card","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#par-one-value-per-card","The Payment Account Reference (PAR) is the same for the card number and every network token of that card. It lets Geidea link payments made with the card number and with a network token to one card, without storing the card number. PGW copies it to paymentAccountReference on every transaction where the gateway returns it, on card-number payments too (NT-M2, NT-C2). Dummy PARs on these pages: Visa V0010000000000000000000000001 , Mastercard 5001TESTPAR000000000000000002 ."],["Network Tokenization","Token layers: who holds what","Visual page","An analogy","network-tokenization/token-layers.html#an-analogy","Card number The house key. Whoever copies it can open the door anywhere. Geidea token The ticket the merchant gets at the key desk. Useless outside Geidea. Gateway token The gateway's locker number for the key. MPGS uses Geidea's ticket number as the locker number; CyberSource gives its own number (the instrument identifier). Network token A copy of the key, cut by Visa or Mastercard, that only opens this door for this merchant. Each use needs a one-time code (the cryptogram). Visa charges a fee when the house key is used instead."],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html","visual page What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails Both gateways fill the same six-field object, from different response fields. Pick a response and follow each field through its rule. The object is written once per transaction and returned to the merchant. Illustrative Reflects PGW dev stories v1.2 · 25-Nov-2026 NT-0 NT-M3 mapping NT-C3 mapping"],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","Mapper","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#mapper","try MPGS token CIT, Visa MPGS token MIT, Mastercard MPGS Pay with card number MPGS response without sourceOfFunds CYBS token CIT, Mastercard (014) CYBS token MIT, Visa (015) CYBS Pay with card number"],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails › Mapper","Visual page","Gateway response","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#h-resp","MPGS v80 · excerpt { \"result\": \"SUCCESS\", \"response\": { \"gatewayCode\": \"APPROVED\", \"acquirerCode\": \"00\" }, \"sourceOfFunds\": { \"type\": \"SCHEME_TOKEN\" , \"token\": \"0A1B2C3D4E5F60718293A4B5C6D7E8F9\", \"provided\": { \"card\": { \"brand\": \"VISA\" , \"deviceSpecificNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\" , \"deviceSpecificExpiry\": { \"month\": \"11\" , \"year\": \"28\" } , \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" , \"storedOnFile\": \"STORED\" } } } }"],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails › Mapper","Visual page","Rules","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#rules-2","NT-M3 Source value Rule PGW field \"SCHEME_TOKEN\" true if SCHEME_TOKEN, else false isNetworkToken true \"VISA\" if network token: VISA → VTS, MASTERCARD → MDES; else null tokenProvider \"VTS\" \"489537xxxxxx0001\" copy; null if absent maskedTokenNumber \"489537xxxxxx0001\" \"11\" copy; null if absent tokenExpiryMonth \"11\" \"28\" copy; null if absent tokenExpiryYear \"28\" \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" copy; null if absent paymentAccountReference \"V0010000000000000000000000001\""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails › Mapper","Visual page","PGW transaction","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#pgw-transaction","\"networkTokenDetails\": { \"isNetworkToken\": true, \"tokenProvider\": \"VTS\", \"maskedTokenNumber\": \"489537xxxxxx0001\", \"tokenExpiryMonth\": \"11\", \"tokenExpiryYear\": \"28\", \"paymentAccountReference\": \"V0010000000000000000000000001\" } If the Geidea token has schemeTokenProvider = null , PGW sets it to VTS on a token CIT or MIT."],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","The object","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#the-object","Field Type Values MPGS source CYBS source isNetworkToken Boolean true / false sourceOfFunds.type = SCHEME_TOKEN processingInformation.paymentSolution = 015 or 014 tokenProvider String VTS / MDES / null …card.brand : VISA → VTS , MASTERCARD → MDES 015 → VTS , 014 → MDES maskedTokenNumber String masked / null …card.deviceSpecificNumber , copied paymentInformation.card.bin + 10 zeros tokenExpiryMonth String e.g. 11 / null …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.month not returned: null tokenExpiryYear String e.g. 28 / null …card.deviceSpecificExpiry.year not returned: null paymentAccountReference String PAR / null …card.paymentAccountReference processorInformation.paymentAccountReferenceNumber …card = sourceOfFunds.provided.card . MPGS REST API version 80. NT-0 requirement 1"],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","Which transactions carry it","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#which-transactions-carry-it","Transaction Object MPGS CYBS Pay, Authorization (card number) yes from the response (NT-M2) from the response (NT-C2) Pay, Authorization (token CIT, MIT) yes from the response (NT-M3, NT-M4) from the response (NT-C3, NT-C4) Capture, Refund, Void yes from the response; no sourceOfFunds : copy from the original always copied from the original Authentication no never carries the object Before this release, or toggle OFF null NT-0 2.4 and criterion 5 Approved and declined transactions both get the object. Written once; never updated."],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","Where the merchant sees it","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#where-the-merchant-sees-it","Merchant API Path Order inquiry GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order/{orderId} order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails Callback to callbackUrl order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay response order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails POST /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token response order.transactions[].networkTokenDetails An addition only: existing fields do not change. The token record fields below are not returned."],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Visual page","The Geidea token record (internal)","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#the-geidea-token-record","Field Values Default Written by Update rule schemeTokenProvider VTS / MDES / null null NT-M1 at token creation; NT-M3, NT-M4, NT-C3, NT-C4 at the first network token payment Once set, never changed cybsInstrumentIdentifierId 19 digits / null null NT-C1 Replaced if CYBS returns a different id (logged) networkTokenState e.g. ACTIVE / null null NT-C1 ( tokenizedCard.state ) With the identifier tokenStatus ACTIVE / INACTIVE ACTIVE nothing in this release For NT-X ( not yet defined ) tokenStatusReason , tokenStatusDate text, UAE time null nothing in this release For NT-X NT-0 requirements 4 and 5"],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: MPGS token CIT, Visa","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=mpgs-cit-visa",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: MPGS token MIT, Mastercard","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=mpgs-mit-mc",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: MPGS Pay with card number","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=mpgs-card",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: MPGS response without sourceOfFunds","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=mpgs-no-sof",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: CYBS token CIT, Mastercard (014)","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=cybs-cit-mc",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: CYBS token MIT, Visa (015)","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=cybs-mit-visa",""],["Network Tokenization","What PGW records: gateway response to networkTokenDetails","Scenario","Try it: CYBS Pay with card number","network-tokenization/what-pgw-records.html#try=cybs-card",""],["Split Payout","Advice lifecycle","Visual page","Advice lifecycle","split-payout/advice-lifecycle.html","visual · split payout Advice lifecycle A split advice tells APEX how to pay one flagged transaction. This page follows an advice from the moment it is sent to the moment the money moves: its statuses at APEX, what PGW records, and what happens to the money each day. Illustrative Reflects product doc v1.6 (6.3–6.5, 7.3, 7.5) and PGW stories v0.5 (SP-7 to SP-9) Read the requirement → End-to-end view → Stories: SP-7 → SP-8 → SP-9 → Terms: partner = the merchant (MID) with split payout on; vendor = a payee of the split. Action A creates an advice at APEX, U replaces it. PGW sends A in real time for a split sent with the order or a Payout Advice API NEW. An UPDATE is not sent in real time: the day-end file carries it and APEX overwrites the earlier advice (agreed with APEX on 23-Nov; stories v0.5 and doc v1.6 still describe a real-time U). APEX advice fields and statuses are drafts until the Emcrey spec (P3)."],["Split Payout","Advice lifecycle","Visual page","The statuses at APEX","split-payout/advice-lifecycle.html#statuses","NOT FINAL · TRANSACTION HELD · UPDATE VIA DAY-END FILE FINAL · NO FURTHER UPDATES A, checks pass A before the transaction A, a structural check fails transaction arrives unmatched at day end amount check fails U in day-end file valid, paid on P P + N days, no valid advice no advice transaction held PENDING_MATCH before the transaction CREATED awaiting validation REJECTED reason code recorded PROCESSED paid out RELEASED after N days"],["Split Payout","Advice lifecycle › The statuses at APEX","Visual page","CREATED","split-payout/advice-lifecycle.html#sd","Received and passed structural checks; awaiting amount validation and payout. Money Held until the payout. Partner can UPDATE with the latest advice ID, on the transaction date only; it reaches APEX in the day-end file and overwrites this advice. PGW shows ACCEPTED (from the real-time response). Source: product doc 6.5 Source: product doc 6.5 Advice statuses · 6.4 · 6.3"],["Split Payout","Advice lifecycle","Visual page","Day by day","split-payout/advice-lifecycle.html#days","Split with the order Deferred split Rejected, then corrected Advice before the transaction Released after N days APEX not reachable The partner sends the legs in Create Session. PGW sends the advice the moment the payment succeeds. When Partner PGW APEX APEX status PGW record Money Day 0 Creates a session with the legs; the customer pays. Checks the split (SP-6). Federates the transaction with splitPayout = Y. Sends advice A in real time (SP-7). Holds the transaction. Structural checks pass. CREATED ACCEPTED held Day 0, after midnight — Day-end file carries advice A (SP-9). File matches the real-time advice: no action. CREATED included in file held Before P — — Amount validation: Rule 1, Rule 2 and single payout pass. CREATED — held P Sees the result in the split payout report. — Pays each vendor, settles the residual. PROCESSED — paid out ← Previous Next → Show all Step 1 of 4 Days are illustrative. Day 0 = payment day. P = the transaction's scheduled payout date under the MID's payout schedule. N = days set on the partner MID (can be 0)."],["Split Payout","Advice lifecycle","Visual page","What the partner can still do","split-payout/advice-lifecycle.html#what-the-partner-can-still-do","APEX status Payout Advice API NEW Payout Advice API UPDATE Update in the day-end file Money no advice Yes , if the order was created with deferredSplit — — held PENDING_MATCH No : a split exists Yes , with the latest advice ID, on the transaction date only Overwrites the advice held CREATED No Yes , with the latest advice ID, on the transaction date only Overwrites the advice held until payout REJECTED No Yes , on the transaction date only: this is how a rejection is corrected Overwrites the advice held PROCESSED No PGW stores it; APEX refuses it Refused : final paid out RELEASED No PGW stores it; APEX refuses it Refused : final released to the partner Source: product doc 7.3 · 6.4 · SP-8 section 2 . Rejections at each step: What can go wrong . The day-end file route for updates was agreed with APEX on 23-Nov; stories v0.5 and doc v1.6 still describe a real-time U. An UPDATE is accepted on the transaction date only (rule of 24-Nov); one sent after that day’s file is rejected."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","1. Introduction","split-payout/docs/product.html","v1.6 10-Nov-2026 Source: Vendor Payout Service - MVP v1.6 (10-Nov-2026).docx Product and implementation requirements · Ecomm (PGW) · Version 1.6 · 10-Nov-2026 1. Introduction The Vendor Payout Service lets a partner (a Geidea merchant) instruct Geidea to pay part of each sale to its own vendors (suppliers). The customer pays once, on the partner’s MID, and the transaction is authorized and cleared with the scheme exactly as today. After settlement, Geidea transfers each vendor’s share to the vendor’s own UAE bank account under Geidea’s domestic fund transfer service and settles the remainder to the partner. This is the working requirements document for implementation. It carries the approved product design and sets out the work items for PGW and APEX, and is kept current as solutioning progresses with the APEX team and its platform vendor."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","Scope","split-payout/docs/product.html#scope","Channel: Ecomm through PGW only. Split modes: Dynamic, Fixed and Profile based. Currency: AED only. The partner and its vendors are paid in AED. Vendors: UAE businesses holding a business registration (trade license). Payouts are domestic only (UAE IBANs, no cross-border). Partners: select large partners, approved case by case. Unlicensed aggregators are excluded. Expected volume: 10 to 20 partners a year."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","Terms used in this document","split-payout/docs/product.html#terms-used-in-this-document","Term Meaning Partner The Geidea merchant that sells to the customer and instructs Geidea how to split the proceeds. Holds a normal Geidea MID. Vendor / beneficiary A business the partner pays out to. Defined in APEX as a vendor definition, not a MID. Beneficiary ID Unique ID APEX generates for each vendor definition. The only vendor identifier the partner and PGW use. Split advice The instruction for one transaction: which beneficiaries receive how much. Split flag Marker PGW sets on a transaction in its federation to APEX when a split advice is expected. APEX holds only flagged transactions. Deferred split Order created without split detail, where the partner declares (deferredSplit) that it will send the advice later through the Payout Advice API. Residual What remains of the partner’s settlement after vendor payouts and remittance fees; settled to the partner. Remittance fee Fee charged per payout (each vendor transfer and the partner’s own payout). N Days, set per partner MID, after which a flagged transaction without a valid advice is released to the partner. EOD split advice file Day-end file from PGW to APEX carrying the day’s advices; backup and update channel to the real-time API. PENDING_MATCH Status of an advice APEX received before the transaction itself reached APEX."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","2. Use Cases","split-payout/docs/product.html#use-cases","View it visually Use case Example Typical mode Marketplace A customer buys from several sellers in one checkout; each seller receives its share. Dynamic Delivery platform An order payment is shared between the restaurant or store and the platform. Dynamic Aggregator with standard terms An insurance aggregator applies a different, pre-agreed split per insurance provider. Profile Standing revenue share A business always passes the same share of every sale to a supplier. Fixed"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","3. Solution Overview","split-payout/docs/product.html#solution-overview","The solution has two parts. The operational setup is done once per partner and per vendor, by people, through agreed operational routes. The transaction and payout flow runs on every transaction, entirely in Geidea systems. Figure 1 shows both end to end. Section 5 describes the operational setup, and sections 6 and 7 what APEX and PGW need to deliver."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 3. Solution Overview","Document","3.1 Solution at a glance","split-payout/docs/product.html#solution-at-a-glance","End-to-end view Figure 1. From partner setup to vendor payout"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 3. Solution Overview","Document","3.2 Split modes","split-payout/docs/product.html#split-modes","View it visually Each partner MID uses one split mode. Mode How the split is defined What the partner sends Dynamic The partner sends the split with each transaction. Vendor legs in the order creation request, or later through the Payout Advice API (deferred split). Fixed One split template, configured by Geidea in PGW, applies to every transaction. Nothing. PGW applies the template to every order. Profile Geidea configures a catalog of split templates in PGW, each with a profile ID. A profile ID in the order creation request, or later through the Payout Advice API (deferred split)."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 3.2 Split modes","Document","Rules common to all modes","split-payout/docs/product.html#rules-common-to-all-modes","A leg names a beneficiary ID and a value. The value is either an amount or a percentage of the gross transaction amount , never both. All legs of one advice use the same split type (all amounts or all percentages). Percentages are converted to amounts by APEX, not by PGW. Each amount is rounded to 2 decimals; the partner’s residual absorbs the rounding difference. Templates and profiles are configured by Geidea only. The partner has no access to split configuration. A split advice carries beneficiary IDs and values only. Bank details always come from Geidea’s records, never from the partner’s request."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 3. Solution Overview","Document","3.3 Design principles","split-payout/docs/product.html#design-principles","Geidea controls who is paid. Vendors are verified and defined by Geidea. A partner can only pay vendors defined against its own MID. A vendor is not a merchant. Vendors are vendor definitions in APEX, not MIDs. They have no products, channels, users or portal access. Payouts never exceed the partner’s net. The partner’s residual can never go negative and no vendor leg can be zeroed by commission or fees. All or nothing. An advice is processed in full or rejected in full. A partial split is never paid. Fail safe, not fail open. PGW flags every split transaction in its federation to APEX. APEX holds flagged transactions until a valid advice is processed, so a missing or failed advice delays the partner’s settlement rather than paying vendor money to the partner. Real-time advice, settlement-time payout. Split advices reach APEX in real time through an API, with a day-end file as backup and update channel. Payouts still run with settlement. Fully automated. Vendor payouts and the partner’s residual run without any manual finance step. The scheme transaction is unchanged. Authorization and clearing work as today; federation to APEX only gains the split flag. Risk approves every partner. The service is never enabled by default."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","4. Money Flow","split-payout/docs/product.html#money-flow","View it visually"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 4. Money Flow","Document","4.1 How funds move","split-payout/docs/product.html#how-funds-move","APEX calculates the partner’s settlement for the transaction and deducts Geidea’s MDR and VAT on the MDR. The remainder is the partner’s net. APEX makes the vendor payouts from the partner’s net. Whether a separate staging account is used, or APEX posts the entries directly from the merchant payout account, is to be defined by Finance. For a transaction with a valid split advice, APEX calculates each vendor’s payout: split amount (converted from a percentage of the gross transaction amount where needed), minus the commission configured on the vendor definition, if any, minus the remittance fee when the partner MID is set to deduct it from vendor payouts, rounded to 2 decimals. A remittance fee is charged for each payout: every vendor transfer and the partner’s own payout of its residual. It is configured on the partner MID, with any applicable VAT. For vendor transfers, an option on the partner MID sets who bears the fee: the partner (deducted from its residual) or each vendor (deducted from that vendor’s payout). The fee on the partner’s own payout is always deducted from its residual. Commission deducted from a vendor’s leg stays with the partner and reaches it in its residual. APEX transfers each vendor’s net payout to its IBAN and settles the residual to the partner. Geidea’s revenue on the transaction is its MDR. Geidea invoices the partner VAT on its MDR for the full transaction amount, however the transaction is split; any invoicing between the partner and its vendors is the partner’s own matter. The movement of funds between accounts, its accounting, and VAT handling on vendor commission and remittance fees are to be defined by Finance."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 4. Money Flow","Document","4.2 Worked example","split-payout/docs/product.html#worked-example","View it visually Transaction AED 1,000. Geidea MDR 1% (VAT on MDR left out for simplicity). An amount split across three vendors; two have a commission configured. A remittance fee of AED 1.00 per payout (illustrative) is set on the partner MID. The transaction ends in four payouts: three to the vendors and one to the partner."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 4.2 Worked example","Document","Option 1 – partner bears the transfer cost of all payouts","split-payout/docs/product.html#option-1-partner-bears-the-transfer-cost-of-all-payouts","Vendor Split amount Commission Commission amount Net payout Vendor A 500.00 2.00% 10.00 490.00 Vendor B 300.00 1.50% 4.50 295.50 Vendor C 100.00 None 0.00 100.00 Total 900.00 14.50 885.50 Partner settlement AED Transaction amount less Geidea MDR (1,000.00 − 10.00) 990.00 Less: net payouts to vendors (payouts 1 to 3) 885.50 Less: remittance fees (4 payouts × 1.00) 4.00 Residual paid to the partner (payout 4: 90.00 unallocated after MDR + 14.50 commission − 4.00 remittance fees) 100.50"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 4.2 Worked example","Document","Option 2 – each vendor bears its own transfer cost","split-payout/docs/product.html#option-2-each-vendor-bears-its-own-transfer-cost","The same transaction, with the partner MID set to deduct the remittance fee from each vendor’s payout. The fee on the partner’s own payout is still charged to the partner. Vendor Split amount Commission amount Remittance fee Net payout Vendor A 500.00 10.00 1.00 489.00 Vendor B 300.00 4.50 1.00 294.50 Vendor C 100.00 0.00 1.00 99.00 Total 900.00 14.50 3.00 882.50 Partner settlement AED Transaction amount less Geidea MDR (1,000.00 − 10.00) 990.00 Less: net payouts to vendors (payouts 1 to 3) 882.50 Less: remittance fees deducted from vendor payouts, to Geidea (3 × 1.00) 3.00 Less: remittance fee on the partner’s payout (1 × 1.00) 1.00 Residual paid to the partner (payout 4: 90.00 unallocated after MDR + 14.50 commission − 1.00 remittance fee) 103.50"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 4. Money Flow","Document","4.3 Outcomes","split-payout/docs/product.html#outcomes","Money flow: outcomes What can go wrong: after payout Situation What happens Transaction not flagged for split Settles to the partner through the normal process, after Geidea’s MDR. Flagged, valid advice processed Vendors receive their net payouts; the partner receives the residual. Flagged, advice rejected Nothing is paid to vendors; the transaction stays held. The rejection and its reason appear in the split payout report. The partner may send a corrected, complete advice through the Payout Advice API. Flagged, no advice received The transaction stays held (for example, a deferred split the partner never sent, or an advice lost in transit and not in the day-end file). Flagged, no valid advice within N days Released to the partner after Geidea’s MDR, and listed in an exception report for Operations and Finance. N is set per partner MID, can be zero, and counts from the transaction’s scheduled payout date. Advice received before the transaction Parked as PENDING_MATCH and linked when the transaction arrives; rejected with a reason if still unmatched at day end. Advice in API but missing in the day-end file Marked as mismatched; settlement held until resolved. Transfer to a vendor fails Existing exception process: retry up to the configured limit, then an exception record, with the case shown in the split payout report. Geidea contacts the partner only, never the vendor."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","5. Partner and Vendor Enablement (Operational)","split-payout/docs/product.html#partner-and-vendor-enablement-operational","View it visually Partner and vendor setup is operational. It is handled by the teams below through agreed operational routes (for example, an email from Business carrying the vendor details), and is detailed in the Operations SOP. No system build is needed for these steps in the MVP."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 5. Partner and Vendor Enablement (Operational)","Document","5.1 Partner eligibility and agreement","split-payout/docs/product.html#partner-eligibility-and-agreement","The service is offered only to select large partners, case by case. Unlicensed aggregators are excluded. Business presents each partner request and its business case to Risk. Risk reviews and approves the partner before any onboarding; the service is never enabled by default. The partner agreement is revisited by Business with Legal so that it covers the payout service and its liabilities: dispute and chargeback liability, refunds and chargebacks deducted from the partner, recovery of any shortfall, and terms related to domestic fund transfer processing."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 5. Partner and Vendor Enablement (Operational)","Document","5.2 Setup steps","split-payout/docs/product.html#setup-steps","View it visually # Step Done by Result 1 Request the service and share the vendors’ details and documents (business registration, relationship or contract with the partner, IBAN), the split configuration and any vendor commission. Partner Request with Business 2 Present the partner request and its business case to Risk. Business Request with Risk 3 Review and approve the partner and its business case. Risk Partner approved 4 Onboard each vendor once: collect and check the due diligence documents (business registration, IBAN in the business’s name, agreement or contract with the partner) and keep them on record; screen the beneficiary. Screening hits go to Risk under the existing process. Operations Vendors verified 5 Create the vendor definitions, linked to the partner MID with IBAN and any commission. Enable split payout on the partner MID with remittance fee, fee-bearer option and N. Share the beneficiary IDs with the PGW integration team. APEX team Beneficiary IDs 6 Enable split payout on the partner MID and configure the split mode, template or profiles, and beneficiary IDs (section 7.1). PGW integration team Partner configured 7 Share the beneficiary IDs and the API specs with the partner and support its integration. PGW integration team Partner integrated 8 Go live. Partner Live Due diligence and screening are done once, when a vendor is onboarded, not on every payout. The documents are kept on record to support each payout (for example, under the Central Bank travel rule). New vendors, changes to a vendor’s details or commission, and deactivation follow the same operational route. Vendors have no portal access; Geidea communicates with the partner only."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","6. APEX","split-payout/docs/product.html#apex","This section sets out what APEX needs to deliver. How each item is built, including the API and file formats, is for the APEX team to define with its platform vendor; structures shown here are the current working proposal."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.1 Vendor definition","split-payout/docs/product.html#vendor-definition","APEX holds a vendor definition for each vendor, identified by a unique beneficiary ID generated by APEX. A vendor definition is not a MID. It holds at least the vendor’s name and IBAN, and is linked to the partner MID, so a partner can only pay its own vendors. A commission (fixed or percentage) can be set at vendor level when the partner requests it. A vendor can be activated and deactivated; a deactivated vendor can no longer be paid. Vendor definitions are created and maintained by the APEX team from the operational setup (section 5)."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.2 Split payout enablement on the partner MID","split-payout/docs/product.html#split-payout-enablement-on-the-partner-mid","Setting Purpose Split payout enabled Identifies a partner MID whose settlement follows the money flow in section 4. Remittance fee Fee per payout (each vendor transfer and the partner’s own payout), with any applicable VAT. Fee bearer for vendor transfers Partner (deducted from residual) or vendor (deducted from each vendor’s payout). The fee on the partner’s own payout is always the partner’s. N (days) Days after which a flagged transaction without a valid advice is released to the partner. Can be zero. The payout cap (%) does not apply to split payout partners. The payout schedule (scheme schedule, matched status or advance payout, as configured on the MID) continues to apply."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.3 Hold of flagged transactions","split-payout/docs/product.html#hold-of-flagged-transactions","Advice lifecycle: released after N days APEX receives the split flag with the transaction in PGW’s federation (real-time Create Transaction API and the day-end transaction file). Unflagged transactions of a split-enabled MID settle to the partner as normal. A flagged transaction is held from payout until a valid advice is PROCESSED for it. If no valid advice is processed within N days of the transaction’s scheduled payout date — whether the advice was never received or was rejected and not corrected — APEX releases the transaction to the partner after Geidea’s MDR, sets the advice status to RELEASED where one exists, and lists the transaction in an exception report for Operations and Finance. The timer runs on the flagged transaction, not on an advice record."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.4 Split advice intake","split-payout/docs/product.html#split-advice-intake","Advice lifecycle APEX receives split advices from PGW through two channels, following the same model as transaction federation today."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6.4 Split advice intake","Document","Real-time Split Advice API","split-payout/docs/product.html#real-time-split-advice-api","PGW sends each advice as soon as it has one: at payment success for a split sent with the order, and on every Payout Advice API call. One request can carry several advices. Working structure (APEX to finalise): <SplitAdvices> <SplitAdvice> <Action>A | U</Action> <!-- A = create, U = update --> <Merchant>partner MID</Merchant> <Transaction_Reference>interSystemID</Transaction_Reference> <Split_Rules> <Split_Rule> <BeneficiaryID>BEN000301</BeneficiaryID> <Percentage></Percentage> <!-- either Percentage ... --> <Amount>600.00</Amount> <!-- ... or Amount, not both --> </Split_Rule> </Split_Rules> </SplitAdvice> </SplitAdvices> PGW / product term APEX structure Partner (split-enabled merchant) <Merchant> MID Beneficiary / beneficiaryId <BeneficiaryID> (APEX may name it PartnerID; “partner” in this document means the merchant) Payout Advice API NEW / UPDATE <Action> A / U interSystemID <Transaction_Reference> Partner residual Settlement to the merchant The API runs the structural checks synchronously and returns them in the response: split enabled on the MID; every beneficiary found, active and linked to the MID; MID matches the transaction; transaction carries the split flag; one of percentage or amount per rule; A only when no advice exists for the transaction; U only when the existing advice is CREATED, REJECTED or PENDING_MATCH. Amount validation runs later (section 6.5)."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6.4 Split advice intake","Document","Transaction not yet on APEX","split-payout/docs/product.html#transaction-not-yet-on-apex","Advice lifecycle: advice before the transaction An advice that arrives before its transaction is not rejected. APEX parks it as PENDING_MATCH and links it when the transaction arrives. If still unmatched at day end, it is rejected with a reason code so the partner sees it in the split payout report."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6.4 Split advice intake","Document","Day-end split advice file","split-payout/docs/product.html#day-end-split-advice-file","Advice lifecycle: APEX not reachable What can go wrong: day-end file PGW sends a day-end file after the Ecomm cut-off (midnight) with every advice of the day, including updates. It is the backup to the API and the channel for updates. APEX reconciles it against the API: Case APEX action Advice in the API and in the file, same split No action. Advice in the file with a different split Overwrite with the file’s split and process. Advice in the file, not received over the API Process as new (covers an API failure). Advice received over the API, missing in the file Mark as mismatched and hold settlement until resolved. No file received Process with what was received over the API. The file carries a trailer with the record count. PGW sends an empty file with a zero count on days with no advices, so APEX can tell “no advices today” from “file not received”. File format to be defined by APEX."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.5 Amount validation","split-payout/docs/product.html#amount-validation","Money flow: amount validation What can go wrong: amount validation Run by APEX as a scheduled process once pricing is available (in-call validation if the platform vendor can support it). Any failure rejects the whole advice with a reason code. Rule Check Rule 1 – partner residual not negative net − Σ advised beneficiary amounts + Σ beneficiary commissions − remittance fees borne by the partner ≥ 0 (net = transaction amount − MDR − VAT on MDR) Rule 2 – every leg above zero advised amount − commission − remittance fee (only when the vendor bears it) > 0, for every beneficiary Single payout A transaction is never paid out twice. “Split ≤ net” is not a sufficient check: it passes advices that leave the partner negative once fees are taken, and rejects valid advices where vendor commission covers the gap. Examples (transaction 1,000, MDR 10, VAT 0.50, net 989.50, fee 1.00 per payout, three beneficiaries at 2% commission): Fee bearer Advised Commission Partner residual Result Partner 400 / 300 / 250 = 950 19.00 989.50 − 950 + 19 − 4 = 54.50 Valid Partner 400 / 300 / 300 = 1,000 20.00 989.50 − 1,000 + 20 − 4 = 5.50 Valid (above net, covered by commission) Partner 400 / 300 / 310 = 1,010 20.20 989.50 − 1,010 + 20.20 − 4 = −4.30 Reject (Rule 1) Vendor 400 / 300 / 250 = 950 19.00 989.50 − 950 + 19 − 1 = 57.50 Valid; vendors receive 391 / 293 / 244 Vendor one leg of 0.80 0.02 — Reject (Rule 2): 0.80 − 0.02 − 1.00 = −0.22 Either one leg of 4.00, fixed commission 5.00 5.00 — Reject (Rule 2)"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6.5 Amount validation","Document","Advice statuses","split-payout/docs/product.html#advice-statuses","Advice lifecycle: statuses Status Meaning CREATED Received and passed structural checks; awaiting amount validation and payout. PENDING_MATCH Received before the transaction reached APEX. REJECTED Failed a check; reason code recorded. Can be corrected with U within N days. PROCESSED Paid out to vendors and residual settled. No further updates. RELEASED N days passed without a valid advice; settled to the partner after MDR. No further updates. Reason codes are shared with PGW and appear in the split payout report so the partner knows what to fix."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.6 Calculation and payout","split-payout/docs/product.html#calculation-and-payout","View it visually Convert percentage splits to amounts against the gross transaction amount; round each to 2 decimals. Calculate each vendor’s commission and net payout, and the partner’s residual (section 4). Rounding differences go to the residual. Make the vendor payouts from the partner’s net as domestic fund transfers to each vendor’s IBAN, deduct remittance fees as set on the partner MID, and settle the residual to the partner, with no manual finance step. Account mechanics as defined by Finance. Handle failed transfers through the existing exception process."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.7 Reporting","split-payout/docs/product.html#reporting","Split payout report to the partner , per transaction: transaction amount, Geidea’s MDR, amount paid to each vendor, commission recovered from each vendor, remittance fees, residual, advice status and any rejection or failure reason. This is the partner’s channel for the outcome of its advices. Payout report to each vendor : amount received against each transaction reference and any remittance fee deducted. FinOps screen in APEX : split advices with filters (partner, status, date) and export. Exception report : transactions released after N days, mismatched advices, failed transfers. Finance and reconciliation reports as required by Finance. Partner and vendor report content comes from Business. Format and delivery to be defined with APEX."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 6. APEX","Document","6.8 APEX work items","split-payout/docs/product.html#apex-work-items","# Work item Section APX-01 Vendor definition with APEX-generated beneficiary ID, name, IBAN, partner MID link, optional commission, activation and deactivation. 6.1 APX-02 Split payout settings on the partner MID: enabled flag, remittance fee, fee-bearer option, N. 6.2 APX-03 Accept the split flag in transaction federation (Create Transaction API and day-end transaction file). 6.3 APX-04 Hold flagged transactions from payout; release after N days from the scheduled payout date; exception report. 6.3 APX-05 Real-time Split Advice API (A/U) with synchronous structural checks and response codes; store advices with status. 6.4 APX-06 PENDING_MATCH parking, matching on transaction arrival, day-end rejection with reason. 6.4 APX-07 Day-end split advice file intake: reconciliation against the API, trailer check, empty-file handling, mismatch hold. 6.4 APX-08 Amount validation: Rule 1, Rule 2, single payout; percentage conversion on the gross amount; rounding. 6.5 APX-09 Advice statuses (CREATED, PENDING_MATCH, REJECTED, PROCESSED, RELEASED) and reason codes. 6.5 APX-10 Payout calculation and execution: commission, remittance fees per fee-bearer option, domestic fund transfers, residual; payout cap not applied; failed-transfer exception handling. 6.6 APX-11 Accounting entries and account mechanics as defined by Finance. 4.1, 6.6 APX-12 Split payout report (partner), vendor payout report, exception report, Finance reports. 6.7 APX-13 FinOps screen with filters and export. 6.7"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","7. PGW (Ecomm)","split-payout/docs/product.html#pgw-ecomm",""],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.1 Configuration","split-payout/docs/product.html#configuration","Set by the PGW integration team per partner MID, from the operational setup in section 5.2. The partner has no access. Setting Purpose Split payout enabled Turns the service on for the MID. Off by default. Split mode Dynamic, Fixed or Profile. Fixed template Fixed mode only: list of legs (beneficiary ID + amount or percentage). Profile catalog Profile mode only: profile IDs, each with its list of legs. Beneficiary IDs The partner’s beneficiary IDs, entered as received from the APEX team. Used to validate the partner’s requests. PGW holds no vendor bank details and does not check vendor status. A beneficiary ID that is wrong or no longer active is rejected by APEX."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.2 Order creation request","split-payout/docs/product.html#order-creation-request","View it visually The split travels in the existing order creation request. The partner never sends bank details, fees or commission. Field Type Mode Description splitPayoutType string Dynamic AMOUNT or PERCENTAGE. Applies to every leg of the order. splitPayoutTransaction array Dynamic One object per vendor leg. splitPayoutTransaction[].beneficiaryId string Dynamic Must be one of the partner’s configured beneficiary IDs. splitPayoutTransaction[].value number Dynamic Amount in order currency (2 decimals) for AMOUNT; percentage of the order amount (up to 2 decimals) for PERCENTAGE. splitPayoutTransaction[].reference string Dynamic Optional. Partner’s own reference for the leg; returned in the split payout report. splitPayoutTransaction[].description string Dynamic Optional. Free text. splitPayoutProfileId string Profile ID of a profile in the partner’s configured profile catalog. deferredSplit boolean Dynamic, Profile Optional. true when the partner will send the split later through the Payout Advice API. Must not be sent together with split detail. PGW also keeps a derived order attribute, splitPayout (boolean), set when the order carries split detail or a profile ID, or is a Fixed-mode order. It is returned on the order and is not a request field. Split detail / profile ID deferredSplit PGW action Split flag to APEX Present (or Fixed mode) false / absent Accept; splitPayout = true Yes Absent true Accept; split expected through the Payout Advice API Yes Absent false / absent Normal order No Present true Reject (ambiguous; use UPDATE to change an inline split) — Sending split fields or deferredSplit for a MID where split payout is not enabled, or split fields that do not match the MID’s mode, rejects the order. An empty splitPayoutTransaction array counts as absent."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7.2 Order creation request","Document","Dynamic mode, amount split","split-payout/docs/product.html#dynamic-mode-amount-split","{ \"merchantId\": \"20100000101\", \"merchantReferenceId\": \"ORD-DEMO-1000\", \"amount\": 1000.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\": \"Pay\", \"splitPayoutType\": \"AMOUNT\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\": [ { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000301\", \"value\": 600.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-A\", \"description\": \"Products - Seller A\" }, { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000302\", \"value\": 300.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-B\", \"description\": \"Products - Seller B\" }, { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000303\", \"value\": 100.00, \"reference\": \"DELIVERY-CO\", \"description\": \"Delivery fee\" } ] }"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7.2 Order creation request","Document","Dynamic mode, percentage split (of the gross order amount)","split-payout/docs/product.html#dynamic-mode-percentage-split-of-the-gross-order-amount","{ \"merchantId\": \"20100000101\", \"merchantReferenceId\": \"ORD-DEMO-1001\", \"amount\": 1000.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\": \"Pay\", \"splitPayoutType\": \"PERCENTAGE\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\": [ { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000301\", \"value\": 60.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-A\" }, { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000302\", \"value\": 30.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-B\" }, { \"beneficiaryId\": \"BEN000303\", \"value\": 8.00, \"reference\": \"DELIVERY-CO\" } ] } Percentage splits should leave room for Geidea’s MDR and remittance fees: a split totalling 100% fails Rule 1 (section 6.5) unless vendor commission covers them."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7.2 Order creation request","Document","Profile mode","split-payout/docs/product.html#profile-mode","{ \"merchantId\": \"20100000101\", \"merchantReferenceId\": \"POL-DEMO-2001\", \"amount\": 2500.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\": \"Pay\", \"splitPayoutProfileId\": \"PRF-INSURER-A\" }"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7.2 Order creation request","Document","Deferred split (Dynamic or Profile)","split-payout/docs/product.html#deferred-split-dynamic-or-profile","{ \"merchantId\": \"20100000101\", \"merchantReferenceId\": \"ORD-DEMO-4001\", \"amount\": 750.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\": \"Pay\", \"deferredSplit\": true } Fixed mode: the partner sends a normal order with no split fields. PGW applies the MID’s fixed template and stores the resulting split against the order."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.3 Payout Advice API","split-payout/docs/product.html#payout-advice-api","End-to-end view: flow B Simulator: Payout Advice API What can go wrong: Payout Advice API A PGW API through which a partner sends a split advice for an existing order, or updates one. Available to Dynamic and Profile MIDs; a Fixed MID gets its split from the template. Endpoint and field naming to be finalised by PGW engineering. Content M/O/C Description Action M NEW or UPDATE. Order reference M The PGW order the advice applies to. Advice ID C Mandatory for UPDATE: the advice ID returned by the latest NEW or UPDATE. Split M Dynamic: splitPayoutType and splitPayoutTransaction as in section 7.2. Profile: splitPayoutProfileId. Always the complete split, never a single leg."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7.3 Payout Advice API","Document","Rules","split-payout/docs/product.html#rules","NEW is accepted only for an order created with deferredSplit = true that has no advice yet. Repeating a NEW with the same content returns the original advice ID, so a retry after a timeout is safe. UPDATE is accepted for any flagged order (split sent at order creation or through NEW) and must carry the latest advice ID, so an older retried request cannot undo a newer correction. APEX accepts it only while the advice is CREATED, REJECTED or PENDING_MATCH; it is refused once PROCESSED or RELEASED. An UPDATE is how a partner corrects a rejected advice. An advice for an order that is not flagged is rejected: the transaction may already have settled to the partner. The order must be a successful sale under the calling partner’s MID. PGW forwards every accepted NEW or UPDATE to the APEX Split Advice API in real time (action A or U). The response returns the advice ID with status accepted, or rejected with a reason code from PGW’s checks or from APEX’s synchronous checks. The final outcome reaches the partner through the split payout report. If APEX cannot be reached, PGW retries; the day-end file carries the advice in any case, and the transaction stays held because it is flagged."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.4 Split flag in federation","split-payout/docs/product.html#split-flag-in-federation","PGW sets the split flag on the transaction it federates to APEX when the order has splitPayout = true or deferredSplit = true. The flag is carried in the real-time Create Transaction API and in the day-end transaction record, on the record APEX settles from, keyed by interSystemID. Field name and position to be agreed with APEX."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.5 Forwarding advices to APEX","split-payout/docs/product.html#forwarding-advices-to-apex","Real time. For a split sent with the order (including Fixed and Profile, resolved into legs), PGW sends action A to the APEX Split Advice API once the payment succeeds. For the Payout Advice API, PGW sends A or U on each accepted call. Day-end file. After the Ecomm cut-off (midnight), PGW sends APEX the split advice file with every advice of the day, including updates, in the latest state held by PGW. The file has a trailer with the record count and is sent every day, with a zero count when there are no advices. Format defined by APEX. PGW keeps each advice’s status: pending, sent to APEX, APEX response (accepted or rejected with reason), included in day-end file."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.6 Validations","split-payout/docs/product.html#validations","What can go wrong PGW validates at order creation, before any payment is taken, and on every Payout Advice API call. Any failure rejects the request with a specific error code (codes to be defined by PGW). Check Order creation Payout Advice API Split payout is enabled for the MID. Yes Yes The request matches the configured mode: legs for Dynamic, a valid profile ID for Profile, no split fields for Fixed. Yes Yes (Fixed MIDs rejected) Split detail and deferredSplit are not sent together. Yes — Every beneficiary ID is one of the partner’s configured beneficiary IDs. Yes Yes All legs use one split type. Yes Yes Amount splits add up to no more than the order amount; percentage splits to no more than 100%. Yes Yes The order exists, is a successful sale and belongs to the calling MID. — Yes The order is flagged for split. — Yes NEW: order created with deferredSplit and no advice exists. UPDATE: advice ID is the latest for the order. — Yes"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.7 Transaction flow","split-payout/docs/product.html#transaction-flow","End-to-end view Simulator The partner creates the order with split detail (Dynamic), a profile ID (Profile), deferredSplit (split to follow), or no split (Fixed, where PGW applies the template). PGW validates the request (section 7.6). If invalid, the order is rejected before any payment is taken. The customer pays. PGW authorizes through the existing route (MPGS or CyberSource), confirms the payment to the partner and federates the transaction to APEX in real time with the split flag where applicable. PGW stores the resolved split against the order and sends it to the APEX Split Advice API in real time. For a deferred split, or to correct an advice, the partner calls the Payout Advice API; PGW validates and forwards it to APEX in real time. After the Ecomm cut-off (midnight), PGW sends the day-end split advice file. APEX holds the flagged transaction, validates the advice, and pays out or releases after N days (section 6)."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction › 7. PGW (Ecomm)","Document","7.8 PGW work items","split-payout/docs/product.html#pgw-work-items","# Work item Section PGW-01 Split payout configuration per partner MID: enabled, mode, Fixed template, Profile catalog, beneficiary IDs. 7.1 PGW-02 Order creation: accept split fields and deferredSplit; derived splitPayout attribute; mode and combination checks. 7.2 PGW-03 Resolve and store the split against the order (Fixed and Profile into legs) with advice ID and status. 7.2, 7.5 PGW-04 Split flag in transaction federation to APEX (real-time API and day-end transaction record). 7.4 PGW-05 Payout Advice API (NEW / UPDATE) with the rules in section 7.3. 7.3 PGW-06 Real-time forwarding of advices to the APEX Split Advice API (A / U), retries, mapping of APEX responses and reason codes. 7.3, 7.5 PGW-07 Day-end split advice file after the midnight cut-off, with trailer, sent every day including empty days. 7.5 PGW-08 Validations in section 7.6 with error codes. 7.6 PGW-09 Merchant API documentation: split fields, deferredSplit, Payout Advice API, error and reason codes. 7.2, 7.3"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","8. Refunds and Chargebacks","split-payout/docs/product.html#refunds-and-chargebacks","What can go wrong: refunds and chargebacks Refunds and chargebacks are debited from the partner’s MID through the normal process. Vendors and their payouts are not involved, and Geidea does not recover amounts from vendors. A chargeback on a transaction whose split has already been paid out is handled the same way as a chargeback on any settled transaction today. Because a partner’s residual can be small, a refund or chargeback may exceed the partner’s settlement on the day. How the shortfall is recovered (for example, from the partner’s later settlements) is to be covered in the partner agreement and confirmed by Finance. New splits should not be held back to recover a partner’s negative balance, as that would stop vendor payments for an amount the partner owes."],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","9. Out of Scope and Later Phases","split-payout/docs/product.html#out-of-scope-and-later-phases","Item Status POS (TMS and MW): split advice for POS transactions. Expected design: MW exposes a split API to the partner, forwards advices to the APEX Split Advice API in real time and generates its own day-end file, as PGW does. Open: how a POS transaction is flagged for hold, as there is no order-creation step. Later phase Merchant Portal: SPLIT tag and filter on Transactions, Payout Split table on transaction detail, split payout view. A split advice inquiry API from APEX is taken up with this view. Later phase MA: APIs on top of APEX for vendor creation and split payout enablement. Later phase Individuals as vendors Out of scope Cross-border payouts Out of scope Vendor portal access or self-service Out of scope Real-time payouts; partial processing of an advice Out of scope"],["Split Payout","1. Introduction","Document","10. Open Items","split-payout/docs/product.html#open-items","# Item Owner 1 Split Advice API specification, day-end advice file format and trailer, field name and position of the split flag in federation. APEX team with Emcrey; PGW 2 Whether amount validation can run in the API call or only as a scheduled process. APEX with Emcrey 3 Reason code list for APEX rejections, shared with PGW for the API response and report. APEX, PGW 4 APEX delivery date for the split scope. APEX team 5 Account mechanics (staging account or direct posting) and accounting entries. Finance 6 VAT on vendor commission and remittance fees; remittance fee amount; whether funds move to a separate account for the remittance fee. Finance 7 Default value of N. Finance, Business 8 Recovery of a refund or chargeback shortfall when the partner’s balance goes negative. Finance, Legal, Business 9 Partner and vendor report content; Finance and reconciliation reports. Business, Finance 10 PGW error codes and Payout Advice API contract review. PGW engineering team"],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","Story map","split-payout/docs/stories.html","v0.5 Published 20-Nov-2026 Source: Vendor Payout Service - PGW Stories v0.5.docx Version 0.5 draft · 17-Nov-2026 · Prepared by Ghulam Rabbani (Product) Team: PGW engineering team These stories are the requirement. Each story can be read alone. A story refers to another story only for work that must be built first. Story map End-to-end view Onboarding Split modes Simulator Money flow Advice lifecycle What can go wrong # Story What it delivers Depends on Status SP-1 FE – Split payout configuration screen The new tab in PGW Configuration as a screen the user can navigate. No save. — Written SP-2 BE – Split payout configuration setup New settings on the product instance. Leg and profile limits. Partner ID search across MIDs. — Written SP-3 FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode Turn split on and off, manage Partner IDs, select Dynamic. Save and checks. SP-1, SP-2 Written SP-4 FE/BE – Fixed mode Fixed template. Save and checks. SP-3 Written SP-5 FE/BE – Profile mode Profile catalog. Save and checks. SP-3 Written SP-6 BE – Create session with split payout Split fields on Create Session. PGW checks and stores the split. Split flag to APEX. SP-2 Written (PTLF part waits on P4) SP-7 BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration PGW sends each split to APEX. SP-6, P3 Waiting on Emcrey SP-8 BE – PGW Split Payout API Merchant API to send a split later (NEW) or correct it (UPDATE). SP-6, SP-7 Written SP-9 BE – Day-end split advice file All advices of the day to APEX after the midnight cut-off. SP-7, P3 Waiting on Emcrey Build order: SP-1 and SP-2 in parallel → SP-3 → SP-4, SP-5 → SP-6 → SP-8. SP-7 and SP-9 after P3."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","Prerequisites (not PGW work)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#prerequisites-not-pgw-work","Onboarding: P1 and P2 # Item Needed for Owner P1 Risk approves the merchant for split payout. Operations onboards and screens each partner (Operations SOP). Before a MID is set up (SP-3) Risk & Compliance, Operations P2 APEX enables split on the merchant MID, creates the partner definitions and shares the Partner IDs. Before a MID is set up (SP-3) APEX team P3 Emcrey shares the APEX Payout Advice API spec and the day-end advice file spec. SP-7, SP-9 APEX / Emcrey P4 The APEX team approves the PTLF spec with the split flag as field 49. SP-6 (PTLF part) APEX team"],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","Rules for every story","split-payout/docs/stories.html#rules-for-every-story","Terms. Merchant = the Geidea merchant whose MID has split payout enabled. Partner = a business that the merchant shares its payout with (for example a seller on a marketplace). The merchant tells PGW how much each partner gets. APEX pays the partner from the merchant's settlement. A partner is defined in APEX. It is not a MID. Partner ID = the ID APEX gives to a partner. Leg = one line of a split: one Partner ID and its amount or percentage. Field names. PGW field names are camelCase. Names in these stories are proposals. PGW engineering can rename them. Keep the meaning. The PGW backend applies every rule, also when the screen already blocks the action. Identify the merchant by MID in every API and in all documentation. New fields in merchant APIs are additions. Do not change or remove existing fields. Times are UAE time (UTC+4)."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-1-fe-split-payout-configuration-screen","Simulator: configuration"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background","The PGW integration team sets merchant settings in the Backoffice: Merchants → Impersonate merchant → Payment Gateway → Configuration. Split payout needs a new tab there. This story builds the screen only. SP-3, SP-4 and SP-5 connect it to the backend."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal","The tab Split Payout Settings exists and the user can navigate all of it. Nothing is saved."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary","Item Value Story ID SP-1 Users PGW integration team (Backoffice) Depends on — Followed by SP-3, SP-4, SP-5 Out of scope Save. Checks. Data from the backend."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Tab","split-payout/docs/stories.html#tab","Add the tab Split Payout Settings after Visa installment Settings and before NOTIFICATION Settings . The gateway_Instance selector (Live / Test) applies, as on the other tabs. Only Backoffice users who can open Payment Gateway Configuration see the tab. The merchant's own portal login does not show it."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Content of the tab","split-payout/docs/stories.html#content-of-the-tab","# Section Shows Component (existing example) 2.1 Split payout Title, one-line description, ENABLED / Disabled toggle. When off, the tab shows nothing else. Section with toggle (NOTIFICATION Settings) 2.2 Split mode Shown when the toggle is on. Three tiles: Dynamic , Fixed , Profile , each with one line of text. One can be selected. Bordered tiles (Gateway Settings: Payment methods) 2.3 Partner IDs Shown when the toggle is on. Table: Partner ID, Partner name, Used in, edit and delete icons. Link + Add Partner ID . Table with Add, edit, delete (Provider Settings: Provider Accounts) 2.4 Partner ID pop-up Opens from + Add Partner ID and from edit. Fields: Partner ID , Partner name (optional) . Buttons: Cancel , Save changes . On edit, Partner ID is read-only. Pop-up (Provider Settings: Edit Account) 2.5 Fixed template Shown when Fixed is selected. Split type radio: Amount (AED) / Percentage of gross order amount . One row per leg: Partner ID dropdown, value field, delete icon. Link + Add leg . Total below the rows. Grey fields, dropdown (all tabs) 2.6 Profile catalog Shown when Profile is selected. Table: Profile ID, Description, Split type, Legs, edit and delete icons. Link + Add profile . Table with Add, edit, delete 2.7 Profile pop-up Opens from + Add profile and from edit. Fields: Profile ID , Description (optional) , split type radio, leg rows as in 2.5. Buttons: Cancel , Save changes . On edit, Profile ID is read-only. Pop-up 2.8 Buttons Discard Changes and Save changes at the bottom of the tab. All tabs"],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Behaviour in this story","split-payout/docs/stories.html#behaviour-in-this-story","The toggle, tiles and radios change what the tab shows, as in section 2. In the pop-ups, Save changes adds or updates the row on the screen only. Cancel closes the pop-up. + Add leg adds an empty leg row. The delete icon removes a row from the screen. The Partner ID dropdown in a leg lists the Partner IDs in the table (2.3). + Add leg is hidden when a template or profile has 10 legs. + Add profile is hidden when there are 10 profiles. (SP-2 makes these limits configurable. SP-4 and SP-5 read them.) Save changes (2.8) does nothing in this story. Discard Changes clears all changes on the screen. The tab does not read data from the backend. When opened, the toggle is off and the tables are empty. Profile mode: the full tab Profile pop-up"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-1 — FE – Split payout configuration screen","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria","The tab shows after Visa installment Settings in the Backoffice. A merchant portal login does not show it. Toggle off: only the Split payout section shows. Toggle on: Split mode and Partner IDs show. Fixed selected: Fixed template shows. Profile selected: Profile catalog shows. Dynamic selected: neither shows. Add, edit and delete a Partner ID, a leg and a profile on the screen. With 10 legs, + Add leg is hidden. With 10 profiles, + Add profile is hidden. Save changes sends no request."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-2-be-split-payout-configuration-setup","Simulator: configuration Onboarding: Partner IDs from APEX"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-1","Merchant PGW settings are stored on the MID's PAYMENT_GATEWAY product instance, in its data object. The Configuration screen reads it with the existing product instance search and saves with the existing product instance update (PATCH /product/api/v1/productInstance/{productInstanceId}, JSON-Patch replace on data/<key>). The key isSplitPayoutEnabled already exists in data (value false). No screen uses it."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-1","The product instance data holds all split payout settings. The leg limit and the profile limit are system settings. PGW can find if a Partner ID is already used on another MID."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-1","Item Value Story ID SP-2 Depends on — Followed by SP-3, SP-4, SP-5, SP-6 Out of scope Screen (SP-1). Save checks (SP-3 to SP-5)."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-1",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Settings in data (PAYMENT_GATEWAY product instance, Live and Test separately)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#settings-in-data-payment_gateway-product-instance-live-and-test-separately","Field Type Default Values isSplitPayoutEnabled Boolean false Existing key. true = split payout on. splitPayoutMode String null DYNAMIC / FIXED / PROFILE splitPayoutPartners Array [] Item: partnerId (String), partnerName (String, max 100, optional) splitPayoutFixedTemplate Object null splitType (String: AMOUNT / PERCENTAGE), legs (Array) splitPayoutProfiles Array [] Item: profileId (String), description (String, optional), splitType (String), legs (Array) Leg item: partnerId (String), value (Number, 2 decimals). Existing MIDs: add the new fields with the defaults above. Do not change isSplitPayoutEnabled. The existing product instance search returns the new fields. The existing product instance update accepts them. partnerName is for the integration team only. Do not send it to the merchant or to APEX."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Limits (system settings, not per MID)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#limits-system-settings-not-per-mid","Setting Default Meaning Maximum legs per split 10 Applies to the Fixed template, each profile, and each split received in SP-6 and SP-8. Maximum profiles per MID 10 Applies to splitPayoutProfiles. Store both as configuration. Do not write the values in code. The Configuration screen can read both values."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Partner ID search","split-payout/docs/stories.html#partner-id-search","Input: Partner ID, instance (Live or Test). Output: the MID that has this Partner ID in splitPayoutPartners, or none. Compare without case."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-2 — BE – Split payout configuration setup","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-1","Product instance search for an existing MID returns the new fields with their defaults. Update splitPayoutMode with the existing product instance update. The search returns the new value. Change the leg limit to 5 in configuration. The screen reads 5. Partner ID search returns the MID that has the ID, and none for an unused ID. Live and Test results are separate."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-3-febe-enable-split-partner-ids-and-dynamic-mode","Simulator: Dynamic configuration Split modes What can go wrong: configuration"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-2","SP-1 built the tab. SP-2 added the settings. This story connects them for the base settings that every mode needs: the split toggle, the split mode and the Partner IDs. With this story, a MID can be fully set up for Dynamic mode. In Dynamic mode the merchant sends the split with each order (SP-6) or later through the Split Payout API (SP-8). No template is needed."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-2","The PGW integration team can turn split payout on for a MID, select a mode, add the merchant's Partner IDs and save. For Dynamic mode, the set-up is then complete."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-2","Item Value Story ID SP-3 Users PGW integration team (Backoffice) Fields written isSplitPayoutEnabled, splitPayoutMode, splitPayoutPartners Save Existing product instance update, as the other tabs Depends on SP-1, SP-2. Before a MID is set up: P1, P2. Followed by SP-4, SP-5"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-2",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Load","split-payout/docs/stories.html#load","When the tab opens, show the saved values of the selected instance. Show the Used in column of the Partner ID table from the saved Fixed template and profiles (SP-4, SP-5). Until those exist, show \"—\"."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Split toggle","split-payout/docs/stories.html#split-toggle","On → store isSplitPayoutEnabled = true. Off → false. Turning the toggle off keeps the other settings stored. They are not applied while split is off."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Split mode","split-payout/docs/stories.html#split-mode","Store the selected tile in splitPayoutMode: DYNAMIC, FIXED or PROFILE. When the mode changes, the template or profiles of the old mode stay stored. They are not applied. Show a note under the mode: \"The Fixed template / profiles are stored but not applied in this mode.\""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Partner IDs","split-payout/docs/stories.html#partner-ids","What can go wrong: Partner ID entry Add and edit in the pop-up. The pop-up checks the entry when the user clicks Save changes in the pop-up: # Check Message (under the field) 4.1 Partner ID has 3–20 letters, digits or hyphens. Remove spaces at start and end. Use 3–20 letters, digits or hyphens. 4.2 Partner ID is not already in the table. Compare without case. This Partner ID is already in the list. 4.3 Partner ID is not on another MID of the same instance (SP-2 search). This Partner ID is configured on another MID (MID nnnnnnnnnnn). A partner belongs to one merchant MID only. 4.4 Partner name: maximum 100 characters. Use up to 100 characters. Delete from the table: # Check Message 4.5 The Partner ID is not used in the Fixed template or in a profile. P000301 is used in Fixed template. Remove it there first. Why 4.3. APEX links each partner to one merchant MID. A Partner ID on a second MID makes APEX reject every split from that MID after the customer has paid. Note 4.1 is a placeholder until the Partner ID convention is agreed (open point 1)."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Save","split-payout/docs/stories.html#save","What can go wrong: save checks On Save changes (bottom of the tab): # Check Message 5.1 Split on → a mode is selected. Select a split mode. 5.2 Split on → at least one Partner ID. Add at least one Partner ID. Any failure: do not save. Show the message under the section and the banner \"Changes not saved. Fix the highlighted fields.\" No failure: save the changed fields with the existing product instance update. After a successful save, use the saved values as the new starting point for Save changes and Discard Changes . Example: turn split off, save, turn it on, save again → the second save stores true. Save changes is off when nothing changed. Discard Changes returns to the last saved values."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","6. Effect of a saved change","split-payout/docs/stories.html#effect-of-a-saved-change","Change Effect Split turned off New sessions with split fields are rejected (SP-6). Split Payout API calls are rejected (SP-8). Orders already flagged stay flagged; APEX releases them after N days. Operations also turns split off in APEX. Partner ID deleted New sessions and API calls with this ID are rejected. Splits already sent to APEX do not change. Any other change Applies to sessions created after the save. Split payout off Dynamic mode with Partner IDs Add Partner ID blocked by 4.3"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-3 — FE/BE – Enable split, Partner IDs and Dynamic mode","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-2","Open the tab on a new MID: split off, no mode, no Partner IDs. Turn split on, save without a mode: message 5.1. Nothing is saved. Select Dynamic, save without a Partner ID: message 5.2. Add P000301, then add p000301: message 4.2. Add an ID that is on another MID: message 4.3 with that MID. Select Dynamic, add two Partner IDs, save, reload: values are shown. Turn split off, save, turn split on, save, reload: split is on. Change on the Test instance: the Live instance does not change."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-4-febe-fixed-mode","Simulator: Fixed configuration Split modes What can go wrong: Fixed template"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-3","In Fixed mode the merchant sends a normal order with no split fields. PGW applies the same split to every order of the MID. The integration team sets this split once, as the Fixed template. SP-3 is in place: split is on and Partner IDs exist."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-3","The PGW integration team can set and save the Fixed template. With this story, a MID can be fully set up for Fixed mode."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-3","Item Value Story ID SP-4 Users PGW integration team (Backoffice) Fields written splitPayoutFixedTemplate (splitType, legs[] with partnerId, value) Save Existing product instance update Depends on SP-3 Followed by SP-6 (applies the template to each order)"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-3",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Template","split-payout/docs/stories.html#template","Split type: Amount (AED) → AMOUNT. Percentage of gross order amount → PERCENTAGE. One type for all legs. Each leg: Partner ID from the MID's Partner IDs, and a value. Show the total of all legs below the rows."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Checks on Save changes","split-payout/docs/stories.html#checks-on-save-changes","These checks apply when splitPayoutMode = FIXED. # Check Message (under the leg or the total) 2.1 At least one leg. Add at least one leg. 2.2 Each leg has a Partner ID. Select a Partner ID. 2.3 Each Partner ID occurs once in the template. Each partner can appear once. 2.4 Each value is above 0, with up to 2 decimals. Enter a value above 0, up to 2 decimals. 2.5 Number of legs ≤ maximum legs (SP-2, default 10). At the maximum, hide + Add leg . Maximum 10 legs. 2.6 Split type PERCENTAGE: total ≤ 100. Percentages cannot add up to more than 100%. Any failure: do not save. Show the banner \"Changes not saved. Fix the highlighted fields.\" No failure: save splitPayoutFixedTemplate with the existing product instance update. Save and discard work as in SP-3 section 5. For AMOUNT, do not check the total at setup. The order amount is not known. SP-6 rejects an order when the legs add up to more than the order amount."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Effect","split-payout/docs/stories.html#effect","A saved template applies to sessions created after the save. Partner IDs used in the template show \"Fixed template\" in the Used in column. They cannot be deleted (SP-3 check 4.5)."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Example","split-payout/docs/stories.html#example","Template: PERCENTAGE, P000301 = 60, P000302 = 30. Order AED 200. PGW sends to APEX: P000301 60%, P000302 30% (SP-6, SP-7). APEX pays them from the merchant's net. The merchant keeps the rest. \"splitPayoutFixedTemplate\": { \"splitType\": \"PERCENTAGE\", \"legs\": [ { \"partnerId\": \"P000301\", \"value\": 60.00 }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000302\", \"value\": 30.00 } ] } Fixed template Save blocked by 2.3, 2.2, 2.4 and 2.6"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-4 — FE/BE – Fixed mode","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-3","Fixed, PERCENTAGE, 60 + 30: saved. Reload shows the template. 60 + 30 + 15: message 2.6. Same Partner ID in two legs: message 2.3. Leg with value 0: message 2.4. 10 legs: + Add leg is hidden. Delete a Partner ID used in the template: message \"P000301 is used in Fixed template. Remove it there first.\""],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-5-febe-profile-mode","Simulator: Profile configuration Split modes What can go wrong: profiles"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-4","In Profile mode the merchant sends a profile ID with each order. Each profile holds a split that the integration team sets up front. Example: an insurance aggregator with one profile per insurer. SP-3 is in place: split is on and Partner IDs exist."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-4","The PGW integration team can add, edit, delete and save profiles. With this story, a MID can be fully set up for Profile mode."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-4","Item Value Story ID SP-5 Users PGW integration team (Backoffice) Fields written splitPayoutProfiles[] (profileId, description, splitType, legs[]) Save Existing product instance update Depends on SP-3 Followed by SP-6, SP-8 (apply the profile the merchant sends)"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-4",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Profile pop-up","split-payout/docs/stories.html#profile-pop-up","Fields: Profile ID , Description (optional) , split type ( Amount (AED) / Percentage of gross order amount ), legs (Partner ID and value). The pop-up checks the profile when the user clicks Save changes in the pop-up: # Check Message 1.1 Profile ID has 1–50 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores. Use 1–50 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores. 1.2 Profile ID is not used by another profile of this MID. Compare without case. This profile ID already exists for this MID. 1.3 At least one leg. Add at least one leg. 1.4 Each leg has a Partner ID. Select a Partner ID. 1.5 Each Partner ID occurs once in the profile. Each partner can appear once. 1.6 Each value is above 0, with up to 2 decimals. Enter a value above 0, up to 2 decimals. 1.7 Number of legs ≤ maximum legs (SP-2, default 10). At the maximum, hide + Add leg . Maximum 10 legs. 1.8 Split type PERCENTAGE: total ≤ 100. Percentages cannot add up to more than 100%. On edit, Profile ID is read-only. To change an ID, delete the profile and add a new one. The pop-up Save changes updates the table on the screen only."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Checks on Save changes (bottom of the tab)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#checks-on-save-changes-bottom-of-the-tab","# Check Message 2.1 Mode PROFILE: at least one profile. Add at least one profile. 2.2 Number of profiles ≤ maximum profiles (SP-2, default 10). At the maximum, hide + Add profile . Maximum 10 profiles. Any failure: do not save. Show the banner \"Changes not saved. Fix the highlighted fields.\" No failure: save splitPayoutProfiles with the existing product instance update. Save and discard work as in SP-3 section 5. For AMOUNT profiles, do not check the total at setup. SP-6 rejects an order when the legs add up to more than the order amount."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Effect","split-payout/docs/stories.html#effect-1","Saved profiles apply to sessions and API calls after the save. A deleted profile: new sessions with this profile ID are rejected (SP-6). Partner IDs used in a profile show the profile ID in the Used in column. They cannot be deleted (SP-3 check 4.5)."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Example","split-payout/docs/stories.html#example-1","\"splitPayoutProfiles\": [ { \"profileId\": \"PRF-INSURER-A\", \"description\": \"Motor policy - Insurer A\", \"splitType\": \"PERCENTAGE\", \"legs\": [ { \"partnerId\": \"P000401\", \"value\": 90.00 }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000403\", \"value\": 5.00 } ] }, { \"profileId\": \"PRF-INSURER-B\", \"description\": \"Motor policy - Insurer B\", \"splitType\": \"AMOUNT\", \"legs\": [ { \"partnerId\": \"P000402\", \"value\": 500.00 }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000403\", \"value\": 25.00 } ] } ] Profile catalog Profile pop-up"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-5 — FE/BE – Profile mode","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-4","Add the two profiles in the example, save, reload: both are shown. Add a profile with ID prf-insurer-a: message 1.2. Profile with percentages 90 + 15: message 1.8. Mode Profile with no profile, save: message 2.1. 10 profiles: + Add profile is hidden."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-6-be-create-session-with-split-payout","End-to-end view Simulator: Create Session Split modes Money flow What can go wrong: Create Session"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-5","A merchant starts every payment with Create Session (POST /payment-intent/api/v2/direct/session). This covers the hosted payment page, the Direct API, and token CIT and MIT. The session becomes the order. For split payout, PGW must know the split of each order and tell APEX that the transaction is a split transaction. APEX then holds the settlement until it receives the split (SP-7). The PGW order already has the field splitPayoutTransaction (empty today)."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-5","A merchant with split payout on can send the split, a profile ID, or deferredSplit with Create Session. PGW checks the split before payment and rejects a wrong request. PGW stores the split on the order and returns it in order inquiry and callback. PGW sends the split flag to APEX with each successful split transaction."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-5","Item Value Story ID SP-6 Geidea endpoint POST /payment-intent/api/v2/direct/session (HPP, Direct API, CIT, MIT) Settings read isSplitPayoutEnabled, splitPayoutMode, splitPayoutPartners, splitPayoutFixedTemplate, splitPayoutProfiles, maximum legs (SP-2) Order fields written splitPayout, deferredSplit, splitPayoutType, splitPayoutProfileId, splitPayoutTransaction[] APEX createTransaction federation: new field splitPayout. PTLF: field 49 (waits on P4). Depends on SP-2. A MID set up with SP-3 to SP-5. Followed by SP-7, SP-8 Out of scope Sending the split to APEX (SP-7). Split after payment (SP-8). Pay by Link. Drop-in session v1. Refunds (no change: debited from the merchant as today)."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-5",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. New request fields (Create Session)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#new-request-fields-create-session","Field Type M/O/C Mode Rule splitPayoutType String C – M when splitPayoutTransaction is sent Dynamic AMOUNT or PERCENTAGE. One type for all legs. splitPayoutTransaction Array O Dynamic One item per leg. splitPayoutTransaction[].partnerId String M Dynamic A Partner ID of the MID splitPayoutTransaction[].value Number M Dynamic Above 0, up to 2 decimals. AED for AMOUNT. Percent of the order amount for PERCENTAGE. splitPayoutTransaction[].reference String O Dynamic Merchant's reference for the leg. Max 50. splitPayoutTransaction[].description String O Dynamic Free text. Max 100. splitPayoutProfileId String O Profile A profile ID of the MID deferredSplit Boolean O Dynamic, Profile true = the merchant sends the split later with the Split Payout API (SP-8). Fixed mode: the merchant sends no split fields. PGW applies the Fixed template. An empty splitPayoutTransaction array counts as not sent."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. What PGW does with each request","split-payout/docs/stories.html#what-pgw-does-with-each-request","Split modes: one order, three modes # MID setting Request PGW action splitPayout on the order 2.1 Split off No split fields Normal session false 2.2 Split off Any split field or deferredSplit Reject — 2.3 Dynamic splitPayoutTransaction Check (section 3). Store the legs. true 2.4 Dynamic deferredSplit = true, no legs Store deferredSplit = true. No legs. true 2.5 Dynamic No split fields, no deferredSplit Normal session. No split. false 2.6 Fixed No split fields Copy the Fixed template legs to the order. Check the amount (3.6). true 2.7 Fixed Any split field or deferredSplit Reject — 2.8 Profile splitPayoutProfileId Copy the profile legs to the order. Check (section 3). true 2.9 Profile deferredSplit = true, no profile ID Store deferredSplit = true. true 2.10 Profile splitPayoutTransaction Reject — 2.11 Any Split detail or profile ID and deferredSplit = true Reject —"],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Checks before payment","split-payout/docs/stories.html#checks-before-payment","Simulator: Create Session What can go wrong: checks 3.1–3.9 Any failure rejects the session (HTTP 400). PGW engineering sets the error codes. # Check Message 3.1 Split fields are allowed for this MID and mode (section 2). Split payout is not enabled for this merchant. / Split fields do not match the merchant's split mode. 3.2 paymentOperation = Pay. Split payout is supported for Pay only. 3.3 Order currency = AED. Split payout is supported in AED only. 3.4 Each partnerId is a Partner ID of the MID. Each occurs once. Unknown partner ID: {id}. / Duplicate partner ID: {id}. 3.5 Number of legs ≤ maximum legs (SP-2). Maximum {n} legs. 3.6 AMOUNT: total of legs ≤ order amount. PERCENTAGE: total ≤ 100. Split total is more than the order amount. / Split total is more than 100%. 3.7 Each value is above 0, up to 2 decimals. Invalid split value. 3.8 splitPayoutProfileId is a profile of the MID. Unknown split profile: {id}. 3.9 Not split detail and deferredSplit together. Send split detail or deferredSplit, not both. Why 3.2. In this release APEX handles split only on a sale. Authorize and capture are not included."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Store on the order","split-payout/docs/stories.html#store-on-the-order","Order field Type Value splitPayout Boolean true when the order is a split order (section 2). Not a request field. deferredSplit Boolean From the request. Default false. splitPayoutType String AMOUNT / PERCENTAGE. From the request, template or profile. null when deferred. splitPayoutProfileId String From the request. null otherwise. splitPayoutTransaction[] Array Legs: partnerId, value, reference, description. Existing field. Store the split as it is at session creation. A later change to the MID settings does not change the order. Do not convert percentages to amounts. APEX converts them on the gross amount."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Return to the merchant","split-payout/docs/stories.html#return-to-the-merchant","Return the fields of section 4 in: Order inquiry GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order/{orderId} and GET /pgw/api/v1/direct/order?MerchantReferenceId=. The callback to callbackUrl. The pay responses (/pgw/api/v2/direct/pay, /pgw/api/v2/direct/pay/token)."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","6. Split flag to APEX","split-payout/docs/stories.html#split-flag-to-apex","Simulator: APEX federation Advice lifecycle When PGW federates a successful Pay transaction of an order with splitPayout = true, send splitPayout = Y in createTransaction. Add the field at the end of the payload. For all other transactions send splitPayout = N. PTLF: send the same value as field 49 (waits on P4). Why. APEX holds a transaction with splitPayout = Y until it receives a valid split. If PGW does not send the split, APEX releases the money to the merchant after N days. Without the flag, APEX pays the merchant the next day and the partners' money stays with the merchant."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","7. Example (Dynamic, amount split)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#example-dynamic-amount-split","{ \"amount\": 1000.00, \"currency\": \"AED\", \"merchantReferenceId\": \"ORD-DEMO-1000\", \"paymentOperation\": \"Pay\", \"timestamp\": \"...\", \"signature\": \"...\", \"callbackUrl\": \"...\", \"splitPayoutType\": \"AMOUNT\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\": [ { \"partnerId\": \"P000301\", \"value\": 600.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-A\" }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000302\", \"value\": 300.00, \"reference\": \"SELLER-B\" }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000303\", \"value\": 100.00, \"reference\": \"DELIVERY\" } ] } Profile: send \"splitPayoutProfileId\": \"PRF-INSURER-A\". Deferred: send \"deferredSplit\": true. Fixed: send no split fields."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-6 — BE – Create session with split payout","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-5","Dynamic MID, the example above: session created. Order inquiry returns splitPayout = true and the three legs. Same request on a MID with split off: rejected (3.1). Legs total AED 1,001 on an AED 1,000 order: rejected (3.6). Unknown Partner ID: rejected (3.4). paymentOperation = PreAuthorize with split: rejected (3.2). Fixed MID, order with no split fields: order has the template legs. Profile MID, splitPayoutProfileId = PRF-INSURER-A: order has the profile legs. Unknown profile: rejected (3.8). deferredSplit = true: order has splitPayout = true and no legs. Split detail and deferredSplit together: rejected (3.9). Successful split payment: createTransaction has splitPayout = Y. Normal payment: N. Change the Fixed template after a session: the order keeps the old legs."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-7-be-apex-payout-advice-api-integration-waiting-on-emcrey-p3","End-to-end view: APEX not reachable Simulator: advice to APEX Advice lifecycle What can go wrong: sending to APEX"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-6","APEX holds a split transaction until it receives the split (the \"advice\"). APEX provides a Payout Advice API. PGW must send each split to this API. The API spec is not final yet. This story gives the requirement from the agreed APEX requirement (APEX team, 11-Nov-2026). Field names follow the APEX draft and can change with the final spec."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-6","PGW sends the split of each successful split order to APEX. PGW sends new and updated splits from the Split Payout API (SP-8). PGW keeps the status of each advice."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-6","Item Value Story ID SP-7 APEX API used Payout Advice API (spec from Emcrey, P3) Depends on SP-6, P3 Followed by SP-8, SP-9"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-6",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. When PGW sends an advice","split-payout/docs/stories.html#when-pgw-sends-an-advice","# Trigger Action 1.1 Pay succeeds on an order with legs in splitPayoutTransaction (Dynamic, Fixed, Profile) Send action A (create) 1.2 SP-8 accepts a NEW Send action A 1.3 SP-8 accepts an UPDATE Send action U (replace the whole advice) Orders with deferredSplit = true and no legs: send nothing until SP-8."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Content (APEX draft)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#content-apex-draft","APEX field PGW source Action A or U Merchant MID TransactionReference interSystemID of the Pay transaction SplitRules[].PartnerID splitPayoutTransaction[].partnerId SplitRules[].Percentage value when splitPayoutType = PERCENTAGE. Else empty. SplitRules[].Amount value when splitPayoutType = AMOUNT. Else empty. Send percentage or amount, never both."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Advice record on the order","split-payout/docs/stories.html#advice-record-on-the-order","Field Values splitAdviceId Generated by PGW at the first advice of the order. A new ID for each UPDATE. splitAdviceStatus PENDING (not sent yet), SENT, ACCEPTED, REJECTED splitAdviceReason APEX reason code and text when REJECTED"],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Errors and retry","split-payout/docs/stories.html#errors-and-retry","Advice lifecycle: APEX not reachable Advice lifecycle: rejected, then corrected Try it: APEX not reachable APEX not reachable or timeout: keep PENDING and retry. Retry count and interval: PGW engineering. The day-end file (SP-9) carries the advice in any case. APEX rejects: store REJECTED and the reason. The merchant can correct it with an UPDATE (SP-8). A failure here never changes the payment result."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-7 — BE – APEX Payout Advice API integration (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-6","To be completed when P3 is received."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-8-be-pgw-split-payout-api","End-to-end view: deferred split Simulator: Payout Advice API Advice lifecycle: deferred split What can go wrong: Payout Advice API"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-7","Some merchants do not know the split when the customer pays. They create the session with deferredSplit = true (SP-6) and send the split later. A merchant can also correct a split that APEX rejected. This story adds a merchant API for both. PGW checks the request and sends it to APEX (SP-7)."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-7","The merchant can send the split of a paid order (NEW). The merchant can replace the split of an order (UPDATE). PGW returns the result at once and sends the advice to APEX."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-7","Item Value Story ID SP-8 Geidea endpoint New. Name and path: PGW engineering (e.g. POST /pgw/api/v1/direct/splitPayout). Same authentication as the other Direct API calls. Modes Dynamic and Profile. Fixed MIDs are rejected (the template applies). Depends on SP-6, SP-7 Out of scope Split inquiry API (later, with the Merchant Portal view)."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-7",""],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","1. Request","split-payout/docs/stories.html#request","Field Type M/O/C Rule action String M NEW or UPDATE orderId String M PGW order ID splitAdviceId String C – M for UPDATE The latest advice ID of the order splitPayoutType String C – M for Dynamic AMOUNT / PERCENTAGE splitPayoutTransaction[] Array C – M for Dynamic Same as SP-6: partnerId, value, reference, description splitPayoutProfileId String C – M for Profile A profile of the MID The request always carries the full split, never one leg."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","2. Checks","split-payout/docs/stories.html#checks","What can go wrong: checks 2.1–2.6 Any failure: reject (HTTP 400) with the message. PGW engineering sets the error codes. # Check Message 2.1 Split is on for the MID. Mode is Dynamic or Profile. Split payout is not enabled for this merchant. / Not allowed for Fixed split. 2.2 The order exists, belongs to the calling MID and has a successful Pay. Order not found. / Order is not paid. 2.3 The order has splitPayout = true. Order is not a split order. 2.4 NEW: the order has deferredSplit = true and no advice yet. A split already exists for this order. Use UPDATE. 2.5 UPDATE: splitAdviceId is the latest advice ID of the order. Advice ID is not the latest. 2.6 The split passes the SP-6 checks 3.4 to 3.8 (Partner IDs, legs limit, totals, values, profile). As in SP-6. Why 2.3. An order without the flag was not held by APEX. Its money may already be paid to the merchant. Why 2.5. A late retry of an old request must not overwrite a newer correction."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","3. Processing","split-payout/docs/stories.html#processing","Repeat of the same NEW with the same content: return the first splitAdviceId. Do not create a second advice. Store the split on the order (fields as in SP-6 section 4). For UPDATE, replace the legs. Send to APEX with SP-7 (NEW → A, UPDATE → U). APEX accepts U only while the advice is not yet processed or released. APEX rejects it after that. Return the APEX reason."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","4. Response","split-payout/docs/stories.html#response","Field Value splitAdviceId New advice ID splitAdviceStatus ACCEPTED or REJECTED (from APEX) or PENDING (APEX not reached) reasonCode, reasonMessage When rejected The final payout result reaches the merchant in the APEX split payout report."],["Split Payout","Story map › Requirements","Document","5. Example","split-payout/docs/stories.html#example-2","{ \"action\": \"NEW\", \"orderId\": \"a1b2c3d4-...\", \"splitPayoutType\": \"PERCENTAGE\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\": [ { \"partnerId\": \"P000301\", \"value\": 60.00 }, { \"partnerId\": \"P000302\", \"value\": 30.00 } ] }"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-8 — BE – PGW Split Payout API","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-7","Order created with deferredSplit = true and paid: NEW accepted. Advice ID returned. NEW on an order that already has a split: rejected (2.4). UPDATE with an older advice ID: rejected (2.5). NEW on an order without the split flag: rejected (2.3). Call on a Fixed MID: rejected (2.1). Same NEW sent twice: same advice ID."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","split-payout/docs/stories.html#sp-9-be-day-end-split-advice-file-waiting-on-emcrey-p3","End-to-end view Simulator: day-end file Advice lifecycle What can go wrong: day-end file"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Background","split-payout/docs/stories.html#background-8","APEX uses a day-end file as a backup to the real-time API, the same way as transaction federation today. If an advice is lost on the API, the file carries it. If the file and the API differ, the file wins."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Goal","split-payout/docs/stories.html#goal-8","PGW sends APEX one file each day with all advices of the day."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Story summary","split-payout/docs/stories.html#story-summary-8","Item Value Story ID SP-9 Depends on SP-7, P3 (file format)"],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Requirements","split-payout/docs/stories.html#requirements-8","Send the file after the Ecomm cut-off (midnight, UAE time), for the day that ended. Include every advice created or updated that day, in its latest state (action A or U). Add a trailer with the number of records. On a day with no advices, send an empty file with a record count of 0. File name, format, delivery path: from P3."],["Split Payout","Story map › SP-9 — BE – Day-end split advice file (waiting on Emcrey, P3)","Document","Acceptance criteria","split-payout/docs/stories.html#acceptance-criteria-8","To be completed when P3 is received."],["Split Payout","Story map","Document","Open points","split-payout/docs/stories.html#open-points","What can go wrong: cases not defined yet # Point Story Owner / status 1 Partner ID convention: who issues it (PGW, Operations or APEX) and its format. MA must be able to use the same convention later. SP-3 Rabbani – parked 2 Where isSplitPayoutEnabled and the order field splitPayoutTransaction come from, and what reads them today. SP-2, SP-6 PGW engineering 3 Partner ID search across MIDs: confirm it is possible on product instance data. SP-2 PGW engineering 4 The tab is in Merchant Portal Backoffice (owner: MA team). Confirm the PGW team builds it, as for Pay by Bank settings. SP-1 Rabbani with the MA team 5 Are all three modes in the first build, or Dynamic first? SP-3 to SP-5 Rabbani 6 After a mode change: how an UPDATE is checked for an order created in the old mode. SP-8 Rabbani 7 Pay by Link with split payout. SP-6 Later"],["Split Payout","End-to-end view","Visual page","End-to-end view","split-payout/end-to-end.html","visual · split payout End-to-end view One order from start to payout, across the customer, the partner, PGW, APEX and the vendors. Change the settings below and both flows redraw: the split mode, when the split is sent, who bears the transfer fees, and what goes wrong on the way. Illustrative Reflects product doc v1.6 and PGW stories v0.5 Read the requirement → Stories: SP-6 → SP-8 → Terms: partner = the merchant (MID) with split payout on; vendor = a payee of the split, with an ID from APEX. Field names in the payloads are the stories' proposals (the stories call the vendor ID partnerId ). APEX advice fields are drafts until the Emcrey spec (P3). Order amount AED 1,000 in every example. Split mode Dynamic Fixed Profile Split type Amount Percentage Split sent With the order Later (deferredSplit) Transfer fees borne by Partner Vendors APEX real-time call Reached Not reachable APEX outcome Accepted Rejected in the call, corrected same day Amount check fails Reset to the default"],["Split Payout","End-to-end view","Visual page","A. From Create Session to payout","split-payout/end-to-end.html#a-from-create-session-to-payout","Dynamic MID · amount split The split (P000301 500.00, P000302 300.00) travels with the order. APEX accepts it and pays on the payout date. Action by the customer or partner PGW or APEX processing Held at APEX Money moves Rejected Waiting or retry Released to the partner Order and payment Hold and advice Validation Payout Customer Partner PGW APEX Vendors 01 Create Session AMOUNT legs 02 Check and store the split row 2.3 · checks 3.1–3.9 03 Pays card, wallet 04 Federate the sale splitPayout = Y 05 Hold the transaction until a valid advice 06 Send advice A real time · ACCEPTED 07 Structural checks advice CREATED 08 Day-end file after midnight · backup 09 Amount validation Rule 1, Rule 2: pass 10 Pay out on P vendors, then the residual 11 Vendors receive their payouts leg − commission 12 Partner receives the residual after MDR, all fees Scroll sideways to see the whole flow → 01 Partner Create Session AMOUNT legs 02 PGW Check and store the split row 2.3 · checks 3.1–3.9 03 Customer Pays card, wallet 04 PGW Federate the sale splitPayout = Y 05 APEX Hold the transaction until a valid advice 06 PGW Send advice A real time · ACCEPTED 07 APEX Structural checks advice CREATED 08 PGW Day-end file after midnight · backup 09 APEX Amount validation Rule 1, Rule 2: pass 10 APEX Pay out on P vendors, then the residual 11 Vendors Vendors receive their payouts leg − commission 12 Partner Partner receives the residual after MDR, all fees ← Previous Next step → Step 1 of 12"],["Split Payout","End-to-end view › A. From Create Session to payout","Visual page","1. Create Session","split-payout/end-to-end.html#aDetail","Partner → PGW (HPP, Direct API, token CIT/MIT) The partner sends the split with the order: the split type and one leg per vendor. Try it in the simulator Story SP-6 section 1 Product doc 7.2 POST /payment-intent/api/v2/direct/session { \"amount\" : 1000, \"currency\" : \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\" : \"Pay\", \"merchantReferenceId\" : \"ORD-1001\", \"splitPayoutType\" : \"AMOUNT\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\" : [ { \"partnerId\" : \"P000301\", \"value\" : 500 }, { \"partnerId\" : \"P000302\", \"value\" : 300 } ], ... : ... other Create Session fields }"],["Split Payout","End-to-end view","Visual page","B. Deferred split: from the Payout Advice API to payout","split-payout/end-to-end.html#b-deferred-split-from-the-payout-advice-api-to-payout","Starts with: a paid order created with deferredSplit, held at APEX, no advice yet The partner sends the split after payment. APEX accepts it and pays on the payout date. Scroll sideways to see the whole flow → ← Previous Next step → Shown when Split sent is set to Later (deferredSplit) ."],["Split Payout","Split Payout","Hub","Split Payout","split-payout/index.html","feature Split Payout A partner's ecommerce order is paid out to the partner and its vendors from one transaction."],["Split Payout","Split Payout","Hub","Documents","split-payout/index.html#documents","Product document Vendor Payout Service, MVP v1.6 · 10-Nov-2026 PGW dev stories Vendor Payout Service, PGW stories v0.5"],["Split Payout","Split Payout","Hub","Visual pages","split-payout/index.html#visual-pages","End-to-end view One order from Create Session, or a Payout Advice API call, to the vendor and partner payouts; switch mode, split type, deferred split, fees and failures and the flow redraws open Money flow Who is paid, and from where, for one order; edit the numbers, see fees and APEX amount validation open Onboarding Operational and system steps in one swimlane, from partner request to go-live open Split modes Dynamic, Fixed and Profile explained side by side open Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator One section per PGW work item: configuration, Create Session, APEX federation, Payout Advice API, day-end file open Advice lifecycle Advice statuses at APEX, and day by day: deferred split, update, rejection, release open What can go wrong Every rejection and exception, from configuration to after payout, each with a \"Try it\" in the simulator open"],["Split Payout","Split Payout","Hub","Stories and where to see them","split-payout/index.html#stories","Prerequisites P1, P2 · Operations, Risk and APEX set-up Onboarding SP-1 · Configuration screen Simulator 1 SP-2 · Configuration settings and limits Simulator 1 · Onboarding SP-3 · Enable split, Partner IDs, Dynamic Simulator 1 · Split modes · What can go wrong SP-4 · Fixed mode Simulator 1 · Split modes · What can go wrong SP-5 · Profile mode Simulator 1 · Split modes · What can go wrong SP-6 · Create Session with split End-to-end view · Simulator 2–3 · Split modes · Money flow · What can go wrong SP-7 · Advice to APEX End-to-end view · Simulator 3 · Advice lifecycle · What can go wrong SP-8 · Payout Advice API End-to-end view · Simulator 4 · Advice lifecycle · What can go wrong SP-9 · Day-end advice file End-to-end view · Simulator 5 · Advice lifecycle · What can go wrong"],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","Money flow","split-payout/money-flow.html","visual · split payout Money flow Who is paid, and from where, for one order. Starts on the product doc's worked example; change any number to see the effect. Band widths are to scale. Illustrative Reflects product doc v1.6 · 10-Nov-2026 Read the requirement → Stories: SP-6 check 3.6 →"],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","The numbers","split-payout/money-flow.html#the-numbers","Doc worked example (4.2) MDR : what Geidea deducts from the partner (MID). Commission : what the partner takes from each vendor's leg. Numbers are fictional; what matters is how each component works. Reset to the doc example Order amount (AED) Geidea MDR (%) VAT on MDR (%) Fee per payout (AED) Split type Amount Percentage Vendor Split (AED) Partner commission (%) × × × + Add vendor"],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","One order, end to end","split-payout/money-flow.html#one-order-end-to-end","No split Split · partner bears transfer fees Split · vendors bear transfer fees The partner bears the transfer cost of every payout (each vendor’s and its own). APEX accepts the advice. Rule 1 and Rule 2 pass: vendors are paid and the partner receives the residual (advice PROCESSED). Money flow for one order CUSTOMER PAYS ACQUIRING (GEIDEA / APEX) PAID TO Geidea MDR 10.00 + VAT 0.00 Partner net: AED 990.00 Vendor A: AED 490.00 Vendor B: AED 295.50 Vendor C: AED 100.00 Remittance fees: AED 4.00 Partner residual: AED 100.50 Customer AED 1,000.00 Geidea MDR AED 10.00 (1%) Partner net AED 990.00 · held for split Vendor A AED 490.00 · to vendor IBAN Vendor B AED 295.50 · to vendor IBAN Vendor C AED 100.00 · to vendor IBAN Remittance fees AED 4.00 · 4 × 1.00, from partner Partner residual AED 100.50 · incl. 14.50 partner commission Money paid out Kept by Geidea (MDR, VAT, remittance fees) Held at APEX Bands under 0.5% of the order are drawn at a minimum width so they stay visible."],["Split Payout","Money flow › One order, end to end","Visual page","How each payout is calculated","split-payout/money-flow.html#how-each-payout-is-calculated","Calculated by APEX, not PGW. A percentage split is first converted against the gross order amount. Each amount is rounded to 2 decimals; the partner's residual absorbs the rounding. Vendor A split 500.00 − partner commission 2% 10.00 − remittance fee 0.00 = 490.00 Vendor B split 300.00 − partner commission 1.5% 4.50 − remittance fee 0.00 = 295.50 Vendor C split 100.00 − partner commission none 0.00 − remittance fee 0.00 = 100.00"],["Split Payout","Money flow › One order, end to end","Visual page","What the partner receives","split-payout/money-flow.html#what-the-partner-receives","The residual: everything left of the partner's net after vendor payouts and fees. Transaction amount less Geidea MDR 1,000.00 − 10.00 990.00 Less: net payouts to vendors payouts 1 to 3 −885.50 Less: remittance fees 4 payouts × 1.00, all charged to the partner −4.00 Paid to the partner payout 4: 90.00 unallocated after MDR + 14.50 commission − 4.00 remittance fees 100.50"],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","APEX amount validation","split-payout/money-flow.html#amount-validation","A scheduled APEX process, once pricing is available. Any failure rejects the whole advice with a reason code. \"Split ≤ net\" is not enough: it passes advices that leave the partner negative once fees are taken, and rejects valid ones where commission covers the gap."],["Split Payout","Money flow › APEX amount validation","Visual page","pass Rule 1 – partner residual not negative","split-payout/money-flow.html#rules","net − Σ advised amounts + Σ partner commissions − remittance fees borne by the partner ≥ 0 net (1,000.00 − MDR 10.00 − VAT 0.00) 990.00 − Σ advised amounts −900.00 + Σ partner commissions +14.50 − remittance fees borne by the partner (4 payouts) −4.00 result 100.50"],["Split Payout","Money flow › APEX amount validation","Visual page","pass Rule 2 – every leg above zero","split-payout/money-flow.html#rules","advised amount − commission − remittance fee (only when the vendor bears it) > 0, for every vendor Vendor A: 500.00 − 10.00 490.00 Vendor B: 300.00 − 4.50 295.50 Vendor C: 100.00 − 0.00 100.00"],["Split Payout","Money flow › APEX amount validation","Visual page","rule Single payout","split-payout/money-flow.html#rules","A transaction is never paid out twice. Source: product doc v1.6, 6.5 Amount validation . Source: product doc v1.6, 4.1 How funds move and 4.2 Worked example. The doc example uses MDR 1%, remittance fee AED 1.00 per payout (illustrative), VAT on MDR left out."],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","The sequence in APEX","split-payout/money-flow.html#the-sequence-in-apex","APEX calculates the partner's settlement and deducts Geidea's MDR and VAT on the MDR. The remainder is the partner's net. For a transaction with a valid split advice, APEX calculates each vendor's payout: split amount, minus commission on the vendor definition (if any), minus the remittance fee when the partner MID is set to deduct it from vendors. Rounded to 2 decimals. A remittance fee is charged for every payout: each vendor transfer and the partner's own payout. The fee on the partner's payout always comes from its residual. Commission taken from a vendor leg stays with the partner and reaches it in the residual. APEX transfers each vendor's net payout to its IBAN and settles the residual to the partner. Not yet defined (Finance) Whether vendor payouts go through a separate staging account, or APEX posts them directly from the merchant payout account. Accounting of fund movements, and VAT on vendor commission and remittance fees. Source: product doc v1.6, 4.1 How funds move ."],["Split Payout","Money flow","Visual page","What happens in each situation","split-payout/money-flow.html#outcomes","paid · normal Transaction not flagged for split Settles to the partner through the normal process, after Geidea's MDR. paid · split Flagged, valid advice processed Vendors receive their net payouts; the partner receives the residual. held Flagged, advice rejected Nothing is paid to vendors; the transaction stays held. The rejection and reason show in the split payout report. The partner may send a corrected, complete advice through the Payout Advice API. held Flagged, no advice received The transaction stays held. Example: a deferred split never sent, or an advice lost in transit and not in the day-end file. released Flagged, no valid advice within N days Released to the partner after Geidea's MDR and listed in an exception report for Operations and Finance. N is set per partner MID, can be zero, and counts from the scheduled payout date. parked Advice received before the transaction Parked as PENDING_MATCH and linked when the transaction arrives; rejected with a reason if still unmatched at day end. held Advice in API but missing in the day-end file Marked as mismatched; settlement held until resolved. exception Transfer to a vendor fails Existing exception process: retry up to the configured limit, then an exception record, shown in the split payout report. Geidea contacts the partner only, never the vendor. Source: product doc v1.6, 4.3 Outcomes ."],["Split Payout","Onboarding","Visual page","Onboarding","split-payout/onboarding.html","visual · split payout Onboarding How a partner gets split payout, from request to go-live. Most steps are operational (emails and documents between teams). Two steps change system set-up: APEX creates the vendors, and PGW configures the partner MID. Illustrative Reflects product doc v1.6, sections 5 and 7.1 Read the requirement → Stories: prerequisites P1, P2 → After set-up: End-to-end view → Terms: partner = the Geidea merchant (MID) that asks for split payout; vendor = a payee of the split. APEX gives each vendor a beneficiary ID; PGW uses that ID to check the partner's requests."],["Split Payout","Onboarding","Visual page","Who does what","split-payout/onboarding.html#who-does-what","Operational step (no system build in the MVP) System set-up Side path Timing not set in the doc Request and approval Vendors PGW set-up Live Partner Business Risk Legal Operations APEX team PGW integration 01 · ops Request the service 02 · ops Present to Risk 03 · ops Approve the partner 04 · ops Onboard each vendor 05 · system Create vendors in APEX 06 · system Configure the partner MID in PGW 07 · ops Support the partner’s integration 08 · ops Go live Screening hit → Risk, existing process Business + Legal revisit the partner agreement (doc 5.1) Request and approval 01 · ops Partner Request the service 02 · ops Business Present to Risk 03 · ops Risk Approve the partner Business + Legal revisit the partner agreement (doc 5.1). The doc does not set when. Vendors 04 · ops Operations Onboard each vendor Side path: screening hit → Risk, existing process 05 · system APEX team Create vendors in APEX PGW set-up 06 · system PGW integration Configure the partner MID in PGW 07 · ops PGW integration Support the partner’s integration Live 08 · ops Partner Go live ← Previous Next step → Show all Step 1 of 8"],["Split Payout","Onboarding › Who does what","Visual page","1. Request the serviceOperational","split-payout/onboarding.html#detail","Done by: Partner The partner asks for the service and shares the vendors’ details and documents, the split configuration and any vendor commission. Business registration Relationship or contract with the partner IBAN Source: product doc 5.2 step 1"],["Split Payout","Onboarding › 1. Request the serviceOperational","Visual page","COMES IN","split-payout/onboarding.html#detail","Partner’s own request"],["Split Payout","Onboarding › 1. Request the serviceOperational","Visual page","GOES OUT TO BUSINESS","split-payout/onboarding.html#detail","Vendor details + documents Split configuration Vendor commission"],["Split Payout","Onboarding › 1. Request the serviceOperational","Visual page","RESULT","split-payout/onboarding.html#detail","Request with Business"],["Split Payout","Onboarding","Visual page","Where each set-up item lives","split-payout/onboarding.html#where-each-set-up-item-lives","Item Set by Kept in Used for Vendor documents (business registration, IBAN in the business's name, agreement with the partner) Operations Operations record Support for each payout, e.g. the Central Bank travel rule Vendor definition with IBAN and any commission APEX team APEX, linked to the partner MID Paying the vendor legs Split payout on the partner MID: remittance fee, fee-bearer option, N APEX team APEX Fees and the N-day hold. See Money flow Beneficiary IDs APEX team creates; PGW integration team enters APEX and PGW configuration PGW checks that each leg in a request uses a known ID Split payout enabled, split mode, fixed template or profile catalog PGW integration team PGW configuration (the partner has no access) Building the split for each order. See Split modes and the configuration modal Source: product doc 5.2 , 7.1"],["Split Payout","Onboarding","Visual page","Rules that apply","split-payout/onboarding.html#rules-that-apply","Offered only to select large partners, case by case. Unlicensed aggregators are excluded. Risk approves the partner before any onboarding. The service is never on by default. Business revisits the partner agreement with Legal: dispute and chargeback liability, refunds and chargebacks deducted from the partner, recovery of any shortfall, and domestic fund transfer terms. Due diligence and screening happen once per vendor, when it is onboarded, not on every payout. New vendors, changes to a vendor's details or commission, and deactivation follow the same operational route. Vendors have no portal access. Geidea talks to the partner only. PGW holds no vendor bank details and does not check vendor status. APEX rejects a beneficiary ID that is wrong or no longer active. Source: product doc 5.1 , 5.2 , 7.1"],["Split Payout","Onboarding","Visual page","Still to add","split-payout/onboarding.html#still-to-add","Detail from the Vendor Payout Service Operations SOP v1.0 (03-Nov-2026): the route and form of each handover, checklists, and how the change and deactivation paths run. This page shows only what the product doc states."],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","split-payout/simulator.html","simulator · split payout Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator One section per PGW work item: configure split payout on a MID, create a session, follow the transaction to APEX, send or correct a split with the Payout Advice API, and generate the day-end file. Illustrative Reflects PGW stories v0.5 and product doc v1.6 Read the stories → Read the product doc → Terms follow the PGW stories. Merchant = the MID with split payout on (the \"partner\" in the product doc). Partner = a payee of the split, with a Partner ID from APEX (a \"vendor\" in the product doc). Field names are the stories' proposals. APEX advice fields and the day-end file layout are drafts until the Emcrey spec (P3). Updates reach APEX only in the day-end file, as agreed with APEX on 23-Nov, and are accepted on the transaction date only (rule of 24-Nov). Stories v0.5 still say real time. Nothing here calls a real system. 1"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Split Payout PGW Configuration","split-payout/simulator.html#split-payout-pgw-configuration","PGW configuration · Split Payout tab · SP-1 to SP-5 load example — Split off Dynamic Fixed Profile Open PGW configuration Saved settings · MID 9000123 isSplitPayoutEnabled true splitPayoutMode DYNAMIC maximum legs (SP-2) 10 last saved example loaded splitPayoutPartners P000301 Seller A P000302 Seller B P000303 Delivery Co Source: SP-1 to SP-5 · SP-2 settings An order keeps the split as it was at session creation. Change and save the configuration, then select an earlier order in section 3: it does not change (SP-6 section 4). 2"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Update Create Session API","split-payout/simulator.html#update-create-session-api","Merchant → PGW · POST /payment-intent/api/v2/direct/session · SP-6 Order amount currency AED USD SAR paymentOperation Pay PreAuthorize merchantReferenceId Split Split with the order deferredSplit = true No split (normal payment) AMOUNT PERCENTAGE partnerId value reference × × × + Add leg Any Partner ID can be typed, including one that is not configured, to see the checks. For other combinations (for example a profile ID on a Dynamic MID), use Edit JSON. Request body Edit JSON Back to form { \"amount\" : 1000, \"currency\" : \"AED\", \"merchantReferenceId\" : \"ORD-DEMO-0001\", \"paymentOperation\" : \"Pay\", \"splitPayoutType\" : \"AMOUNT\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\" : [ { \"partnerId\" : \"P000301\", \"value\" : 500, \"reference\" : \"LEG-1\" }, { \"partnerId\" : \"P000302\", \"value\" : 300, \"reference\" : \"LEG-2\" }, { \"partnerId\" : \"P000303\", \"value\" : 100, \"reference\" : \"LEG-3\" } ], \"timestamp\" : ... , \"signature\" : ... , \"callbackUrl\" : ... } Create session 2"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Create Session result: checks and order","split-payout/simulator.html#create-session-result-checks-and-order","PGW · SP-6 sections 1 to 5 order — Send a Create Session to see the checks. 3"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Update APEX Create Transaction Federation","split-payout/simulator.html#update-apex-create-transaction-federation","Customer → PGW → APEX · SP-6 section 6, SP-7 APEX response Accepts (checks pass) Rejects: Partner ID inactive at APEX Not reachable (timeout) Create a session first. 4"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Payout Advice Create/Update API","split-payout/simulator.html#payout-advice-create-update-api","Merchant → PGW → APEX · independent API · SP-8, SP-7 APEX response Accepts (checks pass) Rejects: Partner ID inactive at APEX Not reachable (timeout) Create a session first. 5"],["Split Payout","Split Payout Config & Payment Simulator","Visual page","Day-End Split Advice File Generation","split-payout/simulator.html#day-end-split-advice-file-generation","PGW → APEX · SP-9 · after the Ecomm cut-off (midnight, UAE) Day 1 Run day-end Day 1 so far No orders today yet. The file carries every advice created or updated today, in its latest state (action A or U). A PENDING advice is included: the file is the backup when the real-time call failed. It is also the only route for an UPDATE: the APEX API only creates advices (agreed with APEX on 23-Nov). Orders with no advice are not in the file. Source: SP-9 · Product doc 6.4 Files sent No file sent yet. Run day-end to send the Day 1 file."],["Split Payout","Split modes","Visual page","Split modes","split-payout/split-modes.html","visual · split payout Split modes Each partner MID uses one split mode. The mode decides who defines the split, and when: the partner with each order, or Geidea once in the PGW configuration. Illustrative Reflects product doc v1.6 and PGW stories v0.5 Read the requirement → Terms: partner = the Geidea merchant (MID) with split payout on; vendor = a payee of the split, identified by an ID from APEX (the stories call it a Partner ID). Field names are from the PGW stories and can be renamed by PGW engineering."],["Split Payout","Split modes","Visual page","The three modes side by side","split-payout/split-modes.html#the-three-modes-side-by-side",""],["Split Payout","Split modes › The three modes side by side","Visual page","Dynamic","split-payout/split-modes.html#dynamic","The partner sends the split with each order, or later. Who defines the split Partner per order Set up by Geidea in PGW Vendor IDs only. No template. Sent with the order splitPayoutType + splitPayoutTransaction[] , or deferredSplit = true , or nothing (normal payment) Split after payment Yes: Payout Advice API, NEW or UPDATE with legs Typical use Marketplace: several sellers in one checkout. Delivery platform: restaurant or store and the platform. Try it in the simulator →"],["Split Payout","Split modes › The three modes side by side","Visual page","Fixed","split-payout/split-modes.html#fixed","One template, set by Geidea, applies to every order. Who defines the split Geidea once, for all orders Set up by Geidea in PGW Vendor IDs + one template ( splitPayoutFixedTemplate ) Sent with the order Nothing. Any split field is rejected. Split after payment No. The Payout Advice API rejects a Fixed MID. Typical use Standing revenue share: the same share of every sale goes to a supplier. Try it in the simulator →"],["Split Payout","Split modes › The three modes side by side","Visual page","Profile","split-payout/split-modes.html#profile","Geidea sets a catalog of templates; the partner picks one per order. Who defines the split Geidea defines the catalog, partner picks per order Set up by Geidea in PGW Vendor IDs + profile catalog ( splitPayoutProfiles ), up to 10 profiles Sent with the order splitPayoutProfileId , or deferredSplit = true . Legs are rejected. Split after payment Yes: Payout Advice API, NEW or UPDATE with a profile ID Typical use Aggregator with standard terms: an insurance aggregator with a pre-agreed split per insurer. Try it in the simulator → Source: product doc v1.6, 2 Use cases and 3.2 Split modes ; stories SP-3 , SP-4 , SP-5 , SP-6 section 2 , SP-8 check 2.1 ."],["Split Payout","Split modes","Visual page","One order, three modes","split-payout/split-modes.html#one-order-three-modes","Dynamic Fixed Profile order amount (AED)"],["Split Payout","Split modes › One order, three modes","Visual page","Geidea Set up once in PGW","split-payout/split-modes.html#st1","Vendor IDs only. No split is stored. { \"splitPayoutMode\" : \"DYNAMIC\", \"splitPayoutPartners\" : [ \"P000301\", \"P000302\", \"P000303\" ] }"],["Split Payout","Split modes › One order, three modes","Visual page","Partner Sent with each order","split-payout/split-modes.html#st2","The partner sends the legs it wants for this order. { \"amount\" : 1000, \"currency\" : \"AED\", \"paymentOperation\" : \"Pay\", \"splitPayoutType\" : \"AMOUNT\", \"splitPayoutTransaction\" : [ { \"partnerId\" : \"P000301\", \"value\" : 500 }, { \"partnerId\" : \"P000302\", \"value\" : 300 }, { \"partnerId\" : \"P000303\", \"value\" : 100 } ], \"...\" : ... other Create Session fields }"],["Split Payout","Split modes › One order, three modes","Visual page","Legs on the order, sent to APEX","split-payout/split-modes.html#st3","PGW stores and sends the amounts: Vendor ID Amount P000301 500.00 P000302 300.00 P000303 100.00 Partner keeps the rest 100.00 Before MDR, VAT, partner commission and remittance fees. See Money flow . The split can differ on every order. The partner can also send deferredSplit = true and send the split after payment with the Payout Advice API. Examples: stories SP-4 section 4 (Fixed template) and SP-5 section 4 (profile catalog); Dynamic legs as in the product doc worked example. Illustrative values."],["Split Payout","Split modes","Visual page","Rules for every mode","split-payout/split-modes.html#rules-for-every-mode","A leg names a vendor ID and a value. The value is an amount or a percentage of the gross transaction amount, never both. All legs of one split use the same type: all amounts or all percentages. Percentages are converted to amounts by APEX, not by PGW. Each amount is rounded to 2 decimals; the partner's residual absorbs the rounding difference. Templates and profiles are configured by Geidea only. The partner has no access to split configuration. A split carries vendor IDs and values only. Bank details always come from Geidea's records, never from the partner's request. Maximum 10 legs per split (template, profile, or a split sent with an order or through the API). Configured as a system setting. Amount legs are checked against the order amount at Create Session, not at setup: the order amount is not known when a template or profile is saved. Source: product doc v1.6, 3.2 Rules common to all modes ; stories SP-2 section 2, SP-4 section 2, SP-6 check 3.6."],["Split Payout","Split modes","Visual page","Changing the mode or the set-up","split-payout/split-modes.html#changing-the-mode-or-the-set-up","Change saved in PGW Effect Mode changed Applies to orders created after the save. The old mode's template or profiles stay stored but are not applied. Orders already created keep their split. Template or profile edited Applies to orders created after the save. Orders already created keep the legs they were given. Profile deleted New orders with that profile ID are rejected. Vendor ID deleted New orders and API calls with that ID are rejected. Splits already sent to APEX do not change. A vendor ID used in the template or a profile cannot be deleted. Split turned off New orders with split fields and Payout Advice API calls are rejected. Orders already flagged stay flagged; APEX releases them after N days. Operations also turns split off in APEX. Source: stories SP-3 section 3 , SP-3 section 6 , SP-4 section 3 , SP-5 section 3 , SP-6 section 4 ."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","What can go wrong","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html","visual · split payout What can go wrong Every rejection and exception in a split payout, in the order an order meets them: from the PGW configuration to after the payout. Each case shows the message, what happens to the money and how it is fixed. \"Try it\" opens the simulator in that exact state. Illustrative Reflects PGW stories v0.5 and product doc v1.6 Read the requirement → Stories: SP-6 checks → SP-8 checks → Terms: partner = the merchant (MID) with split payout on; vendor = a payee of the split. Updates reach APEX only in the day-end file, as agreed with APEX on 23-Nov, and are accepted on the transaction date only (rule of 24-Nov). Stories v0.5 and doc v1.6 still describe a real-time update. The PGW stories call these merchant and partner, so the messages quoted from them say \"partner ID\" for a vendor's ID. Messages are verbatim from the stories; PGW engineering sets the error codes. 1 Configuration 5 cases 2 Create Session 17 cases 3 Payout Advice API 8 cases 4 Sending to APEX 1 cases 5 APEX checks 3 cases 6 Amount validation 3 cases 7 Day-end file 4 cases 8 Payout and after 4 cases 45 of 45 cases Rejected Held at APEX Released to the partner Handled, no loss Not defined yet"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","1. Configuration","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-cfg","PGW back office, before any order. Nothing is saved until the checks pass."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 1. Configuration","Visual page","SP-3 4.1–4.4 Partner ID entry is not valid Not saved","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cfg-partner-id","When Adding or editing a Partner ID in the pop-up. Message Use 3–20 letters, digits or hyphens. This Partner ID is already in the list. This Partner ID is configured on another MID (MID nnnnnnnnnnn). A partner belongs to one merchant MID only. Use up to 100 characters. Money None. Nothing is saved. Fix Correct the entry. For 4.3, ask the APEX team which MID the vendor belongs to. Note Why 4.3: APEX links each vendor to one partner MID. A Partner ID on a second MID makes APEX reject every split from that MID after the customer has paid. Open the configuration Story: SP-3 section 4 Product doc 7.1"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 1. Configuration","Visual page","SP-3 4.5 Deleting a Partner ID that is still in use Not deleted","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cfg-delete-used","When The Partner ID is used in the Fixed template or in a profile. Message P000301 is used in Fixed template. Remove it there first. Money None. Fix Remove the leg from the template or profile first. Open a Fixed configuration Story: SP-3 section 4"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 1. Configuration","Visual page","SP-3 5.1–5.2 Split on with no mode or no Partner ID Not saved","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cfg-save","When Save changes with split payout on. Message Select a split mode. Add at least one Partner ID. Money None. Fix Select a mode and add at least one Partner ID. Open with split off Story: SP-3 section 5 Product doc 7.1"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 1. Configuration","Visual page","SP-4 2.1–2.6 Fixed template is not valid Not saved","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cfg-fixed","When Save changes in Fixed mode. Message Add at least one leg. Select a Partner ID. Each partner can appear once. Enter a value above 0, up to 2 decimals. Maximum 10 legs. Percentages cannot add up to more than 100%. Money None. Fix Correct the template. Note An AMOUNT template is not checked against a total at set-up: the order amount is not known yet. Create Session checks it (see 3.6 below). Open a Fixed configuration Story: SP-4 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 1. Configuration","Visual page","SP-5 2.1–2.2 Profile mode with no profile, or too many Not saved","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cfg-profile","When Save changes in Profile mode. Message Add at least one profile. Maximum 10 profiles. Money None. Fix Add a profile, or remove one. Open a Profile configuration Story: SP-5 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","2. Create Session","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-cs","PGW checks the split before payment (SP-6). A failure rejects the session (HTTP 400): no payment is taken."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 2.2 · 3.1 Split fields sent to a MID with split payout off Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-off","When Any split field or deferredSplit on a MID where split payout is off. Message Split payout is not enabled for this merchant. Money No payment is taken. Fix Remove the split fields, or ask Geidea to enable split payout (see Onboarding). Try it Story: SP-6 section 3 Product doc 7.6"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 2.7 · 3.1 Split fields sent to a Fixed MID Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-fixed-fields","When A Fixed MID sends any split field or deferredSplit. PGW applies the template itself. Message Split fields do not match the merchant's split mode. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send no split fields on a Fixed MID. Try it Story: SP-6 section 2 Product doc 7.6"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 2.10 · 3.1 Legs sent to a Profile MID Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-profile-legs","When A Profile MID sends splitPayoutTransaction instead of a profile ID. Message Split fields do not match the merchant's split mode. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send splitPayoutProfileId. Try it Story: SP-6 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.1 Profile ID sent to a Dynamic MID Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-profile-on-dynamic","When A Dynamic MID sends splitPayoutProfileId. Message Split fields do not match the merchant's split mode. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send the legs in splitPayoutTransaction. Note SP-6 section 2 has no row for this combination; check 3.1 covers it. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 2.11 · 3.9 Split detail and deferredSplit together Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-both","When Legs or a profile ID, and deferredSplit = true, in one request. Message Send split detail or deferredSplit, not both. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send one or the other. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3 Product doc 7.6"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 1 Legs without splitPayoutType Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-no-type","When splitPayoutTransaction is sent with no splitPayoutType, or a leg has no partnerId or value. Message Field rule: splitPayoutType is mandatory when splitPayoutTransaction is sent (AMOUNT or PERCENTAGE). Money No payment is taken. Fix Send splitPayoutType with the legs. Try it Story: SP-6 section 1"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.2 Split on an operation other than Pay Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-not-pay","When paymentOperation is not Pay. Message Split payout is supported for Pay only. Money No payment is taken. Fix Use Pay. Note Why: in this release APEX handles split only on a sale. Authorize and capture are not included. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.3 Split on a non-AED order Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-not-aed","When Order currency is not AED. Message Split payout is supported in AED only. Money No payment is taken. Fix Use AED. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.4 Vendor ID not configured on the MID Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-unknown-id","When A partnerId is not one of the MID’s configured IDs. Message Unknown partner ID: {id}. Money No payment is taken. Fix Use a configured ID, or ask Geidea to add the vendor (see Onboarding). Try it Story: SP-6 section 3 Product doc 7.6"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.4 Same vendor ID twice Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-duplicate","When A partnerId occurs more than once. Message Duplicate partner ID: {id}. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send one leg per vendor. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.5 More legs than the maximum Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-too-many","When More legs than the system maximum (default 10, SP-2). Message Maximum {n} legs. Money No payment is taken. Fix Send 10 legs or fewer. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.6 Amount legs above the order amount Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-over-total","When AMOUNT: the legs add up to more than the order amount. Message Split total is more than the order amount. Money No payment is taken. Fix Reduce the legs. Note Passing 3.6 does not guarantee APEX accepts the amounts: APEX Rule 1 also takes MDR, VAT, commission and fees into account (see Amount validation). Try it Story: SP-6 section 3 Product doc 7.6 Money flow"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.6 Percentage legs above 100% Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-pct-over","When PERCENTAGE: the legs add up to more than 100. Message Split total is more than 100%. Money No payment is taken. Fix Reduce the percentages. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 2.6 · 3.6 Fixed AMOUNT template above the order amount Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-fixed-over","When A Fixed MID with an AMOUNT template larger than this order. Message Split total is more than the order amount. Money No payment is taken. The partner cannot fix this per order. Fix Geidea changes the template, or the partner sends larger orders only. Try it Story: SP-4 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.7 Leg value of 0, negative or more than 2 decimals Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-bad-value","When A value is not above 0 with up to 2 decimals. Message Invalid split value. Money No payment is taken. Fix Correct the value. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 3.8 Profile ID not configured Session rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-unknown-profile","When splitPayoutProfileId is not a profile of the MID. Message Unknown split profile: {id}. Money No payment is taken. Fix Use a configured profile ID. Try it Story: SP-6 section 3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 2. Create Session","Visual page","SP-6 section 2 Profile MID sends no profile ID and no deferredSplit Not defined","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#cs-profile-none","When A Profile MID sends a plain session with no split fields. Money Not defined. The simulator treats it as a normal session (no split, paid to the partner as today). Fix — Open point: SP-6 section 2 has no row for this case. Story: SP-6 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","3. Payout Advice API","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-api","The partner sends or corrects a split after payment (SP-8). A failure rejects the call (HTTP 400). The transaction stays held."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.1 Called for a Fixed MID, or with split off Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-fixed","When The MID has split off, or is in Fixed mode. Message Split payout is not enabled for this merchant. Not allowed for Fixed split. Money Nothing changes on the order. Fix A Fixed split comes from the template; ask Geidea to change it. Try it Story: SP-8 section 2 Product doc 7.3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.2 Order not found, not this MID’s, or not paid Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-not-paid","When The order does not exist, belongs to another MID, or has no successful Pay. Message Order not found. Order is not paid. Money Nothing changes. Fix Send the split after the payment succeeds. Try it Story: SP-8 section 2 Product doc 7.3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.3 Order was created without split Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-not-split","When The order has splitPayout = false. Message Order is not a split order. Money The transaction was not held. It settles to the partner as normal. Fix None for this order. Create future orders with a split or deferredSplit. Note Why: an order without the flag was not held by APEX. Its money may already be paid to the partner. Try it Story: SP-8 section 2 Product doc 7.3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.4 NEW for an order that already has a split Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-new-exists","When NEW on an order not created with deferredSplit, or that already has an advice. Message A split already exists for this order. Use UPDATE. Money Nothing changes. The existing advice stands. Fix Use UPDATE with the latest advice ID. Note Repeating a NEW with the same content returns the first advice ID, so a retry after a timeout is safe (product doc 7.3). Try it Story: SP-8 section 2 Product doc 7.3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.5 UPDATE with an older advice ID Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-stale-id","When splitAdviceId is not the latest advice ID of the order. Message Advice ID is not the latest. Money Nothing changes. The newer correction stands. Fix Use the advice ID from the latest response. Note Why: a late retry of an old request must not overwrite a newer correction. Try it Story: SP-8 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","SP-8 2.6 The split fails the Create Session checks Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-over-total","When Unknown or duplicate vendor ID, too many legs, total too high, bad value or unknown profile (SP-6 3.4 to 3.8). Message As in SP-6, for example: Split total is more than the order amount. Money Nothing changes. The transaction stays held. Fix Correct the split and send again. Try it Story: SP-8 section 2"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","Rule 24-Nov UPDATE after the transaction date Call rejected","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-late-update","When An UPDATE sent after the transaction date, once PGW has generated that day’s day-end file. Message Message to be set in stories v0.6. Money Nothing changes. The advice keeps its last status; a held transaction stays held until a valid advice or the N-day release. Fix Send updates on the transaction date, before midnight (UAE time). Note Rule set by Rabbani on 24-Nov: updates are accepted on the transaction date only. Updates reach APEX only in that day’s day-end file (agreed with APEX on 23-Nov). Try it Story: SP-8 section 2 Product doc 7.3"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 3. Payout Advice API","Visual page","Open point 6 UPDATE after the MID’s mode was changed Not defined","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#api-after-change","When An order created in the old mode is updated after Geidea changed the mode. Money Not defined. Fix — Open point 6 in the stories: how an UPDATE is checked for an order created in the old mode. Story: Open points"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","4. Sending to APEX","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-send","PGW forwards the advice in real time (SP-7). A failure here never changes the payment result."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 4. Sending to APEX","Visual page","SP-7 4 APEX not reachable or times out Advice PENDING, retried","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#apex-down","When The real-time Split Advice API call fails. Money The transaction stays held (it is flagged). The payment result does not change. Fix None by the partner. PGW retries (count and interval: PGW engineering). The day-end file carries the advice in any case. Try it Story: SP-7 section 4 Product doc 7.5 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","5. APEX checks","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-apex","APEX structural checks, in the call (product doc 6.4)."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 5. APEX checks","Visual page","APEX 6.4 Vendor not found, inactive or not linked to the MID Advice REJECTED · held","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#apex-reject","When APEX does not find a beneficiary, it is deactivated, or it is linked to another MID. Message Reason code from APEX (APEX to define). Money Nothing is paid to vendors. The transaction stays held. Fix The partner sends a corrected, complete split with UPDATE on the same day (the transaction date). PGW stores it and the day-end file carries it to APEX. If the vendor was deactivated, contact Geidea. Note PGW holds no vendor bank details and does not check vendor status: only APEX catches an inactive vendor. Try it Story: SP-7 section 4 Product doc 6.4 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 5. APEX checks","Visual page","APEX 6.4 Other structural checks fail Advice REJECTED · held","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#apex-other","When MID does not match the transaction; transaction not flagged; both percentage and amount in a rule; A when an advice already exists; an update (in the day-end file) for an advice already PROCESSED or RELEASED. Message Reason code from APEX. Money The transaction stays held. Fix Mostly set-up or sequence errors: Geidea investigates. After PROCESSED or RELEASED the advice is final: no further updates. Note APEX no longer checks that split payout is enabled on the MID: PGW checks it, as it holds the split set-up (agreed with APEX on 23-Nov). Product doc 6.4 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 5. APEX checks","Visual page","APEX 6.4 Advice arrives before its transaction, never matched PENDING_MATCH → REJECTED","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#apex-unmatched","When The advice reaches APEX before the transaction. APEX parks it as PENDING_MATCH. If still unmatched at day end, APEX rejects it with a reason code. Message Reason code from APEX. Money Held until a valid advice is processed, or released after N days. Fix Usually none: the transaction arrives and APEX links the advice. If rejected, the partner sends an UPDATE. Product doc 6.4 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","6. Amount validation","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-amt","APEX checks the amounts once pricing is known (product doc 6.5). Any failure rejects the whole advice."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 6. Amount validation","Visual page","APEX Rule 1 Partner residual would be negative Advice REJECTED · held","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#amt-rule1","When net − Σ advised amounts + Σ vendor commissions − transfer fees borne by the partner < 0 (net = amount − MDR − VAT on MDR). Message Reason code from APEX, shown in the split payout report. Money Nothing is paid to vendors. The transaction stays held. Fix An UPDATE is accepted on the transaction date only. If this rejection comes after that date, it cannot be corrected and the transaction is released to the partner after N days. Note A split that passes PGW check 3.6 (total ≤ order amount) can still fail here, because MDR, VAT and fees come off first. Open points: whether PGW learns of this rejection (the real-time call already returned ACCEPTED); and when APEX runs amount validation, same day or later. If later, the rejection cannot be corrected. Product doc 6.5 Try it in Money flow"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 6. Amount validation","Visual page","APEX Rule 2 A vendor leg would be zero or negative Advice REJECTED · held","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#amt-rule2","When For any vendor: advised amount − commission − transfer fee (if the vendor bears it) ≤ 0. Example: a leg of 0.80, commission 0.02, fee 1.00 gives −0.22. Message Reason code from APEX. Money The whole advice is rejected, not only that leg. Fix Correctable only with an UPDATE on the transaction date; otherwise the transaction is released after N days. Product doc 6.5 Try it in Money flow"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 6. Amount validation","Visual page","APEX single payout A transaction would be paid out twice Blocked by APEX","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#amt-twice","When Any path that would pay the same transaction again. Money Blocked: a transaction is never paid out twice. Fix — Product doc 6.5"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","7. Day-end file","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-file","APEX reconciles the day-end file against the real-time advices (product doc 6.4)."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 7. Day-end file","Visual page","APEX 6.4 File split differs from the real-time advice File wins","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#file-diff","When The same advice is in the API and the file, with a different split. Money APEX overwrites with the file’s split and processes it. Fix None. This is also how every UPDATE reaches APEX: the APEX API only creates advices (agreed with APEX on 23-Nov). Story: SP-9 Product doc 6.4"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 7. Day-end file","Visual page","APEX 6.4 Advice only in the file Processed as new","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#file-only","When The real-time call never reached APEX. Money APEX processes it as new. This is how an API failure is covered. Fix None. Try it Story: SP-9 Product doc 6.4"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 7. Day-end file","Visual page","APEX 6.4 Advice received over the API, missing in the file Mismatched · held","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#file-missing","When APEX has the advice from the real-time call, but the day-end file does not carry it. Money APEX marks it mismatched and holds settlement until resolved. Fix Geidea investigates (PGW and APEX). Story: SP-9 Product doc 6.4"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 7. Day-end file","Visual page","APEX 6.4 No day-end file received API advices used","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#file-none","When The file does not arrive. Money APEX processes what it received over the API. Fix Geidea investigates the file delivery. Note PGW sends an empty file with a zero record count on days with no advices, so APEX can tell \"no advices today\" from \"file not received\". Story: SP-9 Product doc 6.4"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong","Visual page","8. Payout and after","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#stage-after","Hold timer, transfers, refunds and chargebacks (product doc 4.3, 6.3, 8)."],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 8. Payout and after","Visual page","APEX 6.3 No valid advice within N days RELEASED","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#after-released","When N days after the scheduled payout date, the transaction still has no PROCESSED advice: never sent, or rejected and not corrected. Money Released to the partner after Geidea’s MDR. Vendors are not paid through Geidea. Listed in the exception report for Operations and Finance. Fix Final. No further updates to the advice. Note N is set per partner MID and can be zero. The timer runs on the transaction, not on an advice. Product doc 6.3 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 8. Payout and after","Visual page","Doc 4.3 Deferred split never sent Held, then released","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#after-never","When The order was created with deferredSplit = true and the partner never calls the Payout Advice API. Money Held; released to the partner after N days as above. Fix The partner sends NEW before N days pass. Product doc 4.3 Advice lifecycle"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 8. Payout and after","Visual page","Doc 4.3 · 6.6 Transfer to a vendor fails Exception process","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#after-transfer","When The domestic transfer to the vendor’s IBAN fails. Money Existing exception process: retry up to the configured limit, then an exception record. The case shows in the split payout report. Fix Geidea contacts the partner only, never the vendor. Product doc 6.6"],["Split Payout","What can go wrong › 8. Payout and after","Visual page","Doc 8 Refund or chargeback after the payout Debited from the partner","split-payout/what-can-go-wrong.html#after-refund","When A refund or chargeback on a split transaction. Money Debited from the partner’s MID as normal. Vendors and their payouts are not involved; Geidea does not recover from vendors. A small residual can leave the partner short on the day. Fix Shortfall recovery is set in the partner agreement and confirmed by Finance. New splits are not held back to recover it. Product doc 8"]]};
